69c456fb65990d0119bd25768d32f10dca"}],"sha":"38931aa7162542d285671a2ed915f21497f1f1cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/marketplace-ui/commits/38931aa7162542d285671a2ed915f21497f1f1cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7794387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/marketplace-ui/commits/21f0d369c456fb65990d0119bd25768d32f10dca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:56:11Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:56:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: consume full provider card data and derive provider filter (#199)\n\n* feat: add provider verification badge\n\nShow a verification badge on marketplace provider cards and the provider\ndetail dialog, driven by the optional `verification` metadata on a\nprovider (`{ label, status, icon?, hint? }`).\n\nThe badge is rendered with a single Fundamental `fd-object-status`, which\ncarries the label, the status color, and an SAP-icons glyph together. The\nglyph comes from `verification.icon` and falls back to `verified` when the\ndata omits it; the optional `hint` is surfaced via inline help. Providers\nwithout `verification` metadata render no badge.\n\nAlso adds a sample marketplace response\n(`verification-info.mock.json`) next to the component covering the\nvariants: certified (explicit icon), verified (default icon), partner\n(critical status), community (neutral), and an unverified provider with no\nbadge.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* fix tests\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* fix tests\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* fix tests\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* Set the default style for the verification info as `informative`\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: consume full provider card data and derive provider filter\n\n## What changed\nSelect the full provider card-data fields from the marketplace query\n(category, type, mainLink, labels, serviceLevel) and build the Provider\nfilter dropdown from the actual data instead of a hardcoded list.\n\n## Why\nThe backend now exposes these fields (platform-mesh#352), and the UI models\nand templates already expect them, but the GraphQL query never selected\nthem. The Provider filter was also hardcoded to a single ''Community'' entry,\nso it never reflected the real providers.\n\n## Details\n- Query + local schema: add category, type, mainLink, labels, serviceLevel\n  to the marketplace entries selection.\n- ProvidersUtils.getProviders(data): derive unique, sorted, capitalized\n  options from provider ''type'' values; drop the hardcoded ''Community''\n  fallback and the community special-case in filterByProviders.\n- Catalog passes the loaded data into getProviders.\n- Add verification-info.mock.json with 5 providers covering all card fields\n  and 3 distinct types (composition, integration, managed) for local UI\n  verification.\n\n## Tests\nRewrote providers.utils.spec.ts for the data-driven, capitalized behavior;\nfull suite passes (210 tests).\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix card item badge color\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix the layout of the catalog controls\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: add provider verification badge\n\nShow a verification badge on marketplace provider cards and the provider\ndetail dialog, driven by the optional `verification` metadata on a\nprovider (`{ label, status, icon?, hint? }`).\n\nThe badge is rendered with a single Fundamental `fd-object-status`, which\ncarries the label, the status color, and an SAP-icons glyph together. The\nglyph comes from `verification.icon` and falls back to `verified` when the\ndata omits it; the optional `hint` is surfaced via inline help. Providers\nwithout `verification` metadata render no badge.\n\nAlso adds a sample marketplace response\n(`verification-info.mock.json`) next to the component covering the\nvariants: certified (explicit icon), verified (default icon), partner\n(critical status), community (neutral), and an unverified provider with no\nbadge.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* fix tests\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: consume full provider card data and derive provider filter\n\n## What changed\nSelect the full provider card-data fields from the marketplace query\n(category, type, mainLink, labels, serviceLevel) and build the Provider\nfilter dropdown from the actual data instead of a hardcoded list.\n\n## Why\nThe backend now exposes these fields (platform-mesh#352), and the UI models\nand templates already expect them, but the GraphQL query never selected\nthem. The Provider filter was also hardcoded to a single ''Community'' entry,\nso it never reflected the real providers.\n\n## Details\n- Query + local schema: add category, type, mainLink, labels, serviceLevel\n  to the marketplace entries selection.\n- ProvidersUtils.getProviders(data): derive unique, sorted, capitalized\n  options from provider ''type'' values; drop the hardcoded ''Community''\n  fallback and the community special-case in filterByProviders.\n- Catalog passes the loaded data into getProviders.\n- Add verification-info.mock.json with 5 providers covering all card fields\n  and 3 distinct types (composition, integration, managed) for local UI\n  verification.\n\n## Tests\nRewrote providers.utils.spec.ts for the data-driven, capitalized behavior;\nfull suite passes (210 tests).\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix card item badge color\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix the layout of the catalog controls\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix the default verification info color\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"8719a8b1629cb1c50255161b39db4cf4df151228","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/marketplace-ui/git/trees/8719a8b1629cb1c50255161b39db4cf4df151228"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/marketplace-ui/git/commits/21f0d369c456fb65990d0119bd25768d32f10dca","verification":{"payload":"tree 8719a8b1629cb1c50255161b39db4cf4df151228\nparent cfad74df812db41048498603d427de7b237035ec\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1789124171 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789124171 +0200\n\nfeat: consume full provider card data and derive provider filter (#199)\n\n* feat: add provider verification badge\n\nShow a verification badge on marketplace provider cards and the provider\ndetail dialog, driven by the optional `verification` metadata on a\nprovider (`{ label, status, icon?, hint? }`).\n\nThe badge is rendered with a single Fundamental `fd-object-status`, which\ncarries the label, the status color, and an SAP-icons glyph together. The\nglyph comes from `verification.icon` and falls back to `verified` when the\ndata omits i