"id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8773d73cd061fc5fd8d9e136b7fbe8ffc642448b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:26:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:26:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(gitignore): ignore Archify visual-check rasters, keep the receipts\n\nEvery diagram edit reruns visual-check, which writes four screenshots and a\ncontact sheet — about 2MB a pass, all of it regenerable from the delivered HTML.\nThe .visual-check.json receipt is small and is the actual evidence record, so it\nstays tracked. Matches how the graphify output is already handled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2404d26f43132f615cdc15549607e976710865e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/b2404d26f43132f615cdc15549607e976710865e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8773d73cd061fc5fd8d9e136b7fbe8ffc642448b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8773d73cd061fc5fd8d9e136b7fbe8ffc642448b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDg3NzNkNzNjZDA2MWZjNWZkOGQ5ZTEzNmI3ZmJlOGZmYzY0MjQ0OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554","sha":"14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554"}],"sha":"8773d73cd061fc5fd8d9e136b7fbe8ffc642448b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8773d73cd061fc5fd8d9e136b7fbe8ffc642448b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:14:19Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:14:19Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"diagram(sovereign-tier): resolvers reach the actions box, and the flow selector wraps the four\n\nTwo operator changes. The resolvers now also flow into Workspace Window Actions\n— \"act on it now\" — so a resolved entity can be acted on without going through\nprompt firing first. And a second boundary nests inside Sovereign Shell around\nall four families: Flow Selector + Window Loader, because selecting a flow is\nwhat decides which windows load and in what order.\n\nNested boundaries work through `pad`: both wrap the same four components, the\nouter at 44 and the inner at 18, which gives each its own title rail. The row\nmoved down and inward to make room — two rails need vertical space above the\nnodes, and the outer pad pushed the boundary past the viewBox until the members\nwere inset from the canvas edge.\n\nThe routing took four rounds, and the thing that made it hard is worth writing\ndown: ports sit at the centre of a node''s side and `via` cannot move them, so\ntwo edges leaving the same side can only be separated by Archify''s Automatic\nPort Spread — which is disabled on any edge carrying `via`, `channelX`,\n`channelY` or `labelAt`. Authoring a route to fix one edge therefore un-fixes\nits neighbour. Resolvers now has three outbound edges and this bit twice.\n\nIt came apart once I stopped guessing at geometry and rendered a probe copy to\nread the actual path data. Both DB edges turned out to descend 45px apart and\nland on the same right-hand face — which is why every label placement kept\nfailing the clearance check. Multi-Modal DB moved right, clear of Intake''s right\nedge, so the resolvers'' edge can run straight across and enter over the top\nwhile the actions edge keeps the right face. Two bends, no crossings.\n\nReview and promote is no longer the only way into the actions box, which is the\npoint of the change: the shell can load a flow that skips prompt firing\nentirely.\n\nReceipts: validate showcase 9/9, composition pass, 0 errors, 0 warnings,\nmaxBends 2, crossings 0. deliver ok, sha fd970ca2. Fullscreen patch reapplied.\nvisual-check pass on four viewports in both themes; node text still 6.0px\nagainst the 6px floor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51ada15ecd767da61339b0e611c28683fc3e86b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/51ada15ecd767da61339b0e611c28683fc3e86b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDE0NjA2ZjMyZGM1NGE4ZTVjYWEzMDk1NmM2N2JmNTE4ZWM2NTA1NTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297","sha":"8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297"}],"sha":"14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/14606f32dc54a8e5caa30956c67bf518ec650554"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:56:47Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:56:47Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"diagram(sovereign-tier): the operator commits, the pipeline does not\n\nFlow corrected on the operator''s description. Review and promote hands off to\nWorkspace Window Actions — renamed from Workspace Windows, because the box is\nabout what gets done, not the surface it gets done on — and from there three\narrows fan into the three stores: write the entity, re-target the set, write a\ncorpus file. One action can land in more than one.\n\nThat reverses what the previous version implied. It had each family writing to\nits own store directly, which drew the pipeline as if it committed its own\nresults. It does not. A person reviews the response and decides where it goes,\nand the three arrows leaving one box is the whole point — it is the only place\nin the diagram where one thing becomes three.\n\nThe resolvers also reach the canonical layer directly, added on the operator''s\nfollow-up, so Multi-Modal DB now has two inbound edges.\n\nGeometry. Multi-Modal DB moved off centre because the resolvers'' path to it ran\nstraight through the actions box, which the validator caught as edge-through-node.\nWith it left-of-centre both edges reach it, but automatic routing then sent them\ndown side by side and landed both arrowheads on the same right edge — legal, and\nmuddled to look at. The resolvers'' edge now comes in over the top on an authored\nvia; the actions edge keeps its right-side entry. That is a perceptual repair,\nnot a diagnosed one: composition passed either way, and machine checks cannot\nsee two parallel lines converging on one face.\n\nDropped: the DB-mirrors-to-disk edge. It needs Multi-Modal DB and Local Corpora\nadjacent, and moving the DB left put the whole bottom row between them. The fact\nsurvives in the third card.\n\nAlso trimmed card copy again — the longer card title overflowed 1440x900 by\nexactly 5px, the same failure and the same fix as two commits ago. Worth noting\nthe pattern: this composition sits close enough to the 900px height that any\ncard title long enough to wrap costs a viewport.\n\nReceipts: validate showcase 9/9, composition pass, 0 errors, 0 warnings.\ndeliver ok, sha cc16daaa. Fullscreen patch reapplied. visual-check pass on all\nfour viewports in both themes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"659482c95ea9aee6747214b1a40006d5c9038dc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/659482c95ea9aee6747214b1a40006d5c9038dc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhiNjYxMWIyODgyNDI2ZDFhMDI2YjkyMWI2NTAxMjc0Mjg5MjMyOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9","sha":"f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9"}],"sha":"8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8b6611b2882426d1a026b921b650127428923297"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:47:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:47:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"diagram(sovereign-tier): the shell is the boundary, and the stores are drawn\n\nOperator-directed restructure. The yellow dashed region was always the shell —\nREADME calls shell \"Window manager, peek-deck rotation, pair-mode, Flows\nregistry\" — so it is now named Sovereign Shell and the separate shell node is\ngone. The shell hosts the modules; it is the container, not a peer.\n\n\"window events\" is replaced by Workspace Windows: feature- and flow-driven UIs\nover response data. The old node named a mechanism nobody outside the codebase\nwould recognise; this one names the thing an operator actually uses.\n\nTwo stores join active-record-set along the bottom, both verified before being\ndrawn rather than taken on trust:\n\nMulti-Modal DB — SurrealDB Cloud, the canonical entity layer. Persons,\norganizations, domains/sources and affiliations, shared across every client\nworkspace and resolved via record-surrealdb-resolver (README Core concepts).\n\nLocal Corpora — the per-tenant corpus trees under clients/, markdown and yaml\nand json on disk. The edge between the two is real and was the find of this\npass: content-ingest mirrors every canonical write to an on-disk corpus file,\nso the DB is not the only copy.\n\nLayout notes. Each store now sits directly under the family that touches it, so\nall three cross-row edges are unambiguous verticals; the previous attempt put\ntwo competing edges on one port at the resolvers and the router could not place\ntheir labels. The \"five modules read it\" fan-out became node copy instead of a\nsecond edge into the same port.\n\nOne thing worth recording: moving that fact to a `tag` made it vanish. Archify\nemits tag as data-node-tag for search and the accessibility label, and never\npaints it — the node looked finished while the fact was gone. It is back in the\nsublabel, visible. Same trap as the visually-hidden new-tab notice in\nExternalLink, from the other direction.\n\nNot drawn any more: the navigate asymmetry that was the old diagram''s sharpest\npoint. Five modules dispatch augment-it:navigate and only the shell listens.\nWith the shell as a boundary it has no node to terminate on, so it now lives in\nthe third card and in guided view 04. Flagging it because it is a real loss of\nprominence, not an oversight.\n\nReceipts: validate showcase 9/9, composition pass, 0 errors, 0 warnings.\ndeliver ok, sha 10530ec4. Fullscreen patch reapplied. visual-check pass across\nfour viewports in both themes; smallest projected node text 6.0px against the\n6px floor, which is the binding constraint on any further copy growth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4e9565929c31af2a71d33e7a3679368b30184cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/f4e9565929c31af2a71d33e7a3679368b30184cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGY3NTFhYzExZDViMDE0ZmI1OTdiNmU5OTllZmU2YjAzMzc5NjcyYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8","sha":"4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8"}],"sha":"f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/f751ac11d5b014fb597b6e999efe6b03379672c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:33:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:33:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(diagrams): full screen showed the page bleeding through the diagram\n\nEntering full screen left the header, the guided-view rail and the card rail\nvisible underneath the diagram, both drawn at once. Reported by the operator;\nconfirmed by driving Chrome over CDP and looking at the capture.\n\nThe cause was mine. --panel is rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5) — half transparent — and\nthe previous commit painted both the fullscreen element and its ::backdrop with\nit. A fullscreen element does occupy the top layer, but a translucent one simply\nlets the document behind it paint through. Fixed by layering the panel tint over\nthe opaque page ground, linear-gradient(var(--panel), var(--panel)) over\nvar(--bg), so it keeps its usual look and actually occludes.\n\nThe operator also asked for the page chrome to drop to near zero opacity in full\nscreen and return to default on collapse. That is now a second line of defence\nrather than the fix: sync() sets data-archify-fullscreen on <html>, and the\nstylesheet takes body > .toolbar and .container''s non-panel children to opacity\n0 with pointer-events none. The selector deliberately never touches an ancestor\nof the panel — ancestor opacity has historically leaked onto top-layer elements,\nand fading .container would have faded the diagram itself.\n\nVerified by driving real Chrome, not by reading the markup. In full screen:\npanel background rgb(2, 6, 23) with the tint layered above it, html attribute\nset, and toolbar/header/guided-views/cards all at opacity 0. After exit: every\none back at 1, attribute removed, background back to the translucent panel.\nSame result on both diagrams. visual-check still passes on both across four\nviewports in both themes.\n\nTwo rounds of this debugging reached the wrong conclusion first. A Chrome from\nan earlier run was still holding the debug port, so each new launch attached to\nit and served a page built before the fix — the CSS looked inert while the file\non disk was correct. The driver now asserts the loaded build contains the\ncurrent patch before it measures anything, and exits 2 if not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"400524ff596ca354a811bba8181d1980b0730080","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/400524ff596ca354a811bba8181d1980b0730080"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDRkNzQ0ZmQ3OTU2ZGZjOWFiZWE4NzhjNzM2ZTc0NjM5MmEzOWE3Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b","sha":"ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b"}],"sha":"4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4d744fd7956dfc9abea878c736e746392a39a7b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:21:16Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:21:16Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(diagrams): expand-to-full-screen on both Archify panels\n\nThe diagrams read small on a laptop: page header, card rail and the reader''s\nleft/right margins leave the panel roughly 930px wide inside a 1440px viewport.\nPresent mode drops the chrome but stays inside the browser window. This adds a\nreal Fullscreen API control at the panel''s top right, and Escape or a second\nclick collapses back.\n\nIt is a patch script, not a hand edit. `deliver` regenerates the HTML from the\nspec, so an edit made in the file is lost the next time either diagram changes.\napply-fullscreen.mjs is idempotent and re-runnable, and belongs in the loop:\n\n    node bin/archify.mjs deliver ... && node apply-fullscreen.mjs <file>.html\n\nIt fullscreens .diagram-container rather than the document, because the guide\ndialog, PATH/MAP/LENS, the zoom rail and the live-region status nodes are all\nalready children of that element, so every control comes along. The :fullscreen\nsizing mirrors the rules Archify already ships for html[data-present=\"true\"]\ninstead of inventing new ones.\n\nTwo failures found by measuring rather than by assuming, both of which looked\nfine in the markup:\n\nThe button was first inserted as the container''s first child, and Archify''s nav\ndock immediately overlapped the protected SVG stage by 41px — the viewer measures\nits stage from the container''s first element. Bisecting style-only against\nbutton-only isolated it. The button now goes in after the </svg>, so the SVG\nstays the first child; it is absolutely positioned, so DOM order costs nothing.\n\nThen the icons rendered 98px wide instead of 13px. The viewer ships a global\n`svg { width: 100%; min-width: min(900px, 100%) }` for the diagram itself, and\nmin-width is not overridden by setting width — so the icons inflated to the\nbutton''s full content box and the label spilled out past its own border. Fixed\nwith an explicit min-width/max-width reset on the button''s icons.\n\nVerified in headless Chrome against the patched files, not the source: the init\nscript runs (data-fullscreen-ready on the panel), the container''s first child is\nstill the svg, all five :fullscreen rules survive parsing including the prefixed\nSafari pair, the icon measures 13x13 with the label inside the button, the button\nsits 11px inside the panel at both 1440 and 1920, and clicking throws nothing.\nvisual-check passes on both files across four viewports in both themes —\ncontainment, readability, viewer chrome and captures all green.\n\nNot machine-verified: the fullscreen transition itself. Headless Chrome refuses\nrequestFullscreen without a user gesture, and the code swallows that rejection\nrather than leaving a half-toggled state, so the rendered result of entering\nfull screen still needs a human click.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac74caa6d6ff9d1c7e6d5bc53d7d8d3f941f1ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/ac74caa6d6ff9d1c7e6d5bc53d7d8d3f941f1ef9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGVkOTJkY2YwZjA5OWYyZTc3MTE1NTBmMGM5OWI1NjM1MGZhNGJkNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207","sha":"8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207"}],"sha":"ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ed92dcf0f099f2e7711550f0c99b56350fa4bd6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:52:52Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:52:52Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"diagram(context-v): inside the sovereign tier — nineteen modules, no imports\n\nOpens up the \"19 micro-frontends\" box from federal-design-system. That companion\nshows what the members consume; this one shows what they are and how they reach\neach other.\n\nThe relationships are measured, not recalled. A grep for cross-member imports\nacross every app returns exactly three names, and all three are federal packages\n— @augment-it/federation, /gallery, /workspace. No module imports a sibling.\nThat is the diagram''s whole argument, and it is the boundary label.\n\nSo the interesting question is how nineteen sovereign modules coordinate at all,\nand the answer is two mechanisms, both drawn:\n\nOne localStorage key, augment-it:active-record-set. Two modules write it\n(record-collector, records-surface) and five read it on mount and again on the\naugment-it:active-record-set-changed broadcast — the three resolvers, pack-runner\nand sort-filter-lens.\n\nTen named window events. augment-it:navigate is dispatched by five modules and\nlistened to by exactly one: the shell. A member can ask for a different surface;\nno member can mount one. That asymmetry is the emphasis edge at the bottom right.\n\nviewBox 1280x720, matching the companion so the two present as a pair.\n\nFour rounds of repair, each one the diagnostic''s own supported fix. Two cross-row\nedges were drawn vertical while the router had inferred horizontal sides, because\nthe source and target boxes were nearly the same width at nearly the same x and\nthe inference tie-broke the wrong way; the fix was to align centres exactly so\nvertical is unambiguous, not to hand-author via points. Then both vertical labels\nlanded inside their source node and needed labelAt at the gap midpoint. Then the\ndelivered page overflowed 1440x900 by 5px — repaired by trimming card copy, which\nis content removal before any shrinking.\n\nThe boundary label gained \"in four families\" on perceptual review: the legend\ncounts node shapes (Frontend 5) and the boundary claims nineteen, and without\nthat phrase a reader has to reconcile the two numbers themselves.\n\nReceipts: validate showcase 9/9 checks, composition pass, 0 errors, 0 warnings.\ndeliver ok, artifact sha e42d9ccc. visual-check pass at 1440x900, 1600x1000,\n1920x1080 and 2048x1320, light and dark, no overflow on any axis; smallest\nprojected node text 6.55px against a 6px floor.\n\nPerceptual review: done, by reading the rendered screenshot at 2048x1320 dark.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"508220b7405b9de6c77dd9cc5ed4581e88075b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/508220b7405b9de6c77dd9cc5ed4581e88075b35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhkNmM0M2FlZmFiN2ZkNTEwZmRhMDMwZGQyNmE1NDk3MmFlMDcyMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1","sha":"4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1"}],"sha":"8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d6c43aefab7fd510fda030dd26a54972ae07207"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:24:52Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:24:52Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"diagram(context-v): the federal design system — one kit, nineteen front-ends\n\nAn Archify architecture diagram of the platform components and how members\nconsume them. Companion to augment-it-decomposed-architecture, which covers the\nservice topology; this one covers the design system.\n\nEight nodes, eight relationships, two boundaries. The composition carries the one\nfact that is genuinely hard to hold in your head: a component is imported at BUILD\ntime, its colours resolve at RUN time, and the two arrows into the member tier are\ndifferent arrows. A remote built last month still has to find this month''s tokens,\nwhich is why the shell injects the stylesheet exactly once.\n\nviewBox is 1280x720 — exactly 16:9, and chosen for that reason rather than by\ndefault. A 1600-wide viewBox failed the readability check: on a 1440px desktop the\npanel is 930px, so the scale is 0.58 and 9px context text projects at 5.2px,\nunder the 6px floor. 1280 keeps it at 6.5px and stays exactly 16:9.\n\nGetting there took four rounds of diagnostics, and every repair was the one the\nvalidator named. Two hand-authored `via` routes came out — the skill says start\nautomatic and add a control only when a diagnostic calls for one, and both of mine\nwere premature. The gate moved beside the members it checks, which freed the\nvertical space that was crowding the federal boundary''s title rail. Node copy was\nshortened rather than nodes widened, per the supported-fix order.\n\nThe card rail went 4 cards to 3 and 13 items to 6, because the delivered page\noverflowed a 900px viewport by 321px. That is content removal before panel\nshrinking, which is the order the skill prescribes.\n\nReceipts: validate showcase 9/9 artifact checks, 0 errors, 0 warnings. deliver ok,\nartifact sha 26ce20a8, spec sha 8f8c655c. visual-check pass at 1440x900 and\n2048x1320, light and dark, no overflow on any axis.\n\nPerceptual review: done, by reading the rendered screenshots at both sizes in both\nthemes. It reads left to right, the two-arrow story into the member tier is legible\nat slide distance, and the four guided views are usable as presentation chapters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6635621f2b3d69840da50ff5a2dc0d3738d6fd9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/6635621f2b3d69840da50ff5a2dc0d3738d6fd9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDQxMTJiOTY1OTk3ZDZlZTRlMjkyNThjNDc4OGVlNTUzYTIyMzNlYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85","sha":"96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85"}],"sha":"4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4112b965997d6ee4e29258c4788ee553a2233ec1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:51:21Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:51:21Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(deps): record the vitest devDependencies the ExternalLink sweep added\n\nFour members gained a test suite in the last sweep and their package.json files\nwere committed with it; the lockfile entries were not. Twelve lines, all\n`vitest@^3.2.7` under those same four importers, pinned to the version already\nresolved everywhere else in the workspace.\n\nLeft behind because I staged `apps/` by directory rather than checking `git\nstatus` for what else the install had touched. A lockfile that disagrees with the\npackage.json files beside it means the next clean install resolves something\nnobody chose — the exact class of drift the gates cannot see.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0d3af865d82b76fc181c44a9872cfb4354ae700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/e0d3af865d82b76fc181c44a9872cfb4354ae700"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDk2ZWJlNTIyNjJmODQ2ZjAzZTkxN2U0MTQwZjI4YTI0Yzc5MjBhODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3","sha":"a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3"}],"sha":"96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/96ebe52262f846f03e917e4140f28a24c7920a85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:33:42Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:33:42Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): ExternalLink gains inheritColor, because a contrast decision nearly vanished\n\nA member had `.lib-error a { color: inherit }` — a link sitting on\n--color-error-bg, where link-blue would break a contrast decision the container\nhad already made.\n\nThis component''s scoped rule compiles to (0,2,0) and a one-class member rule is\n(0,1,0), so adoption would have turned that link blue inside a red box WITH\nNOTHING IN THE DIFF TO SHOW IT. Caught by an engineer reading specificity, not by\nany gate.\n\ninheritColor makes it a declaration instead of a specificity argument. The intent\nlives at the call site, and it cannot be lost to a stylesheet injection order that\ndiffers between dev and a federated production build. It covers :visited too — a\nfollowed link that reverts to purple breaks the same contrast the prop exists to\nprotect.\n\nThe header now states the override rules plainly, because three members hit them:\na one-class rule loses, a two-class rule TIES and resolves on injection order\nwhich under Module Federation is not decidable, and a `class` handed to a child\ncomponent gets no scope hash at all so the rule is dead on arrival.\n\n## And I hit a documented trap while documenting\n\nWriting that note with a literal style tag inside a comment broke the file —\nsvelte-preprocess scans raw text, so postcss parsed the rest as CSS and\nsvelte-check reported an unclosed script. An agent recorded this exact trap\nearlier in the arc and I walked into it anyway. It cost one round trip, and the\nnote now says so next to the workaround.\n\nAlso worth recording: the federation reported 13 of 22 units failing for about a\nminute. Every one was a cascade from this single file, which is verify''s design\nworking — one number, one cause, named in one line.\n\n105 tests, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fcc978da152beabc7fa0bd6b53bb2b0f328078e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/5fcc978da152beabc7fa0bd6b53bb2b0f328078e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGExZjJiODNjMzdiY2UyMzBiMDYxYzg1OWYzODU5NjIxZGQ1NDc3ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9","sha":"fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9"}],"sha":"a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a1f2b83c37bce230b061c859f3859621dd5477d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:31:49Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:31:49Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(eight members): ExternalLink complete — 24 of 24, and a contrast decision that nearly vanished\n\nEvery external link in the federation is now on the component. 23 adopted here,\none already done, one pinned holdout. 22 CSS rule-sets reduced to 10. Zero rung 4\nanywhere in the diff.\n\n## The security line, honestly framed\n\nExactly ONE of my eight was missing noopener — org-workbench''s, rel=\"noreferrer\"\nwith no noopener, the same shape as all four of search-results''. The other 23\nalready had it, so those are ratchets rather than repairs.\n\nBut every one of the eight now writes NO rel at all, and that is the property\nworth having: a call site that writes one is a call site that can drop noopener on\nthe next edit. Seven already did.\n\n## The finding that matters more than the links\n\nExternalLink''s scoped style compiles to (0,2,0) — verified in the BUILT CSS, not\nrecalled — so a member rule setting colour or type from a single class loses\nsilently, and from two classes TIES and resolves on injection order.\n\nThe dangerous instance: docs-portal''s `.lib-error a { color: inherit }` was a\nCONTRAST decision — a link sitting on --color-error-bg. Adoption would have turned\nit link-blue inside a red box, with nothing in the diff to show it. Caught by\nreading specificity rather than by any gate.\n\nResolved at rung 2 by element-qualifying the survivors, and the underlying gap is\nclosed federally in the next commit.\n\n## A Svelte fact the rollout had not met\n\nA `class` prop handed to a CHILD COMPONENT gets no scope hash, so a survivor rule\nliving in a component''s own <style> is dead on arrival. svelte-check caught it as\nan unused selector. Every first-group survivor happened to live in a global\napp.css, so nine members went by before this appeared.\n\n## iconOnly fit, and the refusals it came from are closed\n\nBoth records-surface icon links adopted and their refusal comments removed, plus\ntwo more in response-reviewer. Measured: one was 10x20px — 21% of the target floor\n— and another ~19px from a 10px font with no bottom padding. Both inherit 24px now\nrather than being hand-held.\n\nAlso deleted: two bare-element descendant selectors that would have kept styling\nthe component''s own anchor, and a dead `outline: var(--focus-ring, …)` that had\nNEVER painted — the token holds a box-shadow value, so the outline was invalid at\ncomputed-value time and the comma fallback never applied.\n\n## The tests were mutation-checked, and three failed honestly first\n\nThirteen mutations, every one caught. Three assertions failed on first run and\nwere FIXED rather than loosened: a bare /color/ matching var(--color-border), a\nnon-greedy match sailing past icon tags, and a guest-region guard aimed at\n.lib-mount when the class is .lib-host — a guard on a nonexistent selector passes\nforever and guards nothing.\n\nRaised, not chased: person-enrichment''s two window.open(…,''_blank'',''noopener'')\ncontrols have the same no-AT-notice defect in a shape ExternalLink cannot reach,\nsince it renders an anchor and those are Buttons. Pinned by assertion so they stay\nvisible.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd91cf1cc824779f47ff17566976549e031720af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/bd91cf1cc824779f47ff17566976549e031720af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGZhNmIxNWI2MWQzYzU2YjJjMjdhM2Q1ZDI3OTk4MGMxMDZjYjAyYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae","sha":"a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae"}],"sha":"fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fa6b15b61d3c56b2c27a3d5d279980c106cb02a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:25:36Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:25:36Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): the connection vocabulary ships as a module sixteen members can import\n\nConnectionState was declared in StatusIndicator.svelte''s instance script, which no\npackage exports map can reach — so all SIXTEEN adopting members re-declared the\nunion by hand.\n\nSixteen copies of one list is sixteen chances to drift, and nothing would have\ncaught a member that added a seventh state or misspelled a sixth. One member''s\nadoption test resorted to comparing its own union against the component''s\nTEXTUALLY, by reading the source. That test exists because this file did not.\n\n./status.js now carries the type and a CONNECTION_STATES array in the order a\nlegend should list them. StatusIndicator re-exports the type for compatibility, so\nnothing that already imports it breaks.\n\nThree tests, and the second is the one that earns its place: it reads the\ncomponent''s own TONE and WORD maps and asserts every exported state appears in\nboth. A seventh state added to the list without a tone would fail — which is the\ndrift the sixteen copies could not catch.\n\nThe third asserts package.json actually exports it, because a module nobody can\nimport is the defect being fixed, and it is invisible from inside the package.\n\n102 tests, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf6b85167e6094c3b4d042addb2211ef162b34f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/bf6b85167e6094c3b4d042addb2211ef162b34f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGEyYWI2NWYyZDVkMDg1OTI5NDA0NmU5NGRjYjVkNjU2ZmM5MTU3YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3","sha":"721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3"}],"sha":"a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a2ab65f2d5d0859294046e94dcb5d656fc9157ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:24:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:24:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(corpora-curator): the last StatusIndicator holdout, and the slot nobody had counted\n\nSixteen of sixteen now. This member was skipped fifteen times for a good reason\nand the reason turned out to hide a second defect.\n\n## 6 -> 6 on the indicator everyone had looked at\n\nCONNECTION_TONE was ALREADY a correct six-way map, so there was no colour bug\nleft — which is exactly why every sweep passed it over. The migration bought the\nWORD instead: the label rendered {curation.connection} raw, so the operator read\n\"auth_required\" at the precise moment they needed to be told to sign in. It reads\n\"workspace sign-in required\" now. A local tone map structurally cannot fix that\nhalf.\n\n## 1 -> 5 on the slot nobody had counted\n\nThe workspace-picker slot rendered Chip tone=\"info\" \"connecting…\" for EVERY\nnon-open state. Five states, one appearance — and four of them were actively FALSE\nrather than merely undifferentiated: it claimed a handshake in progress while the\nsocket was closed, errored, idle, or gated behind sign-in.\n\nFifteen sweeps counted this member''s tone map and none counted its second slot.\n\n## The gallery forced a section into existence\n\nMore work than it looked, in one specific way. `buttons` and `chips` were both\nsourced from packages/shared-ui while filed under a heading reading \"Class-based\nprimitives from app.css\" — the exact wrongness the federated-libraries spec names.\nSo a Federal primitives section now exists, and the chips entry is rewritten\nrather than merely edited: renamed, its tone claim dropped 5 -> 2 because the\nstatus tones left with the connection states, its token list trimmed, and its a11y\nnote no longer claiming tone comes from a map that is gone.\n\nThe header-bar control also went 4 -> 6 options: idle and auth_required were\nMISSING from the gallery''s own state list, which is the same blind spot that let\nthe workspace slot lie.\n\nexemptClasses stayed at two entries. This is the first adoption to land after the\nui-* namespace reservation, and it paid zero — the stale comment arguing a Chip\nwould cost four entries is rewritten.\n\n## Zero CSS deleted, and that is the tell\n\n.cc-conn and the status-* recipes went in the earlier Chip adoption. This holdout\ndeleted TYPESCRIPT — an 8-line map and its 13-line justifying comment — which is\nprecisely the shape of a member whose colour was already right.\n\nDeletions were checked before being made: ChipTone survives because\nSOURCE_STATUS_TONE needs it, ConnStatus survives because the store types\nconnection from it, and both retentions are ASSERTED so a later sweep does not\nover-reach.\n\nEight adoption tests, suite to 32. They strip comments before asserting absence,\nso the prose audit trail naming the deleted map as history cannot be removed to\nappease a regex.\n\nMember gate 1 -> 1, contrast 30/30, 111 files clean.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf292cba9cd0ae72b22a8e3170b078a4045b06b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/bf292cba9cd0ae72b22a8e3170b078a4045b06b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDcyMWUwOGI2ZWJlMjMzZjAyYTZmNjRmYzAzNDg5NGM3NzZlZGVhYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b","sha":"fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b"}],"sha":"721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/721e08b6ebe233f02a6f64fc034894c776edeac3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:26:46Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:26:46Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(changelog): repair a line the heredoc ate\n\nAn unescaped backtick pair in the shell heredoc was evaluated rather than written,\nso the browser-drive section opened with a blank subject — the exact sentence\nnaming Button''s nowrap, which is the finding.\n\nCaught by reading the file back rather than trusting the write.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3c2760bb7e683d8a5fd96c2e2c446375e1465bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/a3c2760bb7e683d8a5fd96c2e2c446375e1465bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGZkZmQ5MWY2YTE2YWFhYjQ5ZDk0ODdjZjVmMTRlNzdlYTNiYjQ4NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b","sha":"67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b"}],"sha":"fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fdfd91f6a16aaab49d9487cf5f14e77ea3bb486b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:26:29Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:26:29Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"changelog(design-system): nine keyboard widgets that were never implemented\n\nSix primitives across 28 commits — Selector''s two variants, MenuItem,\nDisclosureRow, StatusIndicator, CountBadge, SearchBox''s two over a private core,\nand ExternalLink. 539 federal call sites. Composite roles with no keyboard: nine\nto zero.\n\nThe entry leads on why this arc needed tests when the first three did not: Button,\nChip and CardRow are appearance with a little behaviour, so a screenshot catches\ntheir defects. A broken keyboard renders perfectly.\n\nAnd the tests earned it immediately by finding that MY components were broken.\nSelectWrapper--ClickBody was keyboard-dead — display:contents generates no layout\nbox, so the button was not focusable while reporting tabIndex=0 and working with a\nmouse; three engineers found it independently and one measured tab stops going 37\nto 29, exactly the eight instances. Selector--Menu broke its own headline promise\nthree ways, each revealed only by fixing the one before.\n\nThe section I most want read is the fixture one: Selector--Menu''s Escape test\npassed while both adopters were broken, because the fixture''s trigger was a local\nconst no member could clear — and closing a menu is exactly when the anchor goes\naway. The test and the realistic call site disagreed, and the test won.\n\nTwo agent decisions are credited as the best moves of the arc, both refusals: the\nit.fails tripwire that blocked an adoption rather than silently dropping a\npre-filled value, and the icon-link refusal where adopting would have turned a\nmeasured pass into a measured failure.\n\nIt also records that the drift gate was punishing the practice — documenting a\ndeleted defect re-created it, so the checker was discouraging the one habit this\ncodebase runs on — and that my own census had the same comments-as-code bug, which\nis why the ninth surface turned out never to have existed.\n\nAnd the finding no test could reach: a browser drive on the host caught that\nSelector options did not inherit Button''s nowrap, so every swap silently converted\na clip into a wrap. jsdom has no layout. A component that replaces another must\nmatch its LAYOUT defaults, not just its role and its keyboard.\n\nRefs #101 #105 #107 #112\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ef72538c86777323b80ad5fd8c6e74368255e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/0ef72538c86777323b80ad5fd8c6e74368255e75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDY3YWI4ZTFhZWM1MDBmYTk4MjE1ZmU3MTIwMGQyNzRmNjY4YzAwNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062","sha":"73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062"}],"sha":"67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/67ab8e1aec500fa98215fe71200d274f668c005b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:14:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:14:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): a Selector option did not wrap like a Button, so every swap was a silent layout change\n\nButton declares white-space: nowrap AND a fixed height. A Selector option declared\nneither — only a min-block-size. So a member replacing Button rows with options\nconverted a CLIP into a WRAP without anyone choosing to: one real row measured\n48px against its neighbours'' 29px, its label squeezed to the min-content of its\nfirst word.\n\njsdom cannot see this. There is no layout, so it passed every test in every\nadopting member and was caught by a browser drive on the federation host — the one\nmember where someone looked at pixels. It is latent everywhere the same swap\nhappened.\n\nOptions truncate by default now. That is NOT a style preference, it is swap\ncompatibility: the default has to match what Button did, or adopting a component\nsilently changes a member''s layout and the diff shows nothing.\n\nwrapOptions opts out for a surface that genuinely wants multi-line rows, and a\ntest asserts both the default and the opt-out — plus the source-level nowrap rule,\nbecause \"it truncates\" is the claim the test environment cannot observe.\n\nThe general shape, worth keeping: a component that replaces another component must\nmatch its LAYOUT defaults, not just its role and its keyboard. The parts nobody\ndeclares are the parts that change silently.\n\n99 tests, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e3e114a6db6b8a1aec36d1eea07f36343fee5c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/1e3e114a6db6b8a1aec36d1eea07f36343fee5c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDczYWI4YmVhYzlkZjVlMjBjMjQ5MGM4NGE2N2M2MmJjNmIwNTkwNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f","sha":"cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f"}],"sha":"73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/73ab8beac9df5e20c2490c84a67c62bc6b059062"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:13:19Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:13:19Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(shell): Selector in the federation host — and the ninth surface never existed\n\nThe last composite-role defects, in the unit every remote mounts inside. 33 tests,\nmember gate flat at 12, containment held, zero rung 4.\n\n## Eight surfaces, not nine — and my census had the bug I just fixed in the gate\n\nDevelopersMenu declares no composite role. The grep that put it on the list hit a\nCODE COMMENT — `// role=\"menu\"/\"menuitem\" — rather than inventing a second one` —\nplus a role=\"status\" on a Chip. It composes JumboPopdown and inherits its keyboard\nwholesale.\n\nThat is precisely the defect I fixed in design-drift an hour ago: a checker\nreading comments as code. My own census had it too, and it inflated the plan''s\nheadline number by one for two days.\n\nThe engineer asserted it rather than argued it — the third describe mounts\nDevelopersMenu and proves it went from five tab stops to one with working arrows,\nwithout a line of its own changing.\n\n## What the two real surfaces were shipping\n\nJumboPopdown had the role triad CORRECT — unlike both ConnectorPalettes — and\nnothing the role promises: three raw menuitem buttons with no tabindex and no\nkeydown handler anywhere on the panel. Escape was a document listener that set\nopen = false, so the focused button unmounted with the panel and focus fell to\nbody.\n\nWorkspaceSwitcher had no [tabindex=\"0\"] at all, so the first red failed with\n\"expected null not to be null\".\n\n## One line that is load-bearing, and only in one of the two paths\n\ncloseAndRestore() needs `await tick()` before focusing the trigger, because\n`switching` flips that trigger''s disabled attribute and Svelte writes it on the\nNEXT flush. A synchronous focus() on a still-disabled button is a silent no-op and\nfocus lands on body exactly as before. The Escape path does not have this hazard;\nthe select path does.\n\n## Containment held, measured the same way either side\n\n189 -> 204 selectors, 174 -> 189 hashed, unhashed 15 -> 15 — a byte-identical set,\nevery one from packages/theme. Zero new unhashed selectors, no style global, and\nthe only :global() escapes are the two pre-existing ones under a hashed parent.\n\nrg for composite roles over shell/src now matches only comments.\n\nThe JumboPopdown HOLDOUT note standing since the Button rollout — \"that is a\nMenuItem organ, raised not forced\" — is redeemed: the control recipe is gone,\nleaving only content layout inside the slot.\n\nRefs #101 #107 #112\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df980bb74a44b5187c3db161f369c1a67a8cfa7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/df980bb74a44b5187c3db161f369c1a67a8cfa7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGNjNzg0OWQxODk2MTM2MjkwZDY4ZWJmNDk2MjhlYTRiZGEyNjAyMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266","sha":"ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266"}],"sha":"cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cc7849d1896136290d68ebf49628ea4bda26021f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:06:15Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:06:15Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): ExternalLink had no icon mode, and adoption deleted a visited state\n\nTwo gaps found by an adoption that REFUSED rather than shipping a regression.\n\n## iconOnly\n\nTwo icon-only links could not adopt, for two reasons either of which was\nsufficient:\n\nAn aria-label on the anchor SUPPRESSES the visually-hidden new-tab notice — the\none thing this component exists to add. So a member naming its icon link would\nhave lost the feature it adopted the component for. The name is composed in the\nDOM now, so the notice is part of it and cannot be overridden away.\n\nAnd min-inline-size: 0 is declared in this component''s scoped style at (0,2,0), so\na member class at (0,1,0) could not restore a width floor — reaching 24px WIDE\nneeded rung 4 on the first try. An icon link is square here.\n\nThe refusal was right in the strongest sense: one of those sites already cleared\nthe target floor with its own rules, so adopting would have turned a measured pass\ninto a measured failure. \"This does not fit yet\" is the result that produced the\nfix.\n\n## :visited\n\nOne member had a :visited rule recolouring a followed link, and adoption deleted\nit because link colour is now the component''s — so the visited state stopped being\ndistinguishable in that field.\n\nA visited link that looks unvisited is a usability regression, so it is restored\nfederally rather than left for each member to rediscover. Via\n--color-link-visited with --color-link as the fallback, so it degrades to today''s\nbehaviour until the theme defines one.\n\n97 tests, svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afe32d95604013246bc2667f9aa4085863390da4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/afe32d95604013246bc2667f9aa4085863390da4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGViZDRmY2RmMWRhYmRmOGFiODA2NzU4NmQzNDRjMzY2Mjk2YTUyNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db","sha":"2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db"}],"sha":"ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ebd4fcdf1dabdf8ab8067586d344c366296a5266"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:05:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:05:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(six members): ExternalLink — and six of the federation''s seven missing noopener were in two files\n\nTen links adopted, three deliberately left, all six member gates flat. Fifteen CSS\nrule-sets deleted outright, two slimmed to a single rung-0 declaration, 52\ndeclarations removed. Zero rung 4.\n\n## The security headline\n\nSIX of the federation''s seven missing-noopener links were in the two search\nmembers — four of four in one, two of two in the other, every one\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" with no noopener, so each opened page got\nwindow.opener access back into ours.\n\nThe tests pin the real fix rather than the symptom: those members now write NO rel\nat all, so a call site cannot drop noopener again. That is the whole argument for\nmerging rel in the component rather than documenting it.\n\n## What the migration changed visibly, stated\n\nThe font sizes went too — 0.82rem, 0.92rem, 0.85rem, 0.7rem, 11px — because\nExternalLink declares font-size: inherit specifically so the row owns type, and\nthose were raw values against the shipped seven-step scale. Row titles in both\nsearch members now read LARGER. Per the loop that is the migration working, but it\nis the one visible change and it is named rather than buried.\n\nAlso deleted: a descendant `.srq-note a` selector that would have styled any\nfuture link the component was supposed to own.\n\nEvery adopted link previously had NO height declaration at all, so its hit target\nwas one line box — computed from declared type, between 15px and 20px. All ten now\ninherit a 24px floor by declaration rather than by luck.\n\n## Two holdouts that were right to hold\n\nrecord-collector''s .social-chip is the interactive-badge organ — an anchor with a\nborder, a pill radius, a surface fill and a ConfidencePill inside. Adopting would\nnegate the base recipe rather than adjust it. It is pinned BY IDENTITY rather than\nby count, so a fresh raw anchor cannot hide behind it.\n\nAnd two icon-only links in records-surface exposed a real API gap, fixed in the\nnext commit.\n\n## The tests bite, and were checked\n\nFive adoption suites that read the member''s own source: imports present, no raw\ntarget=\"_blank\", no self-written rel, recipes actually deleted rather than merely\nunused. The engineer MUTATION-CHECKED them — reintroducing a raw anchor failed two\ntests, reverting returned 13 of 13.\n\nrecords-surface has no test, and that is named rather than smoothed: it is the one\nmember of the six with no vitest infrastructure, and wiring it needs a package.json\nchange the brief did not cover.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23a33232acfc338b9bf69c1b1193af40debd581c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/23a33232acfc338b9bf69c1b1193af40debd581c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDJmYmVjMzdkOWUxNzMxZGI0MmZlNTQ0YTI3MjIzMTVkMzZhMmIyZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3","sha":"c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3"}],"sha":"2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2fbec37d9e1731db42fe544a2722315d36a2b2db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:54:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:54:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): ExternalLink — 34 links that never said they leave the app\n\nMeasured across all 34 sightings in 12 members:\n\n  0  warn a screen reader that the link opens a new tab\n  7  set target=\"_blank\" with NO rel=\"noopener\" — the opened page gets\n     window.opener access back into ours\n  1  measured at 10x20px, 21% of the WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 target floor\n\nNone of that is visible in a screenshot, which is how it survived twelve members\nand nine migrations. A sighted mouse user cannot tell any of the three apart from\na correct link.\n\n## Two decisions the component makes that a lint rule could not\n\nThe new-tab notice is VISUALLY HIDDEN, not display:none. display:none removes an\nelement from the accessibility tree as well as the page, so the notice would be\ninvisible to exactly the user it exists for — while looking finished in the\nmarkup. A test asserts the rule contains position:absolute and does NOT contain\ndisplay:none, because that mistake reads as done.\n\nAnd rel is MERGED, never replaced. A member passing rel=\"nofollow\" keeps noopener,\ndeduped so it does not become \"noopener noopener noreferrer\". The security\nproperty must not be something a call site can drop by accident, which is exactly\nhow seven of them lost it.\n\n## A test that could not pass, for the same reason an earlier one could not fail\n\ngetComputedStyle cannot see component CSS here — the plugin does not inject it\ninto the test document, so every property reads as its initial value. An earlier\ntarget-size assertion was VACUOUS for that reason and passed unconditionally; this\none failed unconditionally, which is louder and no more useful. Both now assert\nagainst the source, where the claim actually lives. Recorded in the test so the\nthird person does not rediscover it.\n\n94 tests, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46b4c0c23435de2fd79ca4ed864e486d99524f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/46b4c0c23435de2fd79ca4ed864e486d99524f0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGMwYWNiMGZjM2I0NGYyZTM5NWZkZTljZjE2NjE2MGEwNjBjNzlhYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114","sha":"e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114"}],"sha":"c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c0acb0fc3b44f2e395fde9cf166160a060c79aa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:35:20Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:35:20Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): SearchBox could not address its own input, and its clears were invisible\n\nTwo seams the third adoption lost, both found by a member that had to give\nsomething up to adopt.\n\n## inputClass\n\n`class` lands on the wrapper and `rest.class` is overridden, so a member had no\nway to put a per-field state cue on the FIELD — an invalid ring, a dirty marker, a\nsave flash. The adoption lost a 1.2s save-confirmation pulse that its two sibling\nfields still have, and the engineer correctly declined to reach for rung 4 with a\nraw value on the first try.\n\nA test asserts inputClass reaches the input AND that it does NOT land on the\nwrapper, because \"it applied somewhere\" is the failure mode.\n\n## Programmatic clears now dispatch a real input event\n\nThe delegation recipe — the one the component''s own error message prescribes —\ntells a member to listen on a wrapper, and a wrapper sees DOM events. But when the\nwidget wrote `value` itself, on Escape-to-clear or clearOnSelect, it did so\nsilently. So a member''s listener never learned the box had emptied and kept state\npointing at something no longer on screen: in the adopting member, a double-Escape\nleft an org id selected whose name was gone.\n\nThe recipe saw typing but not the widget''s own writes, which made it a half\nrecipe. Both paths go through one `writeValue` now, and the test listens on a\nwrapper exactly as a member would rather than on the component.\n\n87 tests, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eddb163501e80b8f079aeb15fff11abbc02bbd27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/eddb163501e80b8f079aeb15fff11abbc02bbd27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGU1M2RjMDU4NjM4ZDEzZTg4ZjNjYzhiYmY5ZTU4MGQ2ODQ1MWYxMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319","sha":"a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319"}],"sha":"e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e53dc058638d13e88f3cc8bbf9e580d68451f114"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:35:20Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:35:20Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(scripts): design-drift was reading comments as code, so documenting a deletion re-created it\n\nAn engineer deleted a rule carrying `z-index: 5`, wrote a comment explaining the\ndeletion, and F4 re-reported the literal from the prose. The member sat at its old\ncount until the sentence was reworded.\n\nSo DOCUMENTING A REMOVED DEFECT RE-CREATED IT IN THE GATE — a direct incentive\nnever to explain a deletion, in a codebase whose whole practice is explaining\nthings in place. F8 had the same blind spot on hex literals and it had already\nbeen reported twice as a finding without anyone fixing the cause.\n\nThis file''s own header warns about a checker that reports success because it\nfailed to look. This is the inverse: one that reports failure because it looked\nsomewhere it should not.\n\nF1, F1a, F4 and F8 now read a comment-stripped copy. `n` is untouched for any\ncheck that genuinely wants raw text.\n\nOne subtlety worth the extra line: `//` is stripped ONLY outside .css. In CSS it\nis not a comment, and `background: url(//cdn.example/x.png)` would have swallowed\nthe rest of the line — hiding a real declaration behind a protocol-relative URL.\nThe `[^:]` guard catches `https://` and does not catch `url(//`. Proven with a\nprobe file both ways: a comment naming z-index: 5 and #ff0000 produces zero\nfindings, and a live `z-index: 7` sitting after a protocol-relative url is still\ncaught.\n\nFederation 67 -> 66. The one point was a comment.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"64b02e3ddb2bb882700b86ee70c169540477d3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/64b02e3ddb2bb882700b86ee70c169540477d3b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGExNTRiMTExZTZlY2NjMjA3NWNiYzE1NDcxZmQ2OTY3NTZkOTUzMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c","sha":"59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c"}],"sha":"a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a154b111e6eccc2075cbc15471fd696756d95319"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:32:46Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:32:46Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(person-enrichment): SearchBox--Autocomplete, and a keyboard hint that had started lying\n\nSixteen tests, member gate 2 -> 1, zero override rungs. All eight it.fails\ntripwires flipped on the first run after the refactor and are ordinary tests\nagain — not one of the eight defects had to be re-discovered by hand a commit\nlater, which is the entire argument for the marker.\n\n## The binding had to work both ways, and a test proves it\n\nbind:value={affiliation.completeName} is the adoption. Pre-fill is what blocked\nit, so pre-fill is pinned — but the second test matters more: pickOrg() writes the\nchosen org''s name back ONTO the affiliation, so the binding has to carry\nparent-to-widget, not just widget-to-parent. A settable-once prop would have\npassed the first test and failed this one.\n\nclearOnSelect checked and deliberately NOT applied, with pickOrg() as the proof\nrather than a judgement call: this box holds the ANSWER, not the query — the name\nit ends up with is what gets persisted. Clearing on select would discard the value\nthe pick just produced. Pinned so nobody switches it on later.\n\n## The delegation recipe closed a real gap\n\nThe card needs two reserved keystrokes for its own concerns, so both moved to the\nwrapper and the Enter handler reads exactly what the component''s error message\nprescribes: defaultPrevented is set IFF the widget picked an active option.\n\nThat restored a capability the surface did not have. While any suggestion was on\nscreen the operator COULD NOT COMMIT A NAME THEY HAD TYPED, because Enter was\nhard-wired to suggestions[0] — and the surface''s own hint said \"keep typing to\ncreate new\", which was genuinely the only way.\n\nThe engineer also asserted the NEGATIVE — that the widget refuses no key it was\ngiven — because the refusal is a console error and therefore easy to ignore.\n\n## The deletion worth naming\n\nThe ↵ badge on the first suggestion advertised \"Enter picks the first match\". True\nthen, false now. A keyboard hint that lies is the exact defect class this rollout\nexists to remove, so leaving it would have been worse than the markup it\ndescribed. It moved out from under the popup — inventing a footer slot for a hint\nwould be the wrong shape of fix — and was rewritten for the real contract.\n\nGone with it: suggestions, suggestOpen, lookupSeq, lookupTimer, scheduleLookup,\npick, onCompleteInput, the focus-reopen, the Escape branch, and the CardRow and\nSelectWrapper imports the popup rows were built from. Plus four CSS rule-sets\nincluding a raw z-index.\n\nThe popup adds zero focusable descendants, down from three. Arrowing twice then\nEnter picks the SECOND suggestion — unreachable without a mouse before.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"33de84d4f49953700e4a64a67deaa5df5be767c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/33de84d4f49953700e4a64a67deaa5df5be767c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDU5YzJhMDA5MzUwMmIwZDUzOTcxOWI2YjRiNmM2YWRlNWRkMDBjOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402","sha":"8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402"}],"sha":"59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/59c2a0093502b0d539719b6b4b6c6ade5dd00c9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:24:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:24:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(corpora-curator, org-workbench): SearchBox — and three members correctly refused\n\nTwo members adopted, three refused with evidence, and one of the refusals found a\nbug that was shipping.\n\n## corpora-curator — LiveFilter, and the popup was thirteen tab stops\n\nIts tag suggestions were a div of buttons: no role on the input, so a screen\nreader announced a plain text field and never mentioned suggestions appeared; no\nkeydown handler, so ArrowDown did nothing; and every option was a native tab stop,\nso a twelve-suggestion popup made the field THIRTEEN tab stops and Tab took the\ncaret out of the input mid-word.\n\nIts own app.css had confessed in prose: \"the organ it wants is a combobox listbox\noption, which nobody has built.\"\n\nLiveFilter, not Autocomplete, because suggestTags was a synchronous filter over an\narray the member already held — wrapping a Promise around Array.filter would have\nshipped a debounce, a stale guard and four states that can never occur.\n\nFree text survives, and how is worth keeping: passing onkeydown would have\nreplaced the keyboard contract, so the member listens one level up on a rung-0\nwrapper and reads e.defaultPrevented, which the widget sets IFF it picked an\nactive option. Four rule-sets and 21 declarations deleted, plus a now-dead\nsuggestTags.\n\n## org-workbench — Autocomplete, and its stale guard was half right\n\nif (term === q.trim()) was correct on the success path — the test for it was green\nBEFORE the refactor and was kept so the refactor could not lose it.\n\nBut the catch block had no guard at all, so a rejection for a term the operator\nhad already moved past emptied the suggestions and painted an error over correct,\non-screen results. The finally was unguarded too, clearing the busy indicator\nwhile a newer request was still in flight.\n\nperson-enrichment''s hand-roll guarded both paths. The two members disagreed, the\nweaker one was shipping a real bug, and that is the argument for promoting the\nguard rather than documenting it.\n\nIts ROW HOLDOUT note is resolved — it said the search item was waiting for an\norgan that carries role=\"option\".\n\n## Two tests were wrong, and one was vacuous\n\nThe staleness pair read results through [role=\"option\"], which does not exist\ntoday, so both failed with the MISSING-ROLE defect wearing a staleness test''s\nname. And an Escape test passed because there is no listbox to be null, making\n\"Escape closed it\" and \"it never opened\" the same assertion. Both fixed before the\nmember was touched.\n\n## Three refusals, each with the sweep pinned so it is not re-run\n\nchat has two textareas and zero inputs; its suggestions are a chip row of actions\nalready on Selector--Menu. record-collector has one input, type=file. search-and-add\nhas exactly one input in all of src/, a submit form with no options and no async\nlookup — and three executable claims now pin that negative, so they fail if\nsomeone gives it a half-built combobox.\n\nPer the loop: do not invent a keyboard where none was promised.\n\nperson-enrichment stays unadopted pending its own commit — its eight red\nassertions are live tripwires that fail once the binding they needed exists, which\nit now does.\n\nMember gates: cc 2->1, ow 6->5, saa 3->3, none increased.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ede99578d87aef75039e74b4ce4019814c78f28c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/ede99578d87aef75039e74b4ce4019814c78f28c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhiYzg2MjFhYTc0MDI5YTVhZDcyZmRiMWNkOWM4ZWU5Y2E5MmY0MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20","sha":"8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20"}],"sha":"8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8bc8621aa74029a5ad72fdb1cd9c8ee9ca92f402"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:24:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:24:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): SearchBox could not take an initial value, and rest silently replaced its keyboard\n\nThree defects found by the first two adoptions, all of them mine, all measured at\nreal call sites. 85 tests, six new.\n\n## The blocker that correctly stopped an adoption\n\nSearchBox--Autocomplete kept its query private and never exposed it, so a member\nwhose field ARRIVES POPULATED rendered empty. person-enrichment''s affiliation name\nis auto-detected from the person''s email domain and shown to the operator as\n\"Pre-filled — matched email domain\"; adopting would have silently dropped a value\nthey were looking at.\n\nThat engineer measured it with a throwaway probe rather than inferring it, refused\nto ship the regression, and marked its eight red assertions `it.fails` — which\nPASSES while the defect is present and FAILS the moment it is fixed. A live\ntripwire rather than a silenced test: whoever adds the binding cannot land the\nadoption without returning to that file. That is the best use of a test I have\nseen in this arc.\n\n`value` is bindable on both variants now. The core always had it; the variants\njust failed to pass it through. It unblocks three things at once — an initial\nvalue, reading what was typed to seed a create-instead form, and writing the\nchosen label back on pick.\n\n## The same silent clobber, for the third time\n\n{...rest} was spread AFTER the component''s own handlers, so a member passing\n`onkeydown` — the obvious spelling for \"and also handle my Enter\" — REPLACED the\nentire keyboard contract. No error, renders identically.\n\nThis is the third instance of one bug class: `class` in Button and both\nSelectWrappers, `style` in Chip, now handlers here. rest spreads first everywhere\nnow, and the three keys that would fight the contract are refused out loud with\nthe delegation recipe in the message.\n\n## And the one the picking member worked around\n\nNothing could clear the box after a pick. Five of six members SEARCH — you picked\n\"Acme Corp\", the box should still say \"acme\" — but the one that PICKS was leaving\n\"Emp\" behind so the next tag was typed onto the end of it. It worked around that\nby remounting the whole widget behind {#key} and re-focusing on tick(), six lines\nacross two files.\n\nclearOnSelect, off by default, because the majority case is correct as it was.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c10df1a2a05f54b981d09a83b74dcc1a9513e3f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/c10df1a2a05f54b981d09a83b74dcc1a9513e3f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDg4MzM3MDIxODFkMjA2MTgzZGUyMTAyMGQ3ZGM3ZjBmMmE3YzNhMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f","sha":"b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f"}],"sha":"8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8833702181d206183de21020d7dc7f0f2a7c3a20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:07:57Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:07:57Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): SearchBox--LiveFilter and SearchBox--Autocomplete over a private core\n\nSix members ship a text input that narrows a list you pick from, two of them\nalready declaring a composite ARIA role with no keyboard. Fifteen tests, written\nbefore the components; 79 passing overall.\n\n## The claim that makes this a separate organ\n\nTHE INPUT KEEPS FOCUS. Every other selection organ here moves focus to the thing\nbeing chosen — Selector uses a roving tabindex, so the screen reader announces the\noption because it is focused. A SearchBox cannot: the user is still typing, and\nmoving focus would take the caret out of the input.\n\nSo the active option is named by aria-activedescendant and NO OPTION IS EVER\ntabindex=\"0\". Getting that backwards produces a widget that looks right, reads\nright in a screenshot, and drops the caret on the first arrow key.\n\n## Why a private core rather than nesting the two\n\nNesting was tried both ways on paper and neither works. Autocomplete wrapping\nLiveFilter filters twice — the server already narrowed by the query, so filtering\nagain by the same string discards the fuzzy matches, aliases and\nranked-but-not-prefix results it deliberately returned. LiveFilter wrapping\nAutocomplete inverts the dependency.\n\nWhat they share is neither variant: it is the input, the popup and the keyboard.\nSearchBoxCore holds those and is NOT in package.json exports, so members see only\nthe two named variants and the keyboard contract exists exactly once — which\nmatters because that contract is the entire reason the organ exists.\n\n## The guard two members had already hand-rolled\n\nEvery Autocomplete request takes a ticket and only the latest may write. Without\nit a slow response for \"aa\" lands after a fast one for \"aardvark\" and replaces\ncorrect suggestions with stale ones — invisible in testing, common in use. There\nis a test that resolves the queries out of order and asserts the stale one loses.\n\nFour states LiveFilter does not have: loading, error, empty-after-search, and\nbelow-minimum. The last is the one members get wrong — \"no results\" and \"you have\nnot typed enough yet\" are indistinguishable if you only read an array''s length, so\na user who typed one character is told there is nothing to find. Below the minimum\nis idle, and a test asserts the empty state does NOT appear there.\n\nA failed lookup is an error state rather than a silent empty, for the same reason.\n\n## Two suppressions and a rename, all with reasons in place\n\nThe linter''s \"role=option must have a tabindex\" is the rule for a STANDALONE\nlistbox where focus moves into the list. Here a tabindex would be the very defect\nthat rule exists to prevent, inverted. Suppressed with that written above it.\n\nAnd a variable named `state` SHADOWS the $state rune — the component stops\ncompiling with an error naming the rune rather than the variable. Renamed to\n`phase`, with the reason, because it is cheap to hit and confusing to read.\n\nSpec: context-v/specs/SearchBox-LiveFilter-And-Autocomplete.md\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"239b8fc42a6532602afb28dc6bcfc9127a365932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/239b8fc42a6532602afb28dc6bcfc9127a365932"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGI3MGEwNjgwZGQyNmZlZmZlNjgzOGNiNzE4NjY0OWQ4ZTk5Nzg0NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c","sha":"44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c"}],"sha":"b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b70a0680dd26feffe6838cb7186649d8e997846f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:04:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T17:04:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"spec(context-v): SearchBox — LiveFilter and Autocomplete, subsidiary to the component contract\n\nA subsidiary spec. The federal contract — override ladder, control scale, token\nrules, rung 0 — lives in Component-API-Contract-And-The-Control-Scale and is\ndeliberately not restated; this documents only what is specific to the family.\n\nThe nuance that justifies a spec at all: this is the FIRST ORGAN WHERE THE INPUT\nKEEPS FOCUS. Selector--Listbox and Selector--Menu use a roving tabindex — focus\nlands on the active option and the screen reader reads it because it is focused. A\nSearchBox cannot do that, because the user is still typing; moving focus would\ntake the caret out of the input. So the active option is announced via\naria-activedescendant while focus never leaves. That single difference is why this\nis not a Selector-- variant.\n\nThe axis between the two variants is where options come from, and it is measured\nrather than asserted: --Autocomplete has four states --LiveFilter does not, and two\nmembers independently hand-rolled the same stale-response guard — without which a\nslow response for one query lands after a fast one for another and replaces\ncorrect suggestions with stale ones.\n\nRecords why nesting the two was rejected in both directions. Autocomplete wrapping\nLiveFilter filters twice, discarding the fuzzy matches and aliases the server\ndeliberately returned; LiveFilter wrapping Autocomplete inverts the dependency.\nWhat they share is neither variant — it is the input, popup and keyboard — so\nthose live in a private core that is NOT exported, and the keyboard contract\nexists exactly once and cannot drift.\n\nAnd it records the rejected name with its reasoning, because that generalises:\n__Suggestive misuses BEM''s element syntax for an adjective, and\nAutocompleteLiveFilter stacks three words for one idea so the modifier\ndiscriminates nothing. Splitting those words across the two variants is what\nturned them into a real axis.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c5893be7e71b4684044a71eb0e7a71cb58066832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/c5893be7e71b4684044a71eb0e7a71cb58066832"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDQ0ZmJkMWJkZjgyMWZmNjc0Njg4ODk5OTUwNzVmOGYyZWE2ODYyOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239","sha":"380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239"}],"sha":"44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/44fbd1bdf821ff67468889995075f8f2ea68629c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:47:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:47:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(shell): the queue badge the size prop was added for, and a stale workaround corrected\n\nTwo follow-ons the CountBadge fix created and nobody did. Found by checking\nwhether the fix was actually IN EFFECT rather than merely committed.\n\nshell''s done-count was still a raw span. It is the site the sweep explicitly could\nnot adopt — its metrics row is uniformly sm, and the badge''s single size was a sm\nButton''s entire outer height, so adopting would have painted a pill across the\ncontrol''s border or forced the whole row to grow. That is exactly what `size=\"sm\"`\nwas added to unblock, and then the component was fixed and the member was never\nrevisited.\n\ntone=\"accent\" rather than the default inherit, deliberately: arrival is meant to\nbe loud while the rail is collapsed, per the queue-remote spec, and inherit would\nhave muted it to the toggle''s own colour. Thirteen declarations of hand-rolled\npill CSS deleted, including a 1.15em box and a 10px font that predate the type\nscale.\n\nAnd pack-runner carried a comment describing a constraint that no longer exists —\n\"CountBadge is a fixed --control-h-sm block\". It is not, since the fix. The\nsize=\"md\" stays, but for the better reason the workaround happened to buy rather\nthan the one that is now false: it takes the target from 24px, EXACTLY the WCAG\n2.2 SC 2.5.8 floor, to 28px. Reverting to sm would give that back.\n\nA stale comment explaining a workaround is worse than no comment: it teaches the\nnext reader a constraint that was removed, and it is the shape of thing nothing\nchecks.\n\nMember gates flat at 12 and 5. svelte-check clean across 99 files. 22 of 22 units\nverify.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d672918a60c9d2218ec894cdfa1a4fc5bf3da2a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/d672918a60c9d2218ec894cdfa1a4fc5bf3da2a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDM4MGQ3MmI3ODhkNzMzMTA4MTgwYzA2YTg1Y2ZhYmEwODFlYWQyMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04","sha":"c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04"}],"sha":"380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/380d72b788d733108180c06a85cfaba081ead239"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:55:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:55:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(fifteen members): StatusIndicator and CountBadge — six members were still shipping the identical broken recipe\n\nStatusIndicator in 15 members across 16 call sites; CountBadge in 3 across 9. 24\nCSS rule-sets deleted, 8 independent hand-rolled tone maps gone — about 103 lines\nof duplicated logic. Every member gate flat, federation 70 -> 70.\n\n## The headline is how many states each member could actually show\n\nSIX members carried byte-for-byte the same recipe, still live after nine\nmigrations: five states rendered as three colour treatments, with connecting and\nauth_required sharing an undifferentiated --color-border ground and idle having no\nrendering path at all. Three of the six also carried identical hardcoded\nfallbacks, which is copy-paste scaffolding rather than independent design.\n\nshell''s workspace switcher was the worst, and it was invisible: the socket state\nwas folded into the button label and covered exactly one case. connecting and idle\ncollapsed to \"connecting…\" while open, closed, error AND auth_required all fell\nthrough to the workspace''s display name. A DEAD SOCKET AND A HEALTHY ONE RENDERED\nIDENTICALLY, with the only trace of failure in a title attribute nobody hovers.\nIts dot went too — accent-versus-muted, aria-hidden, no word, a live 1.4.1\ncolour-alone encoding that never read the connection at all.\n\nenhanced-records-list''s empty state rendered \"connecting to workspace…\" for all\nfour non-open states, so a closed socket and a sign-in gate both claimed to be\nconnecting.\n\nEight more members had already got the tone semantics right — independently, eight\ntimes, in a prior Chip rollout. The delta there is eight copies of one decision\ndeleted.\n\nAll six states clear 4.5:1 in all three modes; the tightest is neutral in light at\n4.99.\n\n## CountBadge tone choices, with the reasoning\n\nSeven inherit, all inside a Button''s label — the case the header names, where the\nbadge must track primary-when-selected and secondary-when-not or the row''s\nselected-state cue dies. Two neutral, for list counts inside an h3, because\ninherit would tint them from the heading''s own colour and make a subordinate count\nread as part of the title''s emphasis.\n\nThat second choice is a small measured DECREASE — 4.99 to 4.57 in light — and is\nflagged rather than smoothed: still passing, 0.07 above the floor, thin.\n\n## Three census entries were false positives, and the census is already stale\n\nrecord-card-count and candidates-count are SENTENCES — \"3 responses\" — and\nCountBadge renders a number alone. pe-counter is a RATIO in a baseline-aligned\nstrip a centred pill would break.\n\nAnd two more candidates were absorbed into DisclosureRow''s hint by a parallel run\nDURING this session, so the ~28 figure the sweep opened with was stale before it\nfinished. Worth knowing when a census is used to size work.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d73738d3d434a726f805ce95562ad4a77a652913","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/d73738d3d434a726f805ce95562ad4a77a652913"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGM0OGE1YjE2OWQ5YmYwMDBjOGQ0YTNjYjYwY2EzYWI1NDYyNjFiMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814","sha":"e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814"}],"sha":"c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c48a5b169d9bf000c8d4a3cb60ca3ab546261b04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:55:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:55:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): CountBadge had one size that collided with its own host, and a fill that cost the host its contrast\n\nTwo defects, both measured at real call sites by the sweep that adopted it.\n\n## Its only size was exactly its host''s outer height\n\nblock-size was --control-h-sm, which is exactly an `sm` Button''s OUTER height — so\na badge inside one measured 0.00px inset top and bottom, in all three modes, and\nits pill ground painted straight across the control''s 1px border.\n\nThat hit the two members the component''s header names as its motivating case, both\nof which had `sm` filter rows. One was resolved member-side by taking the row to\n`md`, which also lifted the target from 24px — EXACTLY the WCAG floor — to 28.\nThe other could not: shell''s queue badge sits in a uniformly-small metrics row\nwhere bumping one control breaks the row, so it was correctly not adopted.\n\n`sm` exists now so a badge can sit in a small row without the row growing.\n\n## A ring, not a fill\n\ntone=\"inherit\" used color-mix(currentColor 15%, transparent) — which is exactly\nwhat both members hand-rolled, so adopting it was not a regression. It was\nstandardising a defect: 4.01:1 on a primary button, 3.97:1 on a destructive one,\nboth under the 4.5 floor.\n\nThe mechanism is worth stating because it will recur: the tint mixes toward\nTRANSPARENT, so it always lands between the text and the ground, and costs roughly\n23% of the control''s own text contrast. A ring leaves the ground alone, so the\nnumber keeps whatever contrast the button already earned.\n\nSame fix and same reason as the gallery''s classification-tree count slot, which\nwent 3.68 to 5.47 by replacing a color-mix fill with a currentColor ring. Second\nsighting of one mechanism; recorded in the component so there is not a third.\n\nA test asserts the rule contains no color-mix, because \"we used a ring\" is not\nsomething a screenshot distinguishes from a very faint fill.\n\n64 tests pass, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"370c0b626c4043e475b982b127b74aa66cfa37af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/370c0b626c4043e475b982b127b74aa66cfa37af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGU5YzMxMWY3OTExYjk2NGMwMTJiOGE2YzU4YTc3YzQ4YTE2YzM4MTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773","sha":"49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773"}],"sha":"e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e9c311f7911b964c012b8a6c58a77c48a16c3814"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:52:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:52:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(four members): DisclosureRow — and two controls announcing contradictory contracts\n\nFour members onto DisclosureRow or, where it did not fit, repaired in place. 45\nnew tests. All member gates flat.\n\n## The defect that appeared twice, independently\n\nA control carrying BOTH aria-pressed and aria-expanded. org-workbench''s person row\nand search-results'' card both passed aria-expanded into a SelectWrapper, which\nhard-renders aria-pressed before its rest spread — so one button announced two\ncontradictory contracts at once.\n\nsearch-results was worse: TWO separate controls both claimed to disclose the same\nregion, and neither carried aria-controls, because the card body had no id at all.\n\n## aria-controls pointing at nothing\n\norg-workbench''s aria-controls was unconditional while the id it named lived inside\ntwo nested {#if} blocks — so collapsed, AND open-but-empty, both pointed a screen\nreader at an element that was not in the document.\n\nresponse-reviewer''s manual-URL disclosure renders once per corpus row, so a\nhand-rolled aria-controls would have needed a per-row id. The component mints one\nper instance, which is why that problem disappears rather than being solved N\ntimes. That member now hand-rolls aria-expanded zero times, down from two.\n\n## Chevrons inside accessible names\n\nThree members read their glyph aloud — \"▾ People 2\", \"▾ Investors 1 variant, 2\ngens\", \"▸ snippet\". The component''s chevron is an aria-hidden SVG.\n\n## record-collector''s holdouts are resolved by their own prediction\n\nIts 2026-09-13 comment said both heads stayed raw because the disclosure organ did\nnot exist. It does now. The archive head measured 27px and cleared the 24px floor\nby three pixels purely because padding: 0.3rem added up; it now declares\n--control-h-md, verified present in the built bundle. Seven CSS rule-sets deleted,\n121 lines out against 102 in.\n\n## And one member correctly refused\n\nsort-filter-lens''s picker is a popup trigger over an absolutely-positioned\nlistbox. A row there needs rung-4 overrides for display, inline-size and padding —\nwhich negates the base recipe, so it is not a DisclosureRow. Left as a Button, and\nthree real defects fixed anyway: no aria-haspopup, no aria-controls, and the\nglyphs in the accessible name.\n\nThat also surfaced an inconsistency INSIDE the federation: shell''s\nWorkspaceSwitcher is the same shape and already declares aria-haspopup=\"listbox\".\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d0c0522ccc0e82216bb54e2ac91cc356312da0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/7d0c0522ccc0e82216bb54e2ac91cc356312da0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDQ5ZDc3YmM2NjgxMWJiMGI0MTc5NmVmZGY2Y2QxNmY3MTczMTk3NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2","sha":"bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2"}],"sha":"49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/49d77bc66811bb0b41796efdf6cd16f717319773"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:52:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:52:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): a vacuous DisclosureRow test, and a rest spread on the wrong element\n\nTwo defects an adopter found, and the first is the more embarrassing.\n\n## My test could not fail\n\n`expect(getComputedStyle(b).minBlockSize).not.toBe(''0px'')` — jsdom returns '''' for\nthat property on EVERY element, so the assertion passed unconditionally. A vacuous\nassertion is worse than no assertion, because it reads as coverage. It was\nasserting the one claim that matters: that the 24px floor is DECLARED rather than\nreached by luck, which is exactly how one member''s disclosure hit 27px — its\n0.3rem padding happened to add up.\n\nTwo dead ends before a real version, both recorded in the test so nobody repeats\nthem: document.styleSheets is also empty here, because the plugin does not inject\ncomponent CSS into the test document; and `new URL(..., import.meta.url)` throws\nunder vitest, which rewrites import.meta.url to a non-file scheme. The assertion\nnow reads the component source from the config root.\n\n## {...rest} landed on the wrapper\n\nA member passing any `aria-*` had it silently attached to the wrapper div rather\nthan the button it was meant to describe. The attribute existed, on the wrong\nelement, and nothing warned. It lands on the button now; layout hooks go through\n`wrapperProps`.\n\n## And a ruling, rather than a new organ\n\nTwo members have a card row that discloses, and the adopter asked for a decision.\nComposing DisclosureRow INSIDE CardRow is fine and is the answer: the card owns\nthe surface, the disclosure owns the control.\n\nWhat is NOT fine — and what both members were actually doing — is a SelectWrapper\non the same element, because those hard-render aria-pressed. A control carrying\nboth aria-pressed and aria-expanded claims two contradictory contracts at once.\nThat is the defect; the nesting was never the problem.\n\n62 tests pass, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"98d6300ee0663a4e037f95a945fab38fbfa7cd68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/98d6300ee0663a4e037f95a945fab38fbfa7cd68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGJjMDY1ZmYzZTYwNWIwOWFlMzlkODZlOWM0NjJmODhmY2ZkNzlmZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc","sha":"df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc"}],"sha":"bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bc065ff3e605b09ae39d86e9c462f88fcfd79ff2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:44:26Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:44:26Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): the popdown listbox was a half-built variant, and Button would not hand over its node\n\nFour findings from one sweep, and they are one issue: Selector--Listbox''s own\nheader directs popdowns with a selected state to it, and only Selector--Menu could\nactually do the popdown job.\n\n## Selector--Listbox gains the three props Menu already had\n\nautofocus. A popdown that opens with focus still on the trigger has a keyboard\nhandler nobody can reach. This is the THIRD sighting — the Menu''s header already\nrecords two adopters hand-rolling it before the prop existed — and this\nengineer deliberately did not write a fourth copy. Off by default here, unlike\nMenu, because a listbox is often always-present rather than opened, and stealing\nfocus on mount would be wrong.\n\nonclose and trigger. Escape now closes and returns focus, carrying both scars from\nMenu verbatim: capture the trigger BEFORE calling onclose, because it is a live\ngetter a member usually clears; and claim the one-shot BEFORE releasing focus,\nbecause an attachment that has not yet run will steal it back a tick later.\n\norientation. The handler already treated ArrowLeft/Right as equivalent to Up/Down,\nso the component was half-aware of horizontal and then refused to DRAW it. One\nadopter spent this rollout''s only rung-4 escape on a style= flex-direction plus a\nhand-written aria-orientation — which the loop says means the API is wrong. One\nprop now sets both.\n\n## Button hands over its node\n\n{...rest} cannot carry an element, so a member opening a popup from a shared\nButton had no way to pass it as the popup''s trigger. Two members independently\nwrapped the Button in a span and querySelector(''button'')-ed it back out — the same\ntwo-copies threshold that justifies promoting anything here.\n\nref receives the real node. A test asserts it is the actual button AND that `ref`\ndoes not leak onto the element as an attribute, which is what would have happened\nhad it stayed in the rest spread. It nearly did: the first attempt declared the\nprop without destructuring it.\n\nSeven new tests, 62 passing. svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf3016b9bee1ba8d8602fe6e41399c5eff2b76dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/bf3016b9bee1ba8d8602fe6e41399c5eff2b76dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGRmMDRkMTYyMjllMzUwYzIxZjNkZTEyZTYzYjEwZGJlMTg5MTk3Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3","sha":"aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3"}],"sha":"df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/df04d16229e350c21f3de12e63b10dbe189197cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:42:08Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:42:08Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(chat, sort-filter-lens, search-and-add): Selector, tests first — and two reds that were wrong\n\nThree members, 29 new tests, all three member gates flat. Composite roles with\nwrong or absent children: 3 -> 0. Tab stops per widget: 5/3/4 -> 1/1/1. Escape\nreturns focus to its trigger in 2 of 2 popups, up from 0.\n\n## Two red phases were wrong, and catching that IS the loop working\n\nchat''s first red asserted six menuitems against a five-command registry, and three\ntests failed on the arithmetic rather than on chat''s keyboard. The tell was\n\"expected to be undefined\" — index five did not exist.\n\nsort-filter-lens''s first red CRASHED in its own setup: the helpers queried\n[role=\"option\"], which the shipping markup does not have, so focus() threw before\na key was ever pressed. A test that dies in setup describes the setup, not the\ndefect.\n\nBoth were fixed before the member was touched, which is exactly what the loop''s\nred-phase decision node is for. The rewrite uses a row accessor matching BOTH the\nshipping and target markup, so the failure is \"the key moved nothing\" — the actual\ndefect.\n\n## What the right reds found\n\nchat: role=\"menu\" whose two element children were a headless div and a ul of\nlistitems. The brief said one menuitem from the static source; at runtime it\nrenders five and they were fine. The defect was one level up — the menu owned no\nmenu items at all. Escape worked via a document handler but dropped focus to body.\n\nsort-filter-lens: role=\"menu\" with ZERO menuitems, because its children were\nshared Buttons which carry no role. Selection was aria-current plus a variant\nchange, so zero aria-selected. And there was no Escape handler anywhere — the\npopover could not be dismissed from the keyboard at all.\n\nsearch-and-add: { radiogroups: 1, radios: 0 }, the whole defect as one executable\nclaim.\n\n## The radiogroup was not converted to radios, deliberately\n\nFour reasons, recorded in the member: no form, no name, no submit, so it is not a\nform value; \"auto\" is a behavioural default rather than a value; a thing with a\nselected state is a listbox; and a real radio group is an actual HAZARD in a\nfederated remote, because two mounted copies of the member would share one group\nname and merge into a single group. So no Selector--Radio was requested, and one\nsighting would not have justified it.\n\n## Deletions worth naming\n\nchat dropped a :focus-visible { outline: none } that was SUPPRESSING THE FEDERAL\nFOCUS RING and substituting a background change, plus the .command-row holdout\nwhose own comment named this as the Selector organ — resolved in place.\n\nsearch-and-add dropped .saa-chip.active, which encoded selection in a class no\nscreen reader could hear, and an opacity: 0.35 standing in for a disabled state.\n\nsort-filter-lens deleted no CSS at all: its popover already composed shared\nButtons, so its defect was purely semantic.\n\ngh issues #108, #109, #110.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"750c84474e11c78297d834b86472c6201c4a279b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/750c84474e11c78297d834b86472c6201c4a279b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGFhNzM0MWMwYTg1NWJiOWZmNTZlOTQxMTA3M2FlMGNkYjVhN2E4ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb","sha":"37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb"}],"sha":"aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/aa7341c0a855bb9ff56e9411073ae0cdb5a7a8f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:37:08Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:37:08Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"issue(context-v): a component test whose fixture was simpler than its call sites\n\nSelector--Menu exists so a popup returns focus to its trigger instead of dropping\nit to body. Two tests asserted it, both passed, and both of its first two adopters\nwere broken in exactly that way.\n\nThe fixture''s trigger was a local const the member could not touch. The realistic\ncall site nulls its anchor on close, because that is what closing a menu means —\nand trigger is a live getter read after onclose has already run.\n\nThe test was CORRECT ABOUT WHAT IT ASSERTED. It asserted that focus returns to a\ntrigger that still exists, and no adopter has one. The test and the realistic call\nsite disagreed, and the test won.\n\nThe general form, which is the reason this is a context-v file rather than only a\ncommit message: a fixture simpler than every real call site does not test the\ncomponent, it tests the fixture. And the tell was available before the adopters\nfound it — the fixture did the one thing no member would do.\n\nAlso records the two follow-on defects, each revealed only by fixing the one\nbefore it, and the observation that fixing a focus bug is how you find the next\nfocus bug.\n\nAnd one thing that is not fixed: gh issue create was denied by the permission\nclassifier for the subagent, so step 3 of the loop did not happen for either\nmember. Either the loop stops promising a gh issue from a subagent or subagents\nget a Bash rule. Operator''s call, flagged rather than silently dropped.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee57dfa75fa1dc59379e4dcb92055c79b5d91dbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/ee57dfa75fa1dc59379e4dcb92055c79b5d91dbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDM3YjdlM2FiNjdmMDA2NjAzNmQ4OTAyODdlNzM4YTdlMGZlYzZiYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b","sha":"8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b"}],"sha":"37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/37b7e3ab67f0066036d890287e738a7e0fec6bbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:36:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:36:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(response-reviewer, pack-runner): Selector--Menu in the ConnectorPalette twin, tests first\n\nBoth members onto Selector--Menu. Thirteen tests each, eight of which failed\nfirst — and not one failed because the component was missing.\n\nThe red phase, verbatim failures, each naming the defect that was shipping:\n\n  role=\"menu\" with zero menuitem children   expected [] to have length 4\n  disabled was a dim, not a state           expected undefined to be ''true''\n  three tab stops, not one                  expected length 1, found 3\n  the ArrowDown that moves nothing          activeElement never left row 0\n  Escape does nothing                       expected <div> to be null\n  focus stranded in a popup                 expected menu-item to be connector-chip\n\nOne test deliberately does not assert what jsdom would allow: Enter on a focused\nbutton DOES fire a click in a real browser, so \"Enter does not activate\" would\nhave been a fake defect. It asserts focus moved first, and fails there.\n\nAnd the row accessor matches BOTH shapes — [role=\"menuitem\"], button.palette-menu-item\n— so the same selector sees old markup and new. A test that could only see one\nshape would have failed because the component was absent, which is the failure the\nloop warns about.\n\n## The verdict, decided from the code\n\nSelector--Menu, both. The popup fires a one-shot override for this invocation;\nnothing is marked current, nothing persists, and preferred_connectors is a chain\nthe backend walks rather than a user selection. That is a list of ACTIONS.\n\nrole=\"menu\" moved off a wrapper that held a header div, a ul and a footer div — a\ncontainer role over children that were not menuitems at all — onto the component,\nover real menuitems. The header and footer stay outside the widget, where they\nbelong: they are labels, not actions. The ul went too; a list announced inside a\nmenu was wrong regardless.\n\nZero rung 4 in either member. The item snippet was exactly the seam this shape\nneeded, and the HOLDOUT comment sitting in pack-runner since yesterday — \"this is\nthe Selector organ of D4, not CardRow\" — turned out to be right.\n\n## The twin is not identical, and DESIGN.md is wrong about it\n\nDESIGN.md:1029 lists ConnectorPalette.svelte as byte-identical across the two.\nThat was already false before this migration: response-reviewer renders its status\nbadges as raw spans while pack-runner uses Chip, only one carries the\n.palette-menu-status CSS, and only one carries a font/color compensation for a\ndeleted bare-button rule.\n\nThe Selector question did NOT diverge them — same organ, same snippet, same\ntrigger wiring, same CSS deletions, byte-identical assertions. Recommendation is\nto call them a CONTRACT twin rather than a byte twin, with the status-badge\nrendering named as the open divergence for the Chip sweep to close.\n\nMember gates flat at 9 and 5. CSS blocks 101 -> 77 and 89 -> 73 lines.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd6c03c247b2d0adaa415c4240587d11b2272eda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/dd6c03c247b2d0adaa415c4240587d11b2272eda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhkMTZhYTI1MjJhMGZmMGU4NmZkYWFhMDBlNDE1M2QxYmQ5NmIzOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4","sha":"9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4"}],"sha":"8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d16aa2522a0ff0e86fdaaa00e4153d1bd96b38b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:36:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:36:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): Selector--Menu broke its own headline promise three ways\n\nThe component''s header says it exists so a popup returns focus to its trigger\nrather than dropping it to <body>. The first two adopters both hit exactly that\nfailure. Three separate causes, found in sequence, each revealed by fixing the\none before it.\n\n## 1. `trigger` is a live getter, read after onclose had cleared it\n\n`trigger` is a Svelte prop, so it is read at the moment of the call — and the\nhandler read it AFTER `onclose?.()`. Both adopters did the obvious thing and\nnulled their menu anchor inside `onclose`, so the component read `undefined` one\nline later and focus went to body.\n\nCaptured into a local before calling onclose.\n\n**The component''s own test could not see this**, because its fixture trigger was a\nlocal `const` the member could not touch. The test and the realistic call site\ndisagreed and the test won — so that test is rewritten to use a getter-backed\ntrigger that `onclose` clears, which is what a real adopter does.\n\n## 2. No focus-on-open, so both adopters hand-rolled the same seven lines\n\nA popup whose keydown handler is on the menu, opened with focus still on the\ntrigger, has a widget whose entire keyboard is unreachable. Two independent copies\nof the same `querySelector` on the first two call sites is the same tell that\njustified building this component at all.\n\n`autofocus` now, on by default.\n\n## 3. Which immediately broke the fix from 1\n\nAn attachment re-runs on every update, and an unguarded `focus()` in one stole\nfocus BACK from the trigger a tick after Escape had correctly returned it. So the\ncomponent defeated its own promise on the update rather than the keypress.\n\nA one-shot flag was not enough either: a member can close the menu before the\nattachment has run even once, and the attachment then fires afterwards, sees the\nflag unset, and pulls focus out of the trigger. The guard now means \"focus has\nbeen placed\", not \"the attachment has run\" — Escape claims it before releasing.\n\nThat third bug existed only because of the second fix, and was visible only\nbecause of the first. Worth the note: fixing a focus bug is how you find the next\nfocus bug.\n\n55 tests pass, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8987d1302289388f28566d5ef24ae16b1e04a54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/c8987d1302289388f28566d5ef24ae16b1e04a54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDljMWE5YzE4NDRhOWMxYWEwY2Y2OWZhN2YzNTg1ZTE2MjNlODRhZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f","sha":"851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f"}],"sha":"9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/9c1a9c1844a9c1aa0cf69fa7f3585e1623e84ad4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:30:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:30:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): DisclosureRow''s state initializer captured only the first value\n\nlet internal = $state(openProp ?? false) reads the prop ONCE. Svelte warns about\nit, and the real consequence is worse than the warning: a controlled row whose\nparent changed `open` after mount would desync — the attribute and the panel are\ndriven by one derived, so they would agree with each other and both be wrong.\n\ninternal starts false instead. When `open` is passed the component is controlled\nand internal is unused; when it is not, internal IS the state.\n\nCaught by svelte-check going 0 warnings to 1 and looking, which is the same check\nthat caught the pruned :has() rule in CardRow.\n\n55 tests still green.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95f100f758ddaf68bc4942214b869e397f09ae3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/95f100f758ddaf68bc4942214b869e397f09ae3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDg1MTQxMGEwODk1ZjVjMWZjNTkwMWFlODA1OGY2OTE3Y2NiZjhjMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a","sha":"7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a"}],"sha":"851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/851410a0895f5c1fc5901ae8058f6917ccbf8c1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:30:28Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:30:28Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): DisclosureRow, StatusIndicator, CountBadge — 55 tests green\n\nThree more organs, each sized by counting sightings rather than by the docs''\nclaims. One of those claims was wrong and is corrected below.\n\n## DisclosureRow — eight members hand-roll this\n\nNot a selection and not a CardRow. A disclosure toggles a region; it does not\nchoose anything. Both SelectWrapper variants hard-render aria-pressed, which is\nthe toggle-BUTTON contract, so adopting one announces the wrong thing — the same\nclass of error as nine surfaces declaring role=\"menu\" with no arrow keys.\n\nThree things every hand-roll gets wrong, and none of them is visible:\n\naria-expanded tracking the INTENT rather than the state. If the panel renders\nconditionally and the attribute comes from a separate variable, they drift and a\nscreen reader is told the opposite of what is on screen. Here one $state drives\nboth, so they cannot disagree.\n\naria-controls pointing at an id that does not exist while collapsed. A test\nasserts the target is really in the document.\n\nEnter and Space not toggling, because someone used a div with onclick. This is a\nreal button, so the browser handles both for free.\n\nAnd the target floor is a contract rather than luck: one member''s archive\ndisclosure measured 27px and cleared 24 only because its 0.3rem padding happened\nto add up.\n\n## StatusIndicator — and the count in the docs was wrong\n\nThe plan said sixteen units observe connection_status. Measured: THREE render it.\nRecorded because an inflated number is how an organ gets built for a population\nthat does not exist.\n\nThe finding still stands and is the component: three members drew it\nbyte-for-byte the same wrong way, independently, with no shared code — five\nstates rendered as three appearances, with connecting and auth_required sharing\none undifferentiated grey. A user could not tell a dropped socket from a handshake\nin progress.\n\nauth_required is warn, not error, and that is the distinction every member lost:\nit is a gate the operator can walk through, not a failure.\n\nNever colour alone. The dot is aria-hidden and the word always renders — a live\n1.4.1 defect in one member where the only signal an agent was running was a\npulsing dot, and theme.css''s reduced-motion block sets iteration-count to 1, so\nfor a reduced-motion user it pulsed once and then meant nothing.\n\nSeven tests assert the mapping, one asserts every state renders a DISTINCT word,\nand one asserts connecting and auth_required cannot collapse to the same tone.\n\n## CountBadge — the organ that is deliberately not a Chip\n\n~28 sightings under seven class names. The difference from Chip is one line: this\nINHERITS the host control''s colour by default. pack-runner and response-reviewer\nboth hand-rolled color-mix(currentColor 15%) for exactly that reason, and putting\na Chip there would have painted muted text on an accent fill and erased the\nselected-state cue on a whole filter row.\n\nmax exists because a count is an at-a-glance signal and 1,982 is not one. Over the\ncap it renders 999+ and keeps the true number in the accessible name and the\ntitle, so nothing is lost.\n\n55 tests pass, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify. Nothing consumes these\nyet.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"29c85e0f5364fd2292dd2864d8d2f753f3dd1117","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/29c85e0f5364fd2292dd2864d8d2f753f3dd1117"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDcyOTBkMjE4OWQxNDQ2Njg1OTlhY2RkMjgyMzFjNmJkODAwMGU0MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f","sha":"58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f"}],"sha":"7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/7290d2189d144668599acdd28231c6bd8000e40a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:20:31Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:20:31Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): Selector--Menu and MenuItem — actions, not choices\n\nThe sibling of Selector--Listbox on the what-you-click axis, and the distinction\nis not cosmetic: a menu has NO SELECTED STATE. Its children are menuitem, never\noption, and they carry neither aria-selected nor aria-checked.\n\nTwo members in this federation currently ship role=\"menu\" with no menuitem\nchildren at all, which a screen reader announces as a structurally broken widget.\nA test now asserts the absence of selected state directly, because \"we did not add\naria-selected\" is not something a screenshot can show.\n\nFifteen tests, written before the components. 32 passing across both Selectors.\n\n## Escape returns focus to the trigger, and it is tested\n\nA popup that closes and drops focus to <body> is worse than one that never opened:\nthe user''s place in the document is gone and a screen reader starts over. The\ncomponent takes the trigger element and focuses it BEFORE the member unmounts —\nreturning focus after the menu is gone is exactly how focus lands on body.\n\nTwo tests cover it: one asserts focus lands on the trigger, the other asserts it\nis not body. The second looks redundant and is not — it is the failure mode, named\nso a future refactor that satisfies the first by accident still fails the second.\n\n## The split\n\nMenuItem is appearance only; Selector--Menu owns the keyboard. Same division as\nListContainer and CardRow. An item handling its own keydown would give the widget\nN tab stops, which is the defect the Selector exists to replace, so the reason is\nwritten above the markup rather than assumed.\n\ndanger sets data-danger rather than only a colour. A destructive action\ndistinguished by hue alone is WCAG 1.4.1, and a data attribute is something a\nmember — and a test — can read.\n\n## Carried forward from the listbox\n\nThe container comes from the event''s currentTarget, not bind:this. That binding\nwas never assigned in the first Selector and made an entire keyboard silently do\nnothing while rendering perfectly. The comment says so, in both components, so the\nnext one does not rediscover it.\n\n32 of 32 tests pass, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"58d75f32a8d3a57b421a3da16cd115d19356d900","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/58d75f32a8d3a57b421a3da16cd115d19356d900"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDU4MTA0YTA0NGFjOTQxOWJjMjJlMWQ1YTNiM2VhMjNkZjllN2FkN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423","sha":"2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423"}],"sha":"58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/58104a044ac9419bc22e1d5a3b3ea23df9e7ad7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:18:42Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:18:42Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"loop(context-v): adopt Selector in one member, with the chart\n\nThe house convention for a process loop is a mermaid flowchart, and the three\nadoption loops I wrote skipped it. This one has it.\n\nWhat the chart encodes that prose kept burying: the RED phase has its own decision\nnode. Write a failing test, then ask whether it fails FOR THE RIGHT REASON — a\ntest that fails because the component is missing is not the test. It has to fail\nagainst the member''s current markup, describing the defect that is shipping today:\nthe ArrowDown that moves nothing, the option with no tabindex=-1, the role=menu\nwith no menuitem children.\n\nThat step is the one people get wrong, so it gets its own section as well as its\nown node. A refactor with no red phase produces a green test and proves nothing,\nand proving the nine surfaces are genuinely broken rather than merely undocumented\nis half the point of the sweep.\n\nThe loop also states what NOT to adopt, which the previous three learned the hard\nway: a combobox is a third organ and should be raised rather than forced, and a\nplain list of buttons with no role is not broken — it is a list of buttons. Only\nadopt where a composite role is already declared.\n\nEverything mechanical is inherited from the Button loop rather than forked, as the\nChip and CardRow loops already do.\n\nRefs #101 #107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2382d67f3ccd1db62e038387649d4c6c489c21d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/2382d67f3ccd1db62e038387649d4c6c489c21d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDJmYmZhMDVhYmQ0NGI3ODg2NmU1NWIwMDVlMDBiNjgzNGRlMjY0MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3","sha":"fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3"}],"sha":"2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2fbfa05abd44b78866e55b005e00b6834de26423"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:10:17Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:10:17Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): Selector--Listbox, and the federation''s first component test\n\nNine surfaces across seven members declare role=\"menu\", role=\"listbox\" or\nrole=\"radiogroup\". Not one implements arrow-key navigation. Two declare\nrole=\"menu\" with no menuitem children; one declares role=\"radiogroup\" containing\nno radios. Every one of those roles is a promise to a screen-reader user — this is\na widget you navigate with arrows and Tab takes you out of it — and all nine\ndeliver a plain list of tab stops instead.\n\nSeven members got it wrong independently. The roving-tabindex contract IS the\nsubstance of this organ.\n\n## Tests first, and they had to come first\n\nButton, Chip and CardRow are appearance with a little behaviour, so a probe\nscreenshot catches their defects. This is behaviour with a little appearance: a\ndefect here looks like NOTHING HAPPENING, which no screenshot shows. The three\nprevious primitives each shipped with a defect that rendered perfectly — one made\nits button unfocusable and passed every gate.\n\nSo seventeen tests were written before the component existed, each one a line of\nthe WAI-ARIA authoring practices: one tab stop not N, arrows move the active\noption and focus follows, Home and End, typeahead, Enter and Space activate, click\nstill works, disabled options are skipped and never hold the tab stop, and the\nrole triad is consistent.\n\nThey failed, then the component made them pass. That is also the only way to prove\nthe nine surfaces are genuinely broken rather than merely undocumented.\n\n## Three things the red phase taught, all of which would have shipped silently\n\nThe vitest config copied from the one working precedent is WRONG for component\ntests. Without resolve.conditions: [''browser''], Svelte resolves to its SERVER\nbuild and mount() throws lifecycle_function_unavailable, so every test fails\nbefore asserting anything. apps/corpora-curator never hit it because its tests are\nlogic-only — this is the federation''s first component test, and the precedent did\nnot cover it.\n\nbind:this was never assigned, so the focus call was a no-op against undefined and\narrows did nothing at all. Caught only because a test asserted document.activeElement;\na screenshot of this component would look perfect. The container now comes from\nthe event''s currentTarget — the handler is on the listbox, so there is nothing to\ngo stale and nothing to be undefined on the first keypress.\n\nAnd focus is SYNCHRONOUS on purpose. A deferred focus() is a frame in which the\nwidget has an active option that nothing is focused on, and assistive tech reads\nthe gap. Only the tabindex attribute waits for Svelte''s flush, which is fine\nbecause focus does not depend on it.\n\n## Decisions recorded in the component\n\nWrapping is a decision made once: arrowing past the end returns to the start,\nbecause every member that hand-rolled anything here wrapped, and the alternative\nstrands a keyboard user at a boundary with no feedback.\n\nThe a11y warning about a click handler with no keydown is suppressed WITH ITS\nREASON: the keyboard handler is on the listbox, not the option, because that is\nwhat a composite widget is. Putting a keydown on each option would give the widget\nN tab stops — exactly the defect this replaces.\n\nNo Selector--Radio. Zero radios in the federation, and shipping ahead of consumers\nis how the federal layer got a spacing scale with no adopters.\n\n17 of 17 tests pass, svelte-check clean, 22 of 22 units verify.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4171546b06bc976b4082a15a0932380b14aa20f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/f4171546b06bc976b4082a15a0932380b14aa20f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGZiNDAzNzU5MDU4ZTE5MTgxNmQ3MWE2NDZmNTA3ZGE1NzkxYjM4ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764","sha":"40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764"}],"sha":"fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/fb403759058e191816d71a646f507da5791b38e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:05:30Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:05:30Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"plan(context-v): build Selector and close the keyboard contract\n\nNine surfaces across seven members declare role=menu, role=listbox or\nrole=radiogroup. Not one implements arrow-key navigation. Two declare role=menu\nwith no menuitem children at all; one declares role=radiogroup containing no\nradios, which a screen reader announces as a structurally broken widget.\n\nEach of those roles is a PROMISE — this is a widget you navigate with arrows and\nTab will take you out of it — and all nine deliver a list of tab stops instead.\nSeven members got it wrong independently, which is the tell: the roving-tabindex\ncontract is the substance of the organ and nobody should be hand-rolling it seven\ntimes.\n\nThe plan''s argument is that this component is different in kind from the first\nthree. Button, Chip and CardRow are appearance with a little behaviour; Selector\nis behaviour with a little appearance. So a defect here does not look like wrong\npixels, it looks like NOTHING HAPPENING — which a probe screenshot cannot catch.\n\nThat is why this is the first component with real tests, and why the operator''s\nloop puts a FAILING TEST BEFORE THE REFACTOR. Every previous sweep measured after\nthe change and inferred the defect. This one states the defect as an executable\nclaim before touching anything, which is also the only way to prove the nine\nsurfaces are genuinely broken rather than merely undocumented.\n\nThe contract is seven lines from the WAI-ARIA authoring practices, each one a\nfailing test first. Three variants on the what-you-click axis, of which Radio is\nNOT built — zero sightings, and shipping ahead of consumers is how the federal\nlayer got a spacing scale with no adopters.\n\nOrder puts shell last, because it hosts every remote and three of the nine\nsurfaces are its own chrome, so a regression there is a regression in all twenty\nmembers at once. The two ConnectorPalette copies go first, because they are a\ndeclared converged twin already diverging and whatever is decided applies to both.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f44a0d3c285e9e94263f45278588e3cdbee2e1fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/f44a0d3c285e9e94263f45278588e3cdbee2e1fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDQwZmMxMWFiMzViMDQ2MDcxOTUwNDdkZmNhNzExNjVjODdjOGM3NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686","sha":"de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686"}],"sha":"40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/40fc11ab35b04607195047dfca71165c87c8c764"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:31:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:31:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): context-passing shipped and is unexercised — recorded rather than claimed\n\nListContainer publishes direction and CardRow reads it. Across eight adopting\nmembers it removed the prop from ZERO call sites.\n\nThree still name direction=\"column\" explicitly and an explicit prop wins, so\ncontext changed nothing for them. Every other call site omits it — but\nlayout=\"list\" publishes row, which is already CardRow''s own default, so the\ncontext read is a no-op reproducing the fallback.\n\nIt pays off only at layout=\"grid\", and exactly one member in the federation has a\ngrid list. The 280px-track experiment that motivated the whole mechanism lives in\na member shape that four of four pilots do not have.\n\nSo it is correct AND premature. It costs a getContext in the most-instantiated\ncomponent in the federation and buys one call site today. Left in place because\nthe one grid adopter genuinely works and removing it would re-open a decision\nnothing is pressing — but recorded as not-yet-justified rather than filed as a\nwin, because the temptation to read \"no call site passes direction\" as success is\nexactly the error worth naming.\n\nThe pattern, which generalises: A MECHANISM THAT REPRODUCES THE DEFAULT IT\nREPLACED IS INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM NO MECHANISM. The way to tell is to count call\nsites that actually CHANGED, not call sites that now omit a prop.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba84c9e4a6ac13fbb62267a898285ba61bef06f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/ba84c9e4a6ac13fbb62267a898285ba61bef06f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGRlNjUzMmNkMDUxMzBhMjNmYzU4NTgyMDQ2MTc3MThiMmU3OWQ2ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961","sha":"cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961"}],"sha":"de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/de6532cd05130a23fc5858204617718b2e79d686"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:31:31Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:31:31Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): ListContainer gains a header divider, and its sticky background was transparent\n\nTwo gaps from the second sweep, and the second one is my own fix reintroducing the\nbug it fixed.\n\n## The divider\n\nThree of four members had a hairline under their list header, deleted it along\nwith their own header recipe, and had no way to get it back — class= lands on the\nrows element, not the header. So the sweep''s cost included three dividers that\nsimply vanished.\n\nheaderDivider draws it, and draws it with --color-border-strong: all three\noriginals used --color-border at roughly 1.26:1, under the non-text floor, so the\nones that come back are the first ones that pass.\n\n## The sticky background, which I broke twice in opposite directions\n\nThe header originally hardcoded background: --color-background, which painted a\nnear-black strip inside any --color-surface panel. I fixed that by making the\npinned case background: inherit.\n\nBut .ui-listcontainer declares no background, so inherit resolves to TRANSPARENT —\nand content scrolled visibly through the pinned header. The fix for the\nhardcoded-background bug reintroduced the same symptom by a different route, and\nonly showed up because a member actually tried to pin a header.\n\nNow --ui-list-header-bg with --color-surface as the fallback: the panel most lists\nsit on, overridable by a custom property when yours is not.\n\n## And a note that should stop most people needing sticky at all\n\nThe rows element is already the scroll container, so a header placed outside it is\npinned STRUCTURALLY. The member that hit the transparency bug went on to make its\nrows region scroll instead and deleted the sticky entirely — which is the better\npattern and the one this layout is shaped for. sticky is for a header whose\nscrolling ancestor is somewhere else. That is now written above the rule, so the\nnext member meets the question before the property.\n\n22 of 22 units verify clean.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ef775afa3e6f1a4f98eeb9d6b6194fead864ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/3ef775afa3e6f1a4f98eeb9d6b6194fead864ea3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGNkZDJjZmNkMWMzZjhhODA5OTliYTEyMDFlM2E1MWUxZDMyZDg5NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74","sha":"7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74"}],"sha":"cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cdd2cfcd1c3f8a80999ba1201e3a51e1d32d8961"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:30:15Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:30:15Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(four members): ListContainer — 32 more spacing literals gone, and the context mechanism is unexercised\n\nTen ListContainer call sites across twelve list regions. 32 raw spacing literals\ndeleted (180 -> 148), 91 layout declarations removed against 27 added, 17\nrule-sets gone. Zero rung 4 anywhere in the sweep. One member gate improved 3 -> 2\nbecause a hex literal died with the header recipe it lived in.\n\nEleven named list landmarks where there were none. And two members gained real\nlist semantics by collapsing wrapper <li> elements into CardRow as=\"li\" — both\ncarried stale comments saying CardRow takes no `as`, which it now does.\n\n## The answer to the question I asked, and it is no\n\nContext-passing removed `direction` from ZERO call sites, in all four members.\n\nThree still name direction=\"column\" explicitly and an explicit prop wins, so\ncontext changed nothing for them. Every other call site omits it — but\nlayout=\"list\" publishes `row`, which is already CardRow''s own default, so the\ncontext read is a no-op reproducing the fallback.\n\nThe mechanism can only pay off at layout=\"grid\", and none of these four has a grid\nlist — grepped auto-fit and auto-fill across all four src trees, zero hits in any\nlist surface. Since 16 of 18 members are lists, the honest read is that\ncontext-passing is correct but currently unexercised, and the 280px-track evidence\nthat motivated it lives in a member shape four of four pilots do not have.\n\nIt costs a getContext in the most-instantiated component in the federation. I want\na grid adopter to justify it before it is called settled, and the decision doc now\nsays so rather than claiming a win.\n\n## What the sweep cost, stated\n\nThree boundaries drawn with --color-border at roughly 1.26:1 — under the non-text\nfloor — were removed along with the recipes that held them. None were added, and\nnone replaced: those dividers are simply gone, because the layout has no divider\naffordance. Three of four members wanted one. That is the next fix.\n\nTarget size did not move in either direction; every sub-24px control in all four\nmembers is pre-existing and untouched.\n\n## And the engineer re-cut its own work\n\nA parallel agent revised ListContainer mid-sweep — new gap scale, opt-in sticky, an\nempty snippet, maxBlockSize, a merging class. Rather than ship against the old\nAPI, it re-cut all ten call sites and re-ran every probe, so every number above is\npost-revision. Two findings it had already written up were resolved by that\nrevision and withdrawn, and maxBlockSize and empty each deleted a workaround it\nhad already built.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fab8790425310d6f8e18dc92dbe97e69b2de9800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/fab8790425310d6f8e18dc92dbe97e69b2de9800"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDdlYzE4ZWU4YmRiM2VmNjVkOWUxNDhmYjhiMzNjYzBjMjg3OTNlNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620","sha":"823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620"}],"sha":"7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/7ec18ee8bdb3ef65d9e148fb8b33cc0c28793e74"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:23:05Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:23:05Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(scripts): organ:census — because the BEM rollup could not see its own call sites\n\nThe house convention spells variants in BEM so that rg ''SelectWrapper--'' reads as\na live catalogue with no doc to maintain. It does not, and tonight showed two\nseparate reasons why.\n\nFirst: a Svelte tag must be a valid JS identifier, so the BEM name can never\nappear at a call site. rg on the BEM form found two imports against fourteen call\nsites — a sevenfold undercount.\n\nSecond, and this is the one I got wrong when I first corrected it: matching the\nIDENTIFIER is not the fix either, because the local name is whatever the importing\nmember chose. The same primitive is SelectWrapperClickBody in one member and\nSelectCheck in another. There is no single tag spelling to grep, and a census\nkeyed on one silently omits every member that picked a different alias.\n\nThe import path is canonical — it carries the BEM filename verbatim and cannot be\naliased. So the census resolves each file''s local name from its import, then\ncounts that name''s tags in that file.\n\n  organ                                 call sites  consuming units\n  Button                                       285               19\n  Chip                                         100               12\n  CardRow                                       50               16\n  ListContainer                                 31                8\n  SelectWrapper--ClickBody                      13                5\n  SelectWrapper--Checkbox                        6                4\n  SelectWrapper--ClickPrimary                    6                5\n  ConfidencePill                                 3                2\n  ToggleHeader__PromptOrPackage--Icons           1                1\n  TOTAL                                        495\n\nThe convention survives; it just has to be queried through the import rather than\nthe call site. The decision doc records the correction and the general form, which\nis worth more than the script: A NAMING CONVENTION IS ONLY A ROLLUP IF THE NAME\nSURVIVES TO THE PLACE YOU INTEND TO GREP. Check that before relying on it, because\nthe failure is silent and reads as a low number rather than an error.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9375f225ad4244b8f941d8ead8f83a330b8cbef0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/9375f225ad4244b8f941d8ead8f83a330b8cbef0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDgyM2EzYzU5NzIxMTM5MjY5YTJkNmUyZDc4NWVlOWU1ODE3ODE2MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2","sha":"03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2"}],"sha":"823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/823a3c59721139269a2d6e2d785ee9e581781620"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:21:35Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:21:35Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(three members): checkbox second pass — and my density diagnosis was incomplete\n\nThe two rung-0 workarounds come out now the component has its flex context, the\ndense table gets density=\"compact\", and labelProps carries the tooltip. Ten lines\nof member CSS deleted, still zero rung-4 across four members.\n\nTruncation is genuinely restored and it was PROVEN rather than assumed: at 1280px\nthe name fits, so the truncating flag reads false either way and proves nothing.\nThe engineer measured a second 320px-wide clone of the same row in the same page —\nscrollWidth 423 against clientWidth 177 with overflow hidden, so the ellipsis\nengages from the component alone with no member CSS behind it.\n\n## The correction worth keeping\n\ndensity=\"compact\" recovered 2px of the 10px row-height cost. My pass-1 finding\nblamed the label''s 4px floor, and that was incomplete: the label is INLINE-LEVEL,\nso a table cell whose only content is a checkbox still reserves leading for text\nit does not have. Testing line-height: 0 on the cell dropped the row by ~5.4px —\nmore than twice what the density prop was worth.\n\n  original 13x13 input                         34.7px\n  pass 1, comfortable                          44.7px   +28.8%\n  pass 2, compact + line-height: 0             38.3px   +10.4%\n\nSo the cost of the WCAG fix falls from +28.8% to +10.4%, and the +3.6px that\nremains is the honest price of a 24px control replacing a 13px one. The\nline-height fix is rung 0 in the member, because the column''s sole content is the\ncontrol and there is no text to damage — and it must NOT go in the component,\nwhere a label with children does need its leading.\n\n## labelProps solves attributes, not typography\n\nThe tooltip moved onto the label as intended. But the wrapper span it was supposed\nto retire stays, and the measurement is why: .ui-selectcheck declares\nfont: inherit and color: inherit on purpose, so a member class passed via class=\nties the component''s own scoped rule at (0,2,0) and loses on source order.\nMeasured, that silently promoted a muted 12px secondary option to 13px body text,\ndirectly under the primary Button it qualifies.\n\nThat is the component working as designed — only a PARENT can say \"this option is\nsecondary\" — so the wrapper is the ancestor that says it, and the reasoning is now\nin the markup, the CSS and the component header so nobody deletes it as dead\nweight.\n\n## And the narrowing is closed, in the right direction\n\nThe label went 1280px to 508.8px, and the visible sentence measures 476.8px. Every\npixel of visible text is inside the label, plus the box; what vanished was ~803px\nof blank row nobody could see. It is also the SAFER shape — a full-bleed label in\na multi-control row is exactly the stretch the component now warns is load-bearing\nnot to do.\n\nAll four member gates flat. 22 of 22 units verify clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"89851c4afa7217af452418ecea582ae0a84b919a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/89851c4afa7217af452418ecea582ae0a84b919a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDAzZjFkMDA5MDI5ZDk5MDIyZGFjOTE3OWZhNjg5ZmE0OWM4MmNjZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e","sha":"9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e"}],"sha":"03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/03f1d009029d99022dac9179fa689fa49c82ccf2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:20:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:20:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): ListContainer''s header slot had zero consumers, and four more defects\n\nNineteen call sites across four members adopted ListContainer and NOT ONE used the\nheader slot. Three independent blockers, all of them mine, all in the primitive.\n\n## The header\n\nIts background was hardcoded to --color-background. Three of the four members''\nlist surfaces sit on --color-surface panels, so adopting the slot painted a\nnear-black strip inside a mid-grey card — with no prop to change it and no\nreachable selector to override it, because member CSS lands at (0,1,0) against\nthe component''s hashed (0,2,0). A component that has to be fought is a missing\nprop.\n\nIt now paints NOTHING by default and inherits the surface it is placed on. Only a\npinned header needs to occlude what scrolls under it, so background: inherit moves\nto the sticky case.\n\nIts sticky was unconditional. position: sticky pins to the nearest SCROLLING\nancestor, so a list that is not its own scroll container pins its header to the\nVIEWPORT — every in-page list in the sweep would have glued a heading to the top\nof the page. Now opt-in via stickyHeader.\n\nAnd it was structurally incompatible with as=\"ul\" plus guarded lists: a member\nwhose header must survive loading, error and empty states could not use it,\nbecause the branch content is a <p> and that is not a valid <li>. There is an\n`empty` snippet now, rendered OUTSIDE the rows element, so a <p> is legal even\nunder as=\"ul\".\n\n## The gap names looked like the scale and were not the scale\n\nsm|md|lg mapped to --space-sm|-lg|-2xl, so gap=\"md\" silently gave --space-lg and\n--space-md was unreachable. A member reached for the same-sounding name and its\ngrid went from four tracks at 280.5px to three at 376px.\n\nNow the scale''s own seven names, mapping to themselves. Names that look like the\nscale must BE the scale — the alternative is a private remap nobody can predict\nfrom the token list they already know.\n\n## Two more, both silent\n\nclass was not merged — the spread followed the literal attribute, so\n<ListContainer class=\"x\"> REPLACED ui-listcontainer__rows outright and destroyed\nthe layout. CardRow merges; this did not. Now it does.\n\nAnd `label` was a lying attribute on as=\"div\": aria-label on a role-less div is\nnot exposed to assistive tech at all, and four of nineteen call sites were divs.\nA named div now gets role=\"list\" so the name is real, or no name is claimed.\n\n## One that made the ownership claim half true\n\nThe layout owned overflow-y: auto and exposed no height bound, so two members had\nto add a flex wrapper back just to keep their cap. It owned the scrolling while\nthe member still owned the bound. maxBlockSize closes it.\n\n22 of 22 units verify clean. Nothing consumes the new props yet, so this cannot\nbreak an adopter.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b89237b21013e5968c8133fcba6e8f72ae56f19c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/b89237b21013e5968c8133fcba6e8f72ae56f19c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDlhNzE2NzEzZGRkNWU3NWRhOWQxMTcxNjUwNDdiNmUwOWI2MzUwMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6","sha":"8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6"}],"sha":"9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/9a716713ddd5e75da9d117165047b6e09b63501e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:19:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:19:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(four members): ListContainer — twenty raw spacing literals gone, and the header slot nobody could use\n\nNineteen ListContainer call sites across four members. Twenty raw spacing literals\ndeleted, 227 -> 207. Zero rung-4 escapes. All four member gates flat.\n\nEvery deleted recipe was a list''s own list-style, margin, padding, display:flex or\ngrid, gap and overflow-y — exactly the set the layout now owns. And the three\nrung-0 wrappers that were added all use tokens, so the members gained\nvar(--space-*) uses where they previously had none. That is the layout issue''s\nlever working: spacing stops being hand-rolled when something owns it.\n\n## Context-passing was right for tiles, and the general claim needs narrowing\n\ndocs-portal went from CardRow direction=\"column\" to CardRow with no direction at\nall, inside ListContainer layout=\"grid\". Measured before and after: same rendered\nvalue, one fewer prop, and the equal-height stretch is now the container''s rather\nthan a grid default.\n\nBut there is a counter-example in-tree and it matters. records-surface has a\nFULL-WIDTH LIST ROW WHOSE CHILDREN STACK — direction=\"column\" inside\nlayout=\"list\", where context says row. The explicit prop stayed and correctly won,\nwhich proves the context-is-a-default design, and which also means D5''s claim that\ndirection is determined ENTIRELY by the container''s width holds for tiles and\nfails for that row. Amending the decision rather than the code.\n\n## The header slot has zero consumers, for three independent reasons\n\nWorth stating plainly because it is a design failure in the primitive rather than\na member problem.\n\nIts background is hardcoded to --color-background, and three of these four list\nsurfaces sit on --color-surface panels — so adopting the slot paints a near-black\nstrip inside a mid-grey card, with no prop to change it and no reachable selector\nto override it. A component that has to be fought is a missing prop.\n\nIts sticky is unconditional, so a header in a list that is not its own scroll\ncontainer pins to the VIEWPORT rather than the list. That is every in-page list\nhere.\n\nAnd it is structurally incompatible with as=\"ul\" plus guarded lists: a member whose\nheader must survive loading, error and empty states cannot use it, because the\nbranch content is a <p> and that is not a valid <li>.\n\nSo the controls-up-top half of the shape is currently undelivered. Fixes follow in\nthe next commit.\n\n## Honest gaps\n\norg-workbench has nine call sites and zero pixels seen — every list is behind a\nworkspace round trip. It typechecks, builds, and is structurally identical to the\nones that were driven, but nobody has looked at it. Stated rather than smoothed\nover.\n\nNineteen list regions gained accessible names; before, they were unnamed <ul>\nelements. No control was touched in the largest member, so no target-size or\ncontrast change is expected there — expected, not verified.\n\nZero checkbox adoptions: none of these four has a checkbox, and nothing was\ninvented.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bca530c4f57ec825b066a2c14bc0a8c75dbe31ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/bca530c4f57ec825b066a2c14bc0a8c75dbe31ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhkYWRlYzg4ODVjMmViYWEyNDBjYmQyNTY4Y2ZmOTA0ZTRhZTZjYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03","sha":"bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03"}],"sha":"8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8dadec8885c2ebaa240cbd2568cff904e4ae6cc6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:16:03Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:16:03Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): the checkbox variant''s non-stretch invariant, and a premise the sweep corrected\n\nTwo additions to D3 from SelectWrapper--Checkbox''s first sweep.\n\nThe invariant, which is load-bearing rather than incidental: the checkbox\nvariant''s label is sized to its own content and must never be stretched to the\nrow. In every multi-control row it was adopted into, the label is a SIBLING of the\nother controls rather than an ancestor, so nothing nests and nothing is captured —\nand that works precisely because it shrink-wraps. Give it flex:1 or an inset\noverlay to make the whole row clickable and it swallows the neighbouring buttons,\nlanding back in the --ClickBody problem this variant exists to avoid.\n\nRecorded because a future \"make the checkbox row bigger\" request will look\nentirely reasonable and is the one change that breaks it. The note is in the\ncomponent too, so the request meets the reason before it meets the CSS.\n\nAnd the premise correction, which is the more quotable half. The sweep was\nlaunched on the claim that ONE member ships a 13x13 checkbox. Measured: all nine\nhand-rolled checkboxes across all five members are 13x13 — fifty-four percent of\nthe WCAG floor, every one, without exception, and two of them had no accessible\nname at all.\n\nThe pattern worth keeping: a native control is not an accessible one if nobody\nsized it. \"We use the platform control\" reads as a safety claim and measured as a\nuniform failure.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3078ebbea68a9a28964984154683f33e0c47bcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/b3078ebbea68a9a28964984154683f33e0c47bcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGJjM2JkMDY5M2YxNDEwMTFkY2MwMzYwYzA5Y2M4ZTdmYTczMjhkMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910","sha":"d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910"}],"sha":"bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bc3bd0693f141011dcc0360c09cc8e7fa7328d03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:14:42Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:14:42Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): SelectWrapper--Checkbox — an inline label that killed truncation, and two API gaps\n\nThree defects from the first sweep, all measured at real call sites.\n\n## The label was display:inline, and it did two silent things\n\nIt re-parented children that had been flex items of the member''s own row into one\ninline box, and it made text-overflow: ellipsis dead — one member''s truncating org\nname measured scrollWidth 423 before and 0 after, so a long name would have\noverflowed the row rather than ellipsising.\n\nWorse, the min-inline-size: 0 I wrote to PERMIT that truncation is a no-op on an\ninline box. The declaration meant to make it work could never have worked.\n\nTwo of two members with children had to add the flex context back at rung 0. That\nis the threshold, so it belongs in the component and both workarounds can come\nout.\n\n## No density prop, so the label set the row height of every table adopting it\n\nThe label carries the 28px floor because the label is the target — correct — but\nthat is 4px above the 24px box it contains, and in a 12px-font data table it took\nrow height from 34.7px to 44.7px. A 29% increase from a control that was supposed\nto be fixing an accessibility defect.\n\ncompact drops the label to the box. The control itself never goes below 24px in\neither density: the WCAG floor is not a density setting.\n\n## {...rest} lands on the input, so nothing could be put on the label\n\nA member with a long explanatory title on its toggle would have shrunk the tooltip\nsurface from the whole control to the 24px box, and had to wrap the component in a\nspan to avoid it. labelProps now takes title, id and data-* for the label.\n\nAlso written into the component: the shrink-wrapped label is LOAD-BEARING, not\nincidental. It is what makes this variant safe beside other controls in the same\nrow — the label is a sibling, never an ancestor, so it captures nothing. Giving it\nflex:1 or an inset overlay to make \"the whole row\" clickable would swallow the\nneighbouring buttons and land straight back in the --ClickBody problem this\nvariant exists to avoid. That note is there so a future make-it-bigger request\nmeets the reason first.\n\n22 of 22 units verify clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39e810164eb9f28bdfc24f00875446ef60a5395c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/39e810164eb9f28bdfc24f00875446ef60a5395c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGQ1NjZiOTBkYzUyODEzOTA5YTg0YWJmNDFjOGFjYTg4NDdhNWE5MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad","sha":"205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad"}],"sha":"d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d566b90dc52813909a84abf41c8aca8847a5a910"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:13:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:13:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(four members): SelectWrapper--Checkbox — and it was never one 13x13 checkbox, it was all nine\n\nThe brief said one member ships a checkbox at 13x13. Measured: ALL NINE\nhand-rolled checkboxes across all five members are 13x13. Fifty-four percent of\nthe WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 floor, every one, in every member, without exception.\n\nEight adopted, now 24x24, with their wrapping labels at 28. Zero rung 4 across\nfour members — no style=, no data-deviation. Everything needed was rung 0.\n\nTwo controls went from NO ACCESSIBLE NAME AT ALL to a real one:\nenhanced-records-list''s select-all and per-row checkboxes were bare inputs with no\nlabel and no aria-label. Six were already correct, which is the loop''s \"the a11y\ndelta is usually not aria\" holding again — the delta here was target size and two\nmissing names.\n\nKeyboard verified with real Tab presses rather than el.focus(): all seven operable\ncheckboxes reachable in DOM order, focus-visible matching, one federal ring, no\ndouble-paint.\n\n## The fifth member was correctly refused\n\nprompt-template-manager''s only checkbox sits between Output column and the Save\nbutton inside the New/Edit Prompt form, flanked by four text inputs and a\ntextarea. That is a form field, not a row-selector, and out of scope by the\nsweep''s own rule. The engineer measured it anyway — 13x13, same as the rest — so\nthe debt is on the record, and then did not touch it. Form-field checkboxes are a\ndifferent sweep with a different justification.\n\nrequest-reviewer is adopted with the opposite call made explicit: its checkbox is\nnot in a list either, but it filters which rows a batch touches rather than\ncarrying a value into a submit, so it is a filter over the row set. Flagged as a\nclean single-hunk revert if that reading is wrong.\n\n## The answer to the collision question, and it is sharper than the question\n\nDoes a label-wraps-everything control collide with other clickables in the row?\nYes, twice — and both times the answer was to keep the label SMALL rather than\nstretch it.\n\nIn both cases the label is a SIBLING of the other controls, not an ancestor, so\nnothing nests and nothing is captured. That works precisely because the label\nshrink-wraps. The moment anyone gives one of these labels flex: 1 or\nposition:absolute inset:0 to make \"the whole row\" clickable, it swallows the\nneighbouring buttons and lands straight back in the --ClickBody overlay problem.\n\nSo the invariant is load-bearing rather than incidental: the checkbox variant is\nsafe in a multi-control row EXACTLY AND ONLY BECAUSE IT DOES NOT STRETCH. It is\nthe one selection variant needing neither an overlay nor a MultiControls sibling,\nand a future make-the-whole-row-clickable request would destroy that property.\n\nOne measured narrowing left for an operator''s eye: response-reviewer''s label went\n1280px to 342.7px, because the component shrink-wraps where the old rule\nstretched. The lost 970px was empty space to the right of the text — a phantom\nclick zone, not a readable target.\n\nAll four member gates flat. 22 of 22 units verify clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca9adca9e391d0af32ea2f947b649c004cd4e3c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/ca9adca9e391d0af32ea2f947b649c004cd4e3c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDIwNTI5MDczMmJiNjMwOGExYTliNGIwMGE0ZDVkYWZlNjE3OTY4YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855","sha":"582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855"}],"sha":"205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/205290732bb6308a1a9b4b00a4d5dafe617968ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:01:33Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:01:33Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): ListContainer and SelectWrapper--Checkbox\n\nTwo organs the CardRow sweep produced evidence for, built from that evidence\nrather than from the sketch.\n\n## ListContainer owns direction, because the sweep proved the container decides it\n\nThe decisive measurement was four treatments of IDENTICAL children across a 280px\ngrid track and a full-width list. Three render cleanly; the one that breaks is a\nhorizontal row in a narrow track. Same children, different container — so\ndirection is determined by the container''s width and never by the card''s content.\n\nSo the container owns it. A member sets layout once instead of repeating direction\nat every call site, and CardRow reads it from context. An explicit prop still\nwins: context is a default, not a mandate.\n\nThis is a LAYOUT in the sense the decision doc means — it places children whose\nshape it deliberately does not know — which makes it one of the few components\nallowed to set spacing. That rule is the whole lever on the layout issue: 912 raw\npaddings against zero uses of var(--space-*). Members hand-roll spacing because\nnothing owns it. This owns it.\n\nLayouts nest, and a Layout is a KIND rather than a SCOPE — being one does not make\nit a PageLayout or a WindowLayout. A ListContainer inside a two-column layout\ninside a page layout is three parents each owning the placement of its own slot.\n\nTwo details taken from what members actually do: the header is sticky, because in\nevery member that has one it stays put while the list scrolls under it; and it\nwraps, because a toolbar that cannot wrap clips its own controls.\n\n## SelectWrapper--Checkbox exists because native is not automatically accessible\n\nThe simplest variant by a wide margin — no overlay, no positioning contract,\nnothing to bury. A real input inside a real label beats anything this component\ncould invent.\n\nIt exists anyway because five members hand-roll the shape and one ships a checkbox\nmeasured at 13x13 — FIFTY-FOUR PERCENT of the WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 floor. A native\ncontrol is not an accessible one if nobody sized it. 24px now, with accent-color\nkeeping the platform''s own checked rendering rather than re-drawing a control.\n\nMulti-select only. aria-checked means \"this one is in the set\", so the\naria-pressed toggle semantics the other two wrappers carry are wrong here and\ndeliberately absent. For choose-exactly-one that is a radio, and there are\ncurrently ZERO radios in the federation, so it is not built — shipping ahead of\nconsumers is how the federal layer got a spacing scale with no adopters.\n\nIt also sets `indeterminate` through an effect, because that is a DOM property\nwith no HTML attribute: a member setting it declaratively silently gets nothing.\n\nNothing consumes either yet, so this commit cannot break a member. 22 of 22 units\nverify clean.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39895199755739c7aca0688817e58f59e576b41d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/39895199755739c7aca0688817e58f59e576b41d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDU4MmMzMGVkNjZkYmVjMjc1OTUzZWYzYWVjNmM2ZDA0Nzc1MTE4NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff","sha":"c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff"}],"sha":"582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/582c30ed66dbec275953ef3aec6c6d0477511855"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:28:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:28:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"changelog(design-system): CardRow across twenty members, and a primitive that failed silently\n\nThe third primitive reached every member in one evening — 60 call sites, zero\nsurviving named wrappers, zero rung-4 escapes, 22 of 22 units verifying clean.\n\nThe entry leads with the failure rather than the number, because the failure is\nthe more useful artifact. SelectWrapper--ClickBody shipped with display:contents\non its button, which generates no layout box in Chromium, so the control was not\nfocusable. It reported tabIndex=0, carried a correct accessible name, hit-tested\nperfectly with a mouse, and passed svelte-check, the build and every design gate —\nwhile Tab skipped every row in every list that used it.\n\nThree engineers found it independently. The cleanest statement is a three-way\ncontrolled experiment: 7 of 7 rows reachable before, 0 of 7 with the component,\n7 of 7 restored by forcing display:flex. A fourth measured tab stops dropping from\n37 to 29, exactly the eight instances. A fifth noted the 0x0 target rect that makes\nevery automated checker read the control as zero-sized.\n\nEach backed out, shipped the conservative variant, and wrote into the code that it\nwas a fallback rather than a choice. After the fix they came back and adopted what\nthey wanted originally — and the comments changed from here-is-why-I-could-not-use\n-it to here-is-why-this-surface-wants-it, with nobody adjudicating.\n\nIt also records that the API grew four times and never speculatively, each prop\nadded only after two independent members hit the same gap; that D1''s answer is one\ncomponent and the REASON beats the answer, because CardRow covered every kind\nprecisely by contributing no layout to any of them; that a table row is a\ndifferent organ and a tile is not, both measured with controlled treatments rather\nthan argued; and that a federal token had been under the accessibility floor on\nthe surface it is actually used on, found by five migrations that never compared\nnotes.\n\nOne regression in it is mine and named as mine: the hover cue I added used the\nfaint token, so hovering an interactive row dropped its boundary to 1.34:1. It\nshipped because add-a-hover-state was reasoned about and never measured, which is\nthe exact failure this practice exists to catch, committed by the person writing\nthe practice.\n\nRefs #101 #105 #106\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b13f21fe2fd72f6467fb0105e31c18f4b9c59d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/2b13f21fe2fd72f6467fb0105e31c18f4b9c59d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGM4MTE0ZmYzZjJhNzZiMzA5OTFjMjFiZWNiYjUwMGM0NjI2OGNhZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd","sha":"d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd"}],"sha":"c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c8114ff3f2a76b30991c21becbb500c46268caff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:26:33Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:26:33Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v), doc(shared-ui): D1 answered, and the rollup caveat that limits its own convention\n\nD1 is answered by the sweep rather than by argument: twenty members, sixty call\nsites, ZERO surviving CardRow--<Kind> wrappers and zero rung-4 escapes. Two\nwrappers were written early and both were deleted once direction landed; they had\nbeen byte-identical apart from a member prefix.\n\nThe reason is better than the result. CardRow covered every kind BECAUSE IT\nCONTRIBUTES NO LAYOUT TO ANY OF THEM — its display:flex sits at (0,2,0) in the\ncomponent''s scoped style and a member class is (0,1,0), so every conversion put\nthe real layout on an inner element the member owns. That held in 9 of 9\nconversions spanning flex rows, a three-track grid and a four-track grid.\n\nSo: one component with props. If the paradigm later wants to absorb the per-row\nwrapper element, the missing prop is TRACKS, not more components.\n\nD5 sharpens too, from a four-treatment experiment on identical children: three of\nfour render cleanly and the one that breaks is the wrong argument to the right\ncomponent, so Card is not separate from CardRow — a tile is a CardRow in a narrow\ntrack. And the decisive observation is that direction is determined entirely by\nthe CONTAINER''s width and never by the card''s content, which makes it\nListContainer''s business rather than a per-call-site decision.\n\nThat contrasts with the table result, which is a genuinely different shape:\ndisplay:table-row cannot be a flex container at all, and column alignment is a\ncross-row constraint no per-item prop can express.\n\nAnd a caveat that limits the file''s own naming convention, which is why it is\nrecorded here rather than buried: a Svelte tag must be a valid JS identifier, so\nSelectWrapper--ClickBody is written <SelectWrapperClickBody> at every call site.\nrg ''SelectWrapper--'' finds two import lines against fourteen call sites — a\nsevenfold undercount. Spell-the-variant-so-you-can-grep-it holds completely for\nFILENAMES and breaks for anything used as a TAG, so a rollup has to match the\nidentifier spelling or it under-reports forever.\n\nAlso documents data-tone as a member-facing state hook. One member used it to\ndelete three state classes and a wrapper, and doing so fixed a bug the duplicate\nstate had been hiding — it had been drawing a warn border over ok-coloured text,\nbecause the two copies had drifted.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74227a1eb899650a3f8daa32b0b109216dc5812f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/74227a1eb899650a3f8daa32b0b109216dc5812f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGQ3MTVmOTU2NjhlMDFjNDUxY2RiZjRiZDYzYTE2Yzc1NDA3NGViY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4","sha":"1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4"}],"sha":"d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d715f95668e01c451cdbf4bd63a16c754074ebcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:24:02Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:24:02Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(five members): re-adopt ClickBody now that it works, plus as=li, direction and tone\n\nFive members re-migrated against the fixed primitives. Every gate unmoved — cc 2,\ndp 3, pr 5, resp 9, sfl 4 — federation 71, all 22 units verify clean.\n\nThis is the loop closing on itself, and it is worth stating plainly.\n\nThree engineers independently measured that SelectWrapper--ClickBody was\nkeyboard-dead, each backed out of it, and each shipped --ClickPrimary while\nwriting into their code the reason it was a fallback rather than a choice. One\nwrote that its member \"wanted click-the-body and got click-the-primary\". Another\nrecorded a three-way controlled experiment: 7 of 7 rows tab-reachable at HEAD,\n0 of 7 with --ClickBody, 7 of 7 restored by forcing display:flex.\n\nThe fix landed, they were told, and they came back and adopted what they wanted in\nthe first place. The comments in this diff replace \"here is why I could not use\nit\" with \"here is why this surface wants it\" — which is the difference between a\nworkaround and a decision.\n\nThey also picked up as=\"li\", direction and tone, all three of which exist because\na member hit the gap and said so rather than working around it quietly. The rows\nthat were nesting a div inside a ul are now li elements; the ones that hand-rolled\na column wrapper use direction; the one that spent rung 4 on a status colour uses\ntone.\n\nFederation-wide deviations hold at five — two of which are explanatory comments\nrather than real declarations, and one of which is the single legitimate colour\ndeviation in records-surface that has been there all along.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54c8b7fac556a325d35fd7b23fd13409c14b8efa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/54c8b7fac556a325d35fd7b23fd13409c14b8efa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDFjZGE0ZjM5MzllODhhNjNiMTNlYTVjNjdlYzNlODJjNGJlMDgyZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be","sha":"562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be"}],"sha":"1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1cda4f3939e88a63b13ea5c67ec3e82c4be082e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:22:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:22:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(theme, shared-ui): the control boundary finally clears 3:1, and CardRow''s hover stops making it worse\n\nTwo fixes, both from measurements, one of them mine to own.\n\n## --color-border-strong was under the floor on the surface it is used on\n\n#646785 measures 2.73:1 against --color-surface, under F7''s 3:1 control-boundary\nfloor. FIVE independent migrations measured it the same night — the resolver\nfamily, record-collector, prompt-template-manager, response-reviewer and\norg-workbench all reported the same number without comparing notes.\n\nThe theme''s own comment cited 3.44:1, which is true against --color-background.\nBut CardRow paints --color-surface INSIDE that border, so the boundary a person\nactually reads was never the one the comment described. The component''s fill\nundercut the component''s border claim.\n\n#75789c now: 3.52:1 on surface, 4.43:1 on background. Light was already 3.52 and\nvibrant 3.14, so only dark was short and only dark moved — the three modes now sit\nwithin 0.4 of each other rather than straddling the floor.\n\nThis was deliberately deferred while eight agents were measuring contrast in\nflight. They are all done, so it lands now.\n\n## CardRow''s hover made the boundary FAINTER, and that one is mine\n\nThe hover rule I added hours ago used --color-border, the faint token, so hovering\nan interactive row dropped its boundary from 2.73:1 to 1.34:1. A hover cue that\nREDUCES contrast is worse than no hover cue at all.\n\nIt shipped because \"add a hover state\" was reasoned about and never measured —\nprecisely the failure mode this practice exists to catch, committed by the person\nwriting the practice. Caught by a probe comparing rest and hover on the same row.\n\n--color-text-muted now: 4.64:1 on hover against 3.52:1 at rest, so the cue\nstrengthens the boundary rather than dissolving it.\n\nFederation 71 -> 71, contrast 30/30, all 22 units verify clean.\n\nCloses the last of #106.\n\nRefs #101 #106\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee2f7bf986c044923e48331f8680eff901af19c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/ee2f7bf986c044923e48331f8680eff901af19c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDU2MjYxMmMzMTBkNTAzY2VlZDBiZDVkZDliZWFiMjU5MDIwZTA3YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42","sha":"a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42"}],"sha":"562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/562612c310d503ceed0bd5dd9beab259020e07be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:22:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:22:59Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(search-results): thirteen rows, both ClickBody extremes, and the overlay anchor as a design decision\n\nThirteen CardRows, all as=\"li\", eight SelectWrapper--ClickBody, eight raw buttons\ngone, thirteen wrapper <li> elements gone. Zero deviations, zero a11y errors, zero\nconsole errors on a full drive. Member gate 3 -> 3, federation 71 -> 71.\n\nBoth declared Button holdouts are gone, and the engineer''s framing of why is the\nuseful part: their original rationale was right and their conclusion was wrong.\n.srq-card-row and .srq-gate-pick were never Buttons. They were a CardRow and a\nSelectWrapper, and the organ simply did not exist yet.\n\n## The measurement the assignment asked for\n\n37 of 37 controls reachable by elementFromPoint at their own centre. Zero\nswallowed. Clicking the row at 8, 50 and 82 percent of its width toggles every\ntime; the caret still collapses and expands; the dismiss still advances to its\nconfirm step and does not leak through to the row. Tab order per card is row,\ndismiss, caret, all focus-visible with a real ring, and Enter and Space both\nactivate.\n\nSo the overlay holds at seven controls — which was the open question — and this\nmember exercised BOTH ends of ClickBody''s range in one place: a queue card with\ntwo siblings under the overlay and a gate pick with zero. That is what let it\nseparate \"the guard is wrong\" from \"my markup is wrong\".\n\n## The thing no other pilot could have found\n\nThe overlay''s positioned ancestor is a DESIGN DECISION, not a requirement.\n\nThis member''s card contains a disclosure panel holding five more controls, two of\nwhich write. The anchor sits on .srq-card-top rather than on the CardRow, so\nclick-anywhere covers the collapsed row and STOPS at the panel. Anchor it on the\nCardRow instead and clicking a search result collapses the card.\n\nNo other pilot has a CardRow containing a disclosure, so no other pilot could\ndiscover that.\n\n## Two findings that outlive this member\n\nThe BEM rollup cannot see call sites. A Svelte tag must be a valid JS identifier,\nso SelectWrapper--ClickBody is written <SelectWrapperClickBody> and\nrg ''SelectWrapper--'' finds two import lines rather than eight call sites — a\nfourfold undercount. The spell-the-variant-so-you-can-grep-it argument holds for\nCardRow-- FILENAMES and breaks for anything used as a tag. It will silently\nunder-report every future rollup.\n\nAnd aria-pressed is unconditional on both wrappers, which is right for a toggle\nand wrong for a one-shot commit like the gate pick — it announces \"toggle button,\nnot pressed\" for an action that writes and vanishes.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3213598dbb1eabf7ee6215247e2f413681cc894f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/3213598dbb1eabf7ee6215247e2f413681cc894f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGEyNWU1OWRkZDcxODY0OGI5NTRjOTViNTJlZWJjYjM4ODY1YmFjNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1","sha":"79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1"}],"sha":"a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a25e59ddd718648b954c95b52eebcb38865bac42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:19:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:19:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(response-reviewer, corpora-curator): three view modes split three ways, and the missing organ is the container\n\nTwo members, eleven rows, 32 declarations and 8 rule-sets deleted. Gates unmoved\nat 9 and 2, federation 71 -> 71, 12/12 tests still green in corpora-curator.\n\ncorpora-curator''s two declared holdouts are gone — .cc-strat and .cc-row, rows\nsomeone had already reasoned about in prose and left raw. Only the tag-suggest\noption remains, and the gallery catalog was updated so the library stops claiming\notherwise.\n\n## The three-view-mode question, answered three ways\n\nsingle fits unmodified. content-reader fits with one column-wrapper slot — and the\nadoption FIXED A LIVE BUG, because those cards measured padding: 0 and their\ncontent sat flush against the border.\n\nby-record does not fit, twice over. Its inner row is a three-track grid whose\ncolumns align ACROSS SIBLING ROWS, which a flex CardRow structurally cannot\nexpress; and its outer card is padding-zero with a full-bleed tinted header band,\nwhere CardRow always pads.\n\nNo wrapper would have helped, and that is the useful part. The spread was not\nkinds-of-card — it was row-versus-grid and padded-versus-full-bleed. The missing\norgan is the CONTAINER, not a row variant: by-record needs a ListContainer that\nowns a grid template its rows participate in. That is D5, and by-record is\nevidence it is the harder half.\n\n## The variant was chosen by a defect, not by the card\n\nThis engineer wanted --ClickBody for both corpora-curator rows, built it, measured\nit, and had to back it out. On intent it was right: the rows were already\nwhole-surface buttons and the overlay buried nothing, zero on all seven rows. The\nfallback shrank the target from 359x80 to 302x24.\n\nSo its D3 answer is that the choice was forced by the keyboard defect rather than\nby the card''s contents, and it should be re-run now the primitive is fixed. Four\nof its rows now sit EXACTLY at the 24px floor rather than above it, which is the\nrecoverable cost.\n\nIts three-way controlled experiment is the cleanest statement of that defect\nanyone produced: at HEAD 7 of 7 rows tab-reachable, with --ClickBody 0 of 7,\nforcing display:flex on the same element 7 of 7 restored, and tabindex=\"0\" does\nnot help.\n\nAccessible names went from whole-row text concatenation — one measured as \"The\ndegree is not the job Brookings fetched Work-Based-Learning\nCredential-Attainment\" — to the title alone. aria-pressed was absent entirely\nbefore; selection was background-tint-only.\n\n## A naming finding worth acting on\n\n\"Wrapper\" is wrong in SelectWrapper--ClickBody. It renders no wrapper element,\nwraps nothing, and its entire mechanism is a sibling overlay — the engineer read\nthe file twice before believing it. RowSelect--ClickBody is the suggestion.\nEverything else read clean first pass.\n\nAnd response-reviewer contributes a fact the rollout should not assume away: it\nhas no row selection in ANY of its three modes. Its rows are triage surfaces —\nact on the row — not selection surfaces. Zero SelectWrapper call sites.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e4529acefd2f8c25b6d4306f4704a3c0400f22c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/1e4529acefd2f8c25b6d4306f4704a3c0400f22c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDc5YTg2OWEzZjJlNDNiMWZjMDZiOGY2ZWY4YmE3ODAxMGY5ZDlkZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1","sha":"41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1"}],"sha":"79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/79a869a3f2e43b1fc06b8f6ef8ba78010f9d9df1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:19:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:19:55Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(org-workbench, person-enrichment): the row organ its own CSS asked for, and D1 answered\n\nThirteen surfaces across two members. Zero CardRow--<Kind> wrappers, zero rung-4\nescapes, both member gates unmoved at 6 and 2.\n\n## The holdout note gets rewritten by its own successor\n\norg-workbench''s app.css opens with a four-item ROW HOLDOUT block, written during\nthe Button migration, naming the missing organ — a selectable list item — as the\nreason four rows stayed raw. Three of the four are now gone and the note explains\nwhy the fourth stays. The organ it asked for exists.\n\n## D1, answered with a measurement rather than a preference\n\nOne CardRow covered all four of person-enrichment''s pulse-dimension lists, and the\nREASON is the finding: CardRow contributed no layout to any of them.\n\n.ui-cardrow''s display:flex sits at (0,2,0) in the component''s scoped style; a\nmember class is (0,1,0); direction offers row or column, not tracks. So every\nconversion put the real layout on an inner element the member owns — and that held\nin 9 of 9 conversions across both members, spanning flex rows, a 3-track grid and\na 4-track grid.\n\nThe base is thin enough that one file serves every kind, precisely because what\nvaries between kinds is layout and CardRow never owned it. Collapse to one\ncomponent. The cost is a wrapper element per row, which is rung 0 and cheap; if\nthe paradigm wants to absorb that, the missing prop is TRACKS — a grid direction\ntaking grid-template-columns — not more components.\n\n## The push-back worth keeping\n\nThree of the four pulse-dimension lists are FORM REPEATERS, not object lists. An\nemail-input row is a field, not an object in a generated list. They took CardRow\ncleanly and look heavier for it — a bordered card per input row inside an already\nbordered stack. It works; whether it should is a paradigm-scope question for the\noperator rather than a fit question, and the engineer flagged it before it hardens\nrather than after.\n\n## The largest single a11y win in either member\n\nperson-enrichment''s org-suggest row was an <li onclick> with TWO svelte-ignore\ncomments suppressing a11y_click_events_have_key_events and\na11y_no_noninteractive_element_interactions. It was not keyboard-operable at all.\nIt is a real button with a real accessible name now, and both suppressions are\ndeleted.\n\nRelatedOrgs takes CardRow with NO SelectWrapper — a relation row is displayed and\nacted on, never selected, and its six controls are exactly the population an\noverlay would bury. That is the federation''s densest row proving CardRow stands\nalone.\n\nAlso collapsed: two byte-identical four-track grid recipes into one.\n\nMeasured: 16 CardRows and 13 select controls in one member, 18 and 3 in the other,\nall reachable by real Tab presses, zero buried siblings by hit-test, zero\ndata-a11y-error, zero console errors, and zero non-<li> children of any <ul>.\n\nLeft deliberately and by name: a combobox option under role=\"listbox\" that needs\nrole=\"option\" semantics CardRow does not carry — and whose ARIA is already wrong,\nso papering it with a CardRow would have hidden a real defect.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4e640b0a5d0afa7f54d845a032bd58865685bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/d4e640b0a5d0afa7f54d845a032bd58865685bf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDQxYjM2MTI4NDI0MjIxNGQxZjk0MDUyMzJjNTRkNTMwNDJmNTIyZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415","sha":"ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415"}],"sha":"41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/41b361284242214d1f9405232c54d53042f522e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:18:45Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:18:45Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(chat, pack-runner, docs-portal, sort-filter-lens): four surfaces, zero SelectWrappers, and the Card question answered\n\nFour members, eleven rows, twelve rule-sets and 34 declarations removed. All four\nmember gates unmoved, federation 71 -> 71, four clean builds.\n\nZero SelectWrappers shipped across four surfaces — and that IS the D3 result.\nchat''s proposal card is inert with a Run action inside it; pack-runner uses a\nnative label-wrapped checkbox; sort-filter-lens''s pending row reports status\nrather than offering selection. Not every list row is selectable, and a sweep that\nforced a wrapper onto all four would have said nothing.\n\nTwo of four surfaces cleared the 3:1 non-text floor by adoption alone: chat and\ndocs-portal were both drawing boundaries with --color-border at 1.26:1 and now\ndraw --color-border-strong at 3.44:1. pack-runner gained a visible selected state\nwhere the row previously had no row-level affordance at all.\n\nsort-filter-lens dropped an opacity: 0.75 that was standing in for state, with the\nglyph and the ok token carrying it instead.\n\n## Third independent confirmation of the ClickBody defect\n\nThis engineer measured it on the real MemberLibraries component: display contents,\n0x0 rect, tabIndex 0, focus() does not take, and the tab order goes from\nfive stops to three — the card''s primary action simply vanishes for keyboard\nusers. WCAG 2.1.1 Level A, strictly worse than the raw button it replaced.\n\nIt notes the part that makes it dangerous: the mouse half is perfect. The overlay\nrenders, elementFromPoint returns the button at top and centre, a synthetic click\nreaches onselect, and the positioned sibling stays reachable exactly as documented.\nAnyone who only clicks would sign it off.\n\nIt reverted its adoption and wrote the measurement into the call site. Already\nfixed federally before this commit landed; recorded because three independent\nmeasurements of one defect is the system working.\n\n## Is Card a separate organ? No — and the reason is better than the question\n\nMeasured across four surfaces: three take their width from a container and run\nhorizontally at 42-46px; docs-portal''s tile takes its width from a GRID TRACK and\nruns vertically at 149px. So the axis differs, not the density.\n\nBut the 93px flex-column tile took CardRow with ZERO rung-4 escapes — its\nCard-ness cost exactly one declaration, align-self: stretch. A separate Card\ncomponent would duplicate the entire surface recipe to add a flex-direction.\n\nAnd the giveaway is inside CardRow already: inline-size: 100% is INERT in a\nvertical list, where the item is full-width anyway, and is the only thing making a\ngrid tile fill its track. CardRow already contains the tile case; it just does not\nadmit it.\n\nSo the difference belongs to the CONTAINER, not the item. ListContainer and a\nCardGrid are the separate organs; the item stays one. That keeps D1 at \"one\ncomponent\" for another member.\n\nThe one real difference is not geometric: the tile NAVIGATES — it swaps the\nportal''s view and the grid unmounts, so selected is permanently false. That is\nD3''s CardRow--Link sighting, and it is the thing worth naming about that card\nrather than its height.\n\n## sort-filter-lens''s rung 4 retired before it could rot\n\nIts engineer reached rung 4 on the first try for a row tone and said plainly that\nmeant the API was wrong. It does now — two other members hit the same gap the same\nnight — so the style-string builder becomes a tone name and the deviation is gone\nrather than left as a stale annotation, which is the debt we spent this morning\nclearing.\n\nAlso deleted: pack-runner''s .pr-app .rows li at (0,1,1), which would have\nout-specified .ui-cardrow.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ed8f84962683094cbfcabcabd6f123104cd5af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/2ed8f84962683094cbfcabcabd6f123104cd5af8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGFlODNhZDk4MmQwMTNhNmU0ZTdhYWM2MDUxN2NhNDA1YTFhMmU0MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18","sha":"23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18"}],"sha":"ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ae83ad982d013a6e4e7aac60517ca405a1a2e415"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:16:10Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:16:10Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): CardRow gains a tone axis, because two members needed it in one sweep\n\nCardRow shipped with exactly one state axis, selected. Two independent members hit\nthe gap on the same night: request-reviewer''s unbound token row needs an error\nboundary and spelled it as rung-4 style= plus data-deviation; records-surface''s\naccepted-URL row needs the success equivalent and its engineer LEFT IT RAW rather\nthan mint a second deviation.\n\nThat is both halves of the evidence in one sweep, and the loop is explicit about\nwhat it means — an escape hatch reached on the FIRST adoption is the API being\nwrong, not the member being difficult.\n\nFive tones, same vocabulary as Chip, picked by what the row MEANS rather than what\ncolour someone wants. It composes with selected rather than replacing it, because\na row can be selected and in error at once.\n\nTones paint the BOUNDARY and not the fill, deliberately. A row''s content has to\nstay legible on the same surface at every tone, and a tinted fill would move every\ntext contrast pair inside the row — which is exactly the class of defect the Chip\nrollout spent the evening finding. selected keeps the fill.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65ef18f4ede47f0fc16d7aa7f840d08d79857f64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/65ef18f4ede47f0fc16d7aa7f840d08d79857f64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDIzYjA0Njc4MWJkZjJjZjg1MzBmOWQzYjI1Y2Q2Mjg1OWU4ZmJkMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067","sha":"3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067"}],"sha":"23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/23b046781bdf2cf8530f9d3b25cd62859e8fbd18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:16:09Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:16:09Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(records-surface, request-reviewer): CardRow — and enhanced-records-list proves a table is a different organ\n\nThree members swept. Two adopted, one deliberately did not, and the one that\ndid not is the most useful result of the three.\n\n## records-surface — six rows, a 20x target, and a write-on-select constraint\n\nRecord rows and candidate rows onto CardRow; twelve locally-owned card\ndeclarations drop to zero. The rung-0 override the Button rollout left behind — a\n:global() justify-self with an eight-line comment — was DELETED rather than\nported, because the base handles it now.\n\nThe pick affordance went from a 44.2 x 24 Button to an 894.7 x 24 ClickPrimary.\nSame row, twenty times the target area. And the new open link ships at 24x24\nrather than copying the existing one beside it, which the probe measured at\n10 x 20 — twenty-one percent of the WCAG floor, and now raised.\n\n--ClickBody was rejected for a reason that generalises: picking WRITES to live\nclient data, and the row also carries an external link. A click-anywhere overlay\nputs an accidental write one stray click from opening a tab.\n\n## request-reviewer — rung 4 on the first adoption, which means the API is wrong\n\nThe token-binding row needs an error boundary, and CardRow carries exactly one\nstate axis: selected. An invalid row has nowhere sanctioned to live, so the\nengineer spelled it as style= plus data-deviation and said plainly what the loop\nsays that means — an escape hatch reached on the first try is the API being wrong,\nnot the member being difficult.\n\nIt is not a one-off. records-surface''s accepted-URL row needs the same thing and\nthat engineer LEFT IT RAW rather than mint a second deviation. So both halves of\nthe evidence exist: one member declared it, one refused it. CardRow is getting a\ntone axis in the next commit.\n\nThis member also contributes \"no SelectWrapper applies here\" — its only generated\nlist is read-only, because a binding is reported rather than chosen.\n\nAnd its gallery catalog was updated because it had stopped describing reality: the\ntoken-binding entry moved from Local recipes to Federal primitives, with the token\nlist corrected and a header note that the federal/local boundary MOVES and this\nfile is where that gets recorded.\n\n## enhanced-records-list — CardRow does not apply to a table, measured three ways\n\nNot asserted. Three treatments of the same four-column row, same page, same theme:\n\n  A  real tr/td               31.7px, cells at x = 16 / 369.6 / 950.1 / 1165\n  B  CardRow inside tbody     RENDERS, 710.5px inside a 1248px table, aligned to\n                              no column — Svelte builds DOM via createElement so\n                              it is not foster-parented out, it just silently\n                              becomes an anonymous block\n  C  CardRow in a colspan td  36.8px card in a 51.1px row, +61% vertical, children\n                              at 38.6 / 167.3 / 334.9 / 411.3 against headers\n                              still at 16 / 369.6 / 950.1 / 1165\n\nBoth failures render. The table header simply becomes a caption for columns that\nno longer exist — a plausible-looking page, which is the worst shape.\n\nThe mechanism is that a tr under border-collapse cannot take padding or radius at\nall, and a flex row sizes children to CONTENT while a table sizes them to a shared\nCOLUMN. This member derives its column count at runtime from the union of every\nenrichment set''s keys, so there is no fixed grid to hand-hold either.\n\nZero code changed. One comment block carrying the measurements, so the next sweep\ndoes not re-run the experiment.\n\nIts disabled per-row checkbox measures 13 x 13 — fifty-four percent of the floor —\nand is wired as the selection mechanism in the next version. That is the concrete\ncaller SelectWrapper--Checkbox has been missing.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"345859dcfaa1f46633689b5b6dc56ba7f4ccb588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/345859dcfaa1f46633689b5b6dc56ba7f4ccb588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDMyODJkMWYzMmEyMDE4MTA0MGFiNzM2MjlmNTZlZjQyYjI4NGMwNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e","sha":"c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e"}],"sha":"3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/3282d1f32a20181040ab73629f56ef42b284c067"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:15:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:15:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(prompt-template-manager): the paradigm''s own example, and an 18px delete button\n\nFive rows onto CardRow and SelectWrapper--ClickPrimary. Declarations in the\nlist-surface CSS down 38 percent, four rule-sets deleted, no CardRow--<Kind>\nwrapper needed. Member gate flat at 1, federation flat at 71.\n\nA live target-size failure fixed: the old li { display: flex } had no\nflex: 0 0 auto on the icon Button, so a long row name flex-shrank the DELETE\ncontrol to 18x28 — seventy-five percent of the WCAG floor. Invisible to the drift\ngate, found only by the before/after probe.\n\nAnd selection was visual-only. .prompt-select carried no aria at all, so a screen\nreader user could not tell which prompt was loaded. That is the a11y win of the\nwhole migration and it is why SelectWrapper''s selected prop has to exist.\n\n## Where selection state lives — the recommendation, and it is to keep the duplication\n\nCardRow.selected paints. SelectWrapper.selected announces. They are not one fact\ntwice; they are a paint instruction on a non-interactive div and an ARIA state on\na real button, derived from one source.\n\nEach alternative loses something concrete. The wrapper cannot own it — it sits\nINSIDE the row and cannot reach its ancestor''s attribute; inverting breaks the li\nnesting and the positioned-ancestor contract, so the option that looks cleanest is\nstructurally impossible. Context-passing couples two components D3 deliberately\nkeeps composable and hides the aria decision from the call site. Dropping either\nloses the paint to hand-rolled CSS or loses aria-pressed entirely.\n\nThe ask is a RENAME, not a merge: the shared name is what makes a reader assume\none is redundant. Name them for their jobs — the row''s is a paint, the wrapper''s\nis `pressed`, matching the attribute it sets. Recorded for when Selector lands.\n\n## Honest about what it cost\n\n--ClickPrimary sits inside CardRow''s padding, so the card''s 8/12px padding is\npermanently dead space: clickable card area went from 84-92% to 53-68%. Only\n--ClickBody''s overlay reaches it. The engineer shipped that regression knowingly\nrather than spending rung 4 to claw it back, and the absolute target is still\n182x40, far above the floor.\n\nAlso raised and not chased: loadIntoEditor() discards unsaved editor state with no\ndirty check, though the member already tracks isDirty. A mis-aimed row click\nsilently destroys work — which is an argument for a guard in that function, not\nagainst click-anywhere.\n\nFederation-wide, var(--space-*) in apps/*/src was ZERO at HEAD and is 20 across\nthe three pilots tonight. That is D5''s \"layout arrives as a component, not a\ndoctrine\" actually happening.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6deb4c7f8d501194eda639fe627faa2ebb18343d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/6deb4c7f8d501194eda639fe627faa2ebb18343d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGMxOGZjZWE3OTA2NzczYWFhZmI1ODNjYTM3NTZjM2QzNzI1NzQ3M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b","sha":"8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b"}],"sha":"c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c18fcea7906773aaafb583ca3756c3d37257473e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:15:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:15:01Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(record-collector): CardRow with the thin base, and the measurement that killed ClickBody\n\nFive rows onto CardRow and SelectWrapper--ClickPrimary. Zero rung-4 escapes, zero\nCardRow--<Kind> wrappers, nine raw px/rem literals gone from the migrated\ncomponent. Member gate flat at 1, federation flat at 71.\n\n## The variant was decided by hit-test, not by argument\n\nThe engineer built BOTH and called elementFromPoint at the delete button''s own\ncentre:\n\n  --ClickPrimary   static siblings   delete reachable 5/5\n  --ClickBody      static siblings   delete reachable 0/3  <- overlay covers it\n  --ClickBody      relative wrapper  delete reachable 2/2\n\nUnder --ClickBody as a member would naively write it, clicking delete SELECTS THE\nRECORD SET instead. Button never sets position, so every sibling control in this\nfederation is static by default and every one goes under.\n\nThe engineer then declined to rest on the obvious argument, which is the part\nworth keeping: the failure is in the SAFE direction. Delete becomes unreachable\nrather than accidentally fired, so \"click-anywhere next to a destructive action is\ndangerous\" is weaker than it sounds. The three reasons it shipped --ClickPrimary\ninstead are mechanical (the overlay swallows the control), task-loss (whole-surface\nclick destroys text selection on the one string operators copy out of this member),\nand affordance economics (the free reversible action gets the whole 306x94 card\nwhile the unrecoverable one stays 28x28 inside it).\n\nMeasured distance between the select surface and the delete: 71.7px under\n--ClickPrimary, and under --ClickBody 0px and then MINUS 28, because the select\nsurface does not stop at the delete button, it continues underneath it.\n\n## A disclosure is not a CardRow, and not a SelectWrapper either\n\nThree of four holdouts expand rather than select. Both wrappers hard-render\naria-pressed, which is the toggle-BUTTON contract, so adopting either would\nannounce the wrong thing — the same error as the six role=\"menu\" declarations with\nno arrow keys. And a group header is not a row: wrapping it negates border,\nradius, background and padding, four of the five properties CardRow contributes.\n\nMeasured 70.9px and 27px, the latter clearing the 24px floor by 3px only because\nits 0.3rem padding happens to add up. Luck, not a contract. DisclosureRow is a\nfourth organ, four sightings in this member alone.\n\n## The finding that reframes D3\n\nThe rule keys on whether a card contains controls, which is true of 18 of 18 and\ntherefore sorts nothing. What predicted the failure here was whether a contained\ncontrol is RECOVERABLE. A swallowed download is an annoyance; a swallowed delete\nis a control the user believes they pressed.\n\nAnd the general form: the overlay''s correctness depends on CSS the overlay does\nnot own. It is the only primitive in this system whose contract can be broken by a\nsibling''s default value.\n\nOne a11y regression caught during the run rather than after: adding aria-label\nsuppresses a button''s text content in the accessible name, so \"6 cols · 12 rows\"\nwould silently have stopped being announced. The label carries the dimensions\nexplicitly now.\n\nAlso removed: a 20-line dead block in app.css at (0,2,1) which would have\nout-specified .ui-selectprimary the moment anything rendered under ul.records\nagain.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78ae962b814546c04beb910151f3b8d09249720d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/78ae962b814546c04beb910151f3b8d09249720d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhkNmUwMmIwZDY4ZGYwOGQ3N2VlYTE5MjlmOWNhMzMxOWMwN2I1NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a","sha":"16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a"}],"sha":"8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d6e02b0d68df08d77eea1929f9ca3319c07b55b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:14:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:14:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): SelectWrapper--ClickBody was keyboard-dead, and three more the pilots caught\n\nTwo pilots independently broke the primitives I shipped three hours ago. Every fix\nhere came from a measurement, not a review.\n\n## The blocker\n\n.ui-selectbody was display: contents, and Chromium generates no box for it — so\nthe button was NOT FOCUSABLE. It reported tabIndex=0, carried a correct accessible\nname, hit-tested fine with a mouse, and Tab skipped every row. One pilot found it\nby enumerating tab order and seeing only delete buttons; another by measuring a\n0x0 target rect, which also means every automated SC 2.5.8 audit would read the\nrow''s primary control as zero-sized.\n\nIt rendered perfectly and looked like it worked. That is the failure shape this\nentire practice exists to catch, and I shipped it.\n\nA real box, visually inert, is what was always intended: CardRow paints the\nsurface, the button carries the name and the tab stop, ::after does the\nstretching.\n\n## The guard was wrong twice over\n\nIt read `position` on each sibling control and flagged anything static. But a\nmember CANNOT set position on a Button without reaching into .ui-btn — the only\nlegal remedy is a positioned WRAPPER, which the check never looked at. So a pilot\napplied the correct fix, proved by hit-test that the delete button was reachable,\nand still got console-errored on all five rows.\n\nIt hit-tests now. elementFromPoint at each sibling''s own centre, asking the\nbrowser what is actually on top rather than inferring it from one property.\n\n## Two silent clobbers\n\nBoth SelectWrappers spread {...rest} after class=, so a caller passing class=\nREPLACED the component''s own class rather than merging. Measured: display fell\nfrom flex to block, and min-block-size, focus ring and cursor all vanished. Button\ngets this right; CardRow was safe by accident. Both wrappers now destructure and\nmerge.\n\nAnd --ClickPrimary had no min-inline-size: 0, so as a flex item it defaulted to\nmin-width:auto and one long unbreakable token pushed the row''s sibling controls\nclean out of the card — measured at 0% reachability for a delete button.\n\n## Two API gaps, each of which 16 members would have hit alone\n\nCardRow gains `as`, because 16 of 20 members render rows as <li> and a <ul>\npermits only <li>. Shipping div-only meant sixteen independent discoveries of the\nsame workaround.\n\nAnd CardRow gains a hover cue, because a selectable row without one reads as\ninert — one pilot spent its only rung-4 escape restoring the li:hover its own\nstylesheet used to provide.\n\nThat hover rule needed :global() inside :has(). Without it Svelte cannot see the\nslotted children statically and PRUNES the entire rule at build time, silently,\nreporting only a svelte-check warning. Caught because the warning count went 0 ->\n1 and I looked. The rule is verified present in a built member bundle rather than\nassumed.\n\nAlso documented rather than changed: CardRow.selected and SelectWrapper.selected\nare deliberately both passed. One is a paint instruction on a non-interactive div,\nthe other an ARIA state on a real button — same source, different jobs.\n\nAll 22 units verify clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65000db45914107b6cc271daa028b4879aacf5e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/65000db45914107b6cc271daa028b4879aacf5e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDE2YTdjYWY2YjhkOTI0NzIzZjYwNDJkMmYwMzJkYmM0NjljZGE3MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba","sha":"c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba"}],"sha":"16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/16a7caf6b8d924723f6042d2f032dbc469cda71a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:10:34Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:10:34Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(resolvers): CardRow across the resolver family, and the one axis it splits on\n\nperson-db-resolver, record-db-resolver and affiliation-rating-resolver onto CardRow\nand SelectWrapper. Nine rows, all three member gates unchanged at 3 -> 3, all\npre-existing failures, none button- or row-related.\n\nZero rung 4. No class=, no style=, no data-deviation, zero data-a11y-error rendered.\nEvery layout need resolved at rung 0.\n\n## The API gap, which is one property\n\nCardRow is display:flex, align-items:flex-start — a HORIZONTAL row. Every resolver\ncandidate is vertically stacked: identity and score, then stats, then a disclosure,\nthen a preview, then the commit. Rendering those as flex children lays them side by\nside.\n\nSo the family splits on exactly one axis. Eight horizontal call sites took the base\nwith zero overrides. Three stacked ones needed a wrapper — and the two wrappers\nwritten are byte-equivalent modulo the member prefix, carrying no domain knowledge\nat all, only flex-direction: column.\n\nThat is two of D1''s three-identical-wrappers threshold, and the engineer''s\nrecommendation is right: do not promote a CardRow--Stacked file, add a direction\nprop. A wrapper whose entire content is one layout property is what a prop is for.\n\n## The rule this family produced\n\nSelectWrapper--ClickBody is actively dangerous here, and the reason generalises:\nthe resolver row''s act is match, which writes to the canonical layer — creates\npersons and orgs, RELATEs affiliations, stamps the source row. Not undoable from\nthe surface. Click-anywhere makes the whole card a hit area for that write, next\nto a disclosure the operator is meant to click freely. A stray click becomes a\ncanonical write against live client data.\n\nSo: any member whose row action is match, apply or promote should be assumed\n--ClickPrimary until argued otherwise.\n\nThe engineer also split arm from commit rather than forcing one control to do\nboth — clicking the name arms it via aria-pressed, the primary Button commits.\nTwo controls, two distinct accessible names, no stray-click write. Flagged as a\ndeliberate addition rather than hidden.\n\n## Measured\n\nThe candidate name went from a non-interactive span at 16px, unreachable by\nkeyboard at all, to a button at 24px. Tabbable controls in one member''s candidate\nlists went 5 -> 10.\n\nAnd the loop''s known rung-0 regression reproduced exactly as predicted: a\ncolumn-flex CardRow stretched an inline-flex Button to 1034px inside a 1060px row.\nCaught only by the before/after probe — no gate sees it — fixed at rung 0 and\nre-measured at 199.9px. Worth its own line in the CardRow loop: the first thing a\nstacked CardRow does is stretch your Buttons.\n\n## A correction to my own count\n\naffiliation-rating-resolver is NOT a list surface and should come off the 16-of-18\nfigure. It renders one record at a time in a single card; its 21 controls were a\nfile-level count of a single-record form, not a row. The real count is 15 of 18 —\nand arr''s actual rows contain one anchor and one code element, which is the\nzero-sibling-control case the decision doc''s table claims does not exist in this\ncodebase. So there IS a surface where an overlay-free wrapper would be safe.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5b0fc729839cb0ea9353bc6cd012a318e03de7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/e5b0fc729839cb0ea9353bc6cd012a318e03de7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGMxOWM1ZjkyNzM5OWIzMWVmMzQyMmRlNmRmNDk0MmMzYmM3ODBlYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c","sha":"376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c"}],"sha":"c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c19c5f927399b31ef3422de6df4942c3bc780eba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:01:35Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:01:35Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(scripts): pnpm verify — one command that says WHICH member broke, and when\n\nThe gates we had prove a unit typechecks and builds. They do not prove the\nfederation is intact, and more importantly they do not answer the question that\nactually matters on a demo morning: not \"is something broken\" but \"WHICH member,\nand at WHICH commit\".\n\nEight agents are mid-sweep across fourteen members tonight. Without this, a break\nfound Monday night is a bisect session; with it, it is one command.\n\nWalks every buildable unit independently and prints a table. A failing unit does\nNOT stop the others, because the point is to learn how many are broken rather than\nthat one is. Exit code is the failure count capped at 125, so `git bisect run\npnpm verify` works directly and CI gets a usable signal.\n\nTwo modes that matter under time pressure. --fast skips builds and runs in\nseconds, which is the pre-commit check. --since HEAD~5 scopes to units whose files\nactually moved, with one deliberate exception: any change under packages/ widens\nit back to everything, because a federal component can break any consumer and\nscoping there would be exactly the wrong optimisation.\n\nsvelte-check exits 0 on warnings, so the parser reads the ERRORS count out of its\noutput rather than trusting the exit status — matching how every migration loop\nhas been reading this gate by hand all week.\n\nBaseline right now: 22 units, all passing.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ea42c759a2a2481c320bc059d3b5ea0dafb39c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/5ea42c759a2a2481c320bc059d3b5ea0dafb39c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDM3Njg4MTIwOTIzMGUwOWQwMmIxYzllNmU5ZWUwZjA1NTUzM2FjMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3","sha":"b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3"}],"sha":"376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/376881209230e09d02b1c9e6e9ee0f055533ac2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:58:37Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:58:37Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"changelog(design-system): Chip, the federal gallery, and an escape hatch that never worked\n\nTwelve units, 100 Chip call sites, declared deviations from eight to one, 171 net\nlines of CSS gone across 24 commits.\n\nThe entry argues that Chip found what Button could not, because buttons diverge in\nshape and chips diverge in MEANING. docs-portal''s contrast report was itself\nunreadable at 2.11:1 on half its cells. An outcome of skipped was painted green\nwith the high-confidence token, so the one outcome meaning we did not look read\nexactly like we looked and it was good. enhanced-records-list rendered four of\nfive connection states identically, with closed and error drawing like connecting.\n\nAnd three members with no shared code had each drawn connection_status the same\nwrong way — the eleven-renderings problem in miniature.\n\nAuthoring the primitive surfaced the third federal scale that DESIGN.md specified\nand never shipped, and records that I reached for the wrong names and the doc had\nalready rejected them by name. It shipped at seven steps rather than six on the\noperator''s better argument: the fold costs a 1px increase across 130 declarations\nof dense table content, and the token indirection makes that trade unnecessary\nbecause converging later is a one-line merge.\n\nThen the rollout found three defects in the primitives themselves, every one\ncaught by an engineer measuring rather than reading — including Chip''s accent tone\nfailing the floor its own header promises, which the contrast gate passed 30/30\nstraight through because it walks text pairs and a chip paints its own ground.\n\nThe section that will matter most to a reader is rung 4. The escape hatch the\ngovernance model treats as its detection mechanism never worked, and could not be\nfixed by the obvious means, and nobody noticed across nineteen members because it\nhas zero real call sites. An unused escape hatch is indistinguishable from a\nworking one.\n\nPlus the gallery finally existing and auditing itself into a fix, the probe\nincident and the rule it produced, and an honest what-is-not-done ending on the\nobservation that F7 has no mechanical check at all.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53096472f6911e4a2e801941dd55d35dc1d8e988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/53096472f6911e4a2e801941dd55d35dc1d8e988"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGIzMDY2ZTFkNGM2MmI1Mzg4NGNhZjNhNWZhNDYxYTFiOTNmMDMxYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789","sha":"b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789"}],"sha":"b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b3066e1d4c62b53884caf3a5fa461a1b93f031c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:56:14Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:56:14Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"loop(context-v): the CardRow pilot executor\n\nThree members, chosen to disagree. The loop says plainly that the job is as much\nto produce evidence as a diff, and that an API which does not fit a member is a\nRESULT rather than a failure — do not contort the member, and do not reach for\nrung 4 on the first try, because an escape hatch used immediately means the API is\nwrong.\n\nEverything mechanical is inherited from the Button loop rather than forked, as the\nChip loop already does. What is new is a table mapping each pilot''s report to the\nopen decision it is evidence for: did the thin base fit or did you need a\nCardRow--<Kind> wrapper, did any name need explaining, which SelectWrapper and why\nwas the other one wrong here, and what does your member have that the other two do\nnot.\n\nOne rule is stricter than previous loops: never touch packages/. Three members\nediting shared-ui in parallel is how a component ends up with three incompatible\nAPIs in one evening. If the primitive is wrong, say so and stop.\n\nAnd one rule is new because of the Tuesday demo: additive where possible, and a\nmember left half-migrated is worse than one not started. Finish fewer surfaces\ncompletely and name what you left.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b6cf301452adec3ec16ecff54add1acd3e88c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/0b6cf301452adec3ec16ecff54add1acd3e88c7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGIyODMzNWIzMGRiZWI2MDE4ZjgwYTFhODBiMGU4MzIwMTBmNTY3ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133","sha":"45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133"}],"sha":"b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/b28335b30dbeb6018f80a1a80b0e832010f56789"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:56:14Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:56:14Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): CardRow and two SelectWrapper variants — first pass, deliberately thin\n\nSixteen of eighteen members are the same shape: controls up top, a generated list\nbelow. These are the first three pieces of it, built thin on purpose so the three\npilot members can answer the open decisions with evidence instead of argument.\n\nCardRow is one object in a list. It renders a <div>, has no onclick, and is not a\ncontrol — selection composes in from outside. It sets no margin, no width and no\nposition offset, because rung 0 says layout is the parent''s job and a\nListContainer will eventually be that parent.\n\nD1 stays open on purpose. This ships as a thin base; a member needing a distinct\nlook writes CardRow--<Kind>.svelte in its own src/ wrapping this. If three\nmembers'' wrappers turn out identical they promote; if they stay different the BEM\nnames already document the spread, because rg -o ''CardRow--\\w+'' | sort | uniq -c\nis a live catalogue either way. That rollup works whether the answer is one\ncomponent or sixteen, which is exactly why the question does not need answering\nyet.\n\nSelectWrapper--ClickBody obeys the operator''s rule: a select wrapper may NOT be a\nbutton wrapped around a card. Measured, every row surface in this federation\ncontains 3 to 23 controls and not one has zero, so a wrapping button would mean\ninteractive content inside interactive content in all sixteen — the defect removed\nfrom sort-filter-lens today, where the nested span measured 14x14, thirty-four\npercent of the WCAG target floor.\n\nSo it renders no wrapper element at all. One real button carries the accessible\nname and stretches across the nearest positioned ancestor with a pseudo-element;\nsiblings sit above the overlay and keep working. CardRow is position: relative for\nprecisely this reason.\n\nAnd it ENFORCES rather than documents: on mount it finds sibling controls that are\nposition:static — the ones that would be buried under the overlay and silently\nunclickable — and console-errors naming them. A convention living only in a\ncontext-v file gets violated by the fourth engineer who never reads it, which is\nthis morning''s lesson about sandboxes that are not asserted.\n\nSelectWrapper--ClickPrimary is the conservative sibling: only the primary label\nacts, so no overlay, no positioning contract, nothing to swallow. For dense rows,\nor where click-anywhere would make an adjacent destructive action feel dangerous.\n\nBoth names are spelled variants with no unnamed base, per the operator''s rule that\nyou spell the variant even when it is not strictly necessary. The name that sits\non the what-you-click axis is an agent leaning and flagged in both files as a\ncoin-flip against the operator''s original --SingleControl, which sits on the\nwhat-the-card-holds axis.\n\nsvelte-check clean across 90 files. Drift 71 -> 71. Nothing consumes these yet, so\nthis commit cannot break a member.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc4794e78c314456be5772ad7a49acf1f31534d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/bc4794e78c314456be5772ad7a49acf1f31534d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDQ1YjRkOWZhOTE1NWI4Yjk1ZWE4MmI4OTA3OWQyMTNlOGJiNDgxMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae","sha":"2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae"}],"sha":"45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/45b4d9fa9155b8b95ea82b89079d213e8bb48133"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:44:19Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:44:19Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): D5 — a layout is a parent whose job is layout\n\nThe operator''s Astro framing settles the conceptual question: layouts are just\ncomponents that happen to live in a layouts folder, and they nest. No separate\nmechanism, no special folder semantics.\n\nWhich means rung 0 already drew this line without anyone noticing. It says layout\nis the parent''s job — so a layout is a parent whose job is layout. That resolves\nnesting directly: nested parents, each owning placement of its own slot.\n\nThe operational test is whether the thing places children whose shape it\ndeliberately does not know. CardRow knows its children — title, meta, actions — so\nit is a component. ListContainer does not know what a CardRow is; it places a\nheader slot and a scroll region and does not care what lands in them. The\noperator''s LayoutHeader--FilterOptions and the two-column list-left/list-right\npattern both pass that test, so both are layouts, and that is fine.\n\nThe rule that stops \"layout\" from becoming a word with no information is token\nownership: a layout may set spacing, placement and container width; a component\nmay not. That is rung 0 restated from the other side, and it is the actual lever\non the layout issue — 912 raw paddings against 0 uses of var(--space-*). Members\nhand-roll spacing because nothing owns it. Give layouts the job and they stop,\nwhich beats asking nineteen teams to adopt a scale by discipline.\n\nOn naming, the operator offered FilterOptionsContainer--Header and\nLayoutHeader--FilterOptions and the rollup decides it. Structural role in the\nblock, domain in the modifier: rg ''ListContainer--'' answers every list surface we\nhave, and rg -- ''--FilterOptions'' answers everywhere filter options appear. Put\nthe domain in the block and the first rollup is lost while the second survives.\n\nMarked by author as the file now requires: the operator decided layouts are\ncomponents and that the examples qualify. The does-it-know-its-children test, the\ntoken-ownership rule and the naming direction are agent leanings and stay open —\nnone blocks code until the first ListContainer is written.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92df9ae13537038a3198ebd14bf3149855d53951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/92df9ae13537038a3198ebd14bf3149855d53951"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDJhMDllZmU5Yzk3ODI0Y2VlNDQ5ODE4ZWNiYzZjNTZjNWM2NjBjYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0","sha":"885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0"}],"sha":"2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2a09efe9c97824cee449818ecbc6c56c5c660cae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:42:25Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:42:25Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui, spec): rung 4 is style=, not class= — the escape hatch never worked\n\nThe override ladder shipped saying rung 4 was class= plus data-deviation. The\nfirst time anyone exercised it — building the federal gallery — it did not work,\nand how it failed is the part worth keeping.\n\nSvelte compiles a component''s scoped rules to .ui-btn.svelte-<hash>, which is\n(0,2,0). A member''s rung-4 class is (0,1,0). It loses every property the component\nsets WHILE RENDERING PERFECTLY AND LOOKING LIKE A WORKING OVERRIDE. The gallery''s\nfirst rung-4 fixture showed justify-content: center and read as a success.\n\nDropping our own selector to :where(.ui-btn) does not fix it. Svelte still appends\nthe hash, so the component lands at (0,1,0) and TIES the member''s class — and a\ntie resolves by stylesheet order, which under Module Federation is chunk load\norder across independently deployed remotes. That is not decidable. A\nnondeterministic override is worse than one that reliably loses, because it works\nin dev and differs in production.\n\nSo rung 4 is an inline style=, which beats every class rule regardless of load\norder. Still declared, still requires data-deviation, still surfaces in the\nmember''s catalog under Deviations, and if anything uglier at the call site — which\nis correct for the last rung.\n\nclass= still passes through and is still a declared deviation, but it can only win\nfor properties the component does NOT set. A member hook, not an override.\n\nBoth primitives now require data-deviation for style= as well as class=, so the\ncountability the ladder depends on survives the change.\n\nAnd a real bug found while making it: Chip spread {...rest} AFTER style={radiusStyle},\nso passing both radius and style silently dropped the radius. The two are merged\nnow rather than one clobbering the other. Nobody hit it because rung 4 had no call\nsites — which is the same reason nobody hit the specificity problem.\n\nWhy nineteen members never found this: rung 4 has ZERO real call sites. The escape\nhatch we have been treating as the detection mechanism had never once been\nexercised. That is its own finding about escape hatches — an unused one is\nindistinguishable from a working one.\n\nGates 71 -> 71, S1-S5 pass, svelte-check clean, docs-portal builds.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f90835a0c51ebdc06e98df64bb878707864c23b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/f90835a0c51ebdc06e98df64bb878707864c23b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDg4NTk1NWE4MGMwYzZjYWJmNDFhMjM3YzhlMGFhOGNjOGEyMzA1YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52","sha":"3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52"}],"sha":"885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/885955a80c0c6cabf41a237c8e0aa8cc8a2305c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:39:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:39:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): an open decision is a signal, not a debt — and record who closed what\n\nTwo corrections to how this file works, both from the operator.\n\nFirst, the usage rule pushed toward closing. It said the agent \"resolves them as\nthe work reaches them, writes the outcome into the Decided line, and does not stop\nto ask\", which reads as an instruction to tidy. It now says the opposite where it\nmatters: leaving a decision open is the CORRECT outcome, not a debt. An open\ndecision is how we know to come back to it, and closing one early to tidy the file\ndestroys exactly the signal the file exists to carry. Resolve when the work forces\nit — when code cannot be written without an answer — and not before. A leaning is\nenough until then, and a leaning is not a decision.\n\nSecond, and this is the failure I actually committed: D3 recorded the operator''s\nrule and four of my own judgement calls under one \"Decided\" line, as though they\ncarried the same weight. They do not. The operator decided that a SelectWrapper\nmay not wrap a card containing controls and that the cases get distinct named\nvariants — that is settled. Whether the family is named on what-you-click or on\nwhat-the-card-holds, whether --SingleControl becomes --ClickPrimary, whether\nrow-as-anchor is a separate organ, and whether --Radio is built are MINE, and\nthree of the four are close calls.\n\nAn agent''s judgement recorded as settled reads, six weeks later, like something\nthe team agreed, and nobody will know to revisit it. So entries now say who closed\nthem, and D3 splits into the operator''s rule plus four explicitly-open leanings.\nThe --SingleControl rename is flagged as a genuine coin-flip that should be\noverturned if the team reasons about card composition rather than click target.\n\nNone of the four blocks writing code. The first --ClickBody call site forces one\nof them; the rest can stay open indefinitely, which is the point.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d15178d2912b81b410b48c61d6147fa1a739fa26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/d15178d2912b81b410b48c61d6147fa1a739fa26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDMzNjc4NjQwOTJmZDI5ZjBhZmI4ZTYxNjVlYTRlMTFlMTZiNTNkNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e","sha":"d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e"}],"sha":"3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/3367864092fd29f0afb8e6165ea4e11e16b53d52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:38:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:38:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): D3''s variant family — name on what you click, enforce what the card holds\n\nThe operator proposed SelectWrapper--SingleControl and --ClickBody and asked for a\nread. The useful observation is that those two names sit on DIFFERENT AXES, and\nmixing axes is where component families rot — two variants can both be true of one\ncard.\n\nAxis A is what you click, which is what the engineer actually chooses. Axis B is\nwhat the card contains, which is a constraint and is derived rather than chosen.\n--ClickBody is A; --SingleControl is B.\n\nSo: name on axis A, enforce axis B.\n\nThe family, grounded in sightings rather than invented — row''s primary control is\na button (8), whole-surface click (the --ClickBody case), checkbox in a list (5\nmembers), radio (ZERO). Plus aria-pressed at 29 against aria-selected at 1, which\nsays the aria vocabulary in this codebase is almost entirely toggle-shaped today.\n\nTwo calls inside it. Rename --SingleControl to --ClickPrimary so it reads as a set\nwith --ClickBody: what do you click, the body or the primary? Flagged as a genuine\ncoin-flip if the team thinks in card composition rather than click target — the\noperator should overturn it freely. And row-as-anchor, 4 sightings, is NOT a\nSelectWrapper: those navigate rather than select, so they are CardRow--Link, and\nconflating them would put a navigation affordance inside a selection component.\n\nDo not build --Radio. Zero sightings, and shipping ahead of consumers is exactly\nhow the federal layer got a spacing scale sitting at 0 uses against 912 raw\npaddings.\n\nAxis B becomes the runtime check rather than a name, and the measurement earns it:\nevery row-rendering surface in the federation contains controls, minimum 3 and\nmaximum 23, not one has zero. So --ClickBody always needs the overlay here. On\nmount it queries its subtree for interactive descendants and console-errors with\ndata-a11y-error if it finds any, the same mechanism Button uses for size=\"icon\"\nwithout a name.\n\nThis replaces the earlier \"build --MultiControls first, defer the plain one\"\nframing, which mis-read the operator as deferring a variant when they were asking\nfor the family to be named.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4745e0f3ddc5f82a92ca5a44da0b6a41bf701563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/4745e0f3ddc5f82a92ca5a44da0b6a41bf701563"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGQwNWVlNTU3YTM5MzgwNGI5ZGNhY2JhZjIyZDk1Mzk2ZWRlN2E4MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a","sha":"1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a"}],"sha":"d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/d05ee557a393804b9dcacbaf22d95396ede7a80e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:38:10Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:38:10Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui, docs-portal): the federal primitives gallery — Button and Chip finally have a page\n\n388 call sites across 19 units and neither primitive had a specimen page anywhere.\nYou could not see six Button variants or six Chip tones side by side without\nreading source — which is how eleven renderings of one status value happened in\nthe first place.\n\nFive sections, ten entries, 29 fixtures: Choosing (the decision tree), Button,\nChip, the override ladder with a live specimen per rung, and the rest of\nshared-ui. 169 live primitive instances, measured in a real browser rather than\ninferred — 99 Buttons, 63 Chips, 5 ConfidencePills, plus 72 more across the\nthree-mode check.\n\nEvery claim the catalog makes was verified against the rendered page: sizes\n24/28/32/28², zero of 24 matrix buttons under the target floor, five dismiss\ntargets at 28x28 all named, a plain sm chip at 17px against a dismissible sm chip\nat 34px, revealOnHover at opacity 0 at rest, radius rungs resolving to 8/4.8/2px,\ntype=button not submitting and type=submit submitting, three modes yielding three\ndistinct primaries.\n\nrequest-reviewer''s library also ships. It had a catalog, a ./gallery expose and a\nstandalone branch — and no portal row and no remote, so it had been invisible\nsince it was written. The same hand-maintained-list failure S5 exists to catch one\nlevel up.\n\n## The audit caught a defect in the page that documents the audit\n\nOn its first run the classification tree''s count-slot measured 3.68:1. Replaced\nthe color-mix fill with a currentColor ring: 5.47. The gallery''s own Audit tab\nfound it, which is the argument for the gallery existing.\n\nZero F2/F3 leaks across all 24 Button/Chip/ladder fixtures — the ui-* namespace\nreservation works exactly as written. The one leak that remains is .pill on the\nConfidencePill fixtures, correct and deliberately NOT exempted, written up as a\ndeviation in that entry.\n\n## Three findings that matter beyond this page\n\nRung 4 of the override ladder does not work as specified. Svelte compiles\nButton''s rule to .ui-btn.svelte-<hash>, which is (0,2,0); a rung-4 class= alone is\n(0,1,0) and loses every property the component sets. The first fixture rendered\njustify-content: center and LOOKED like a working override. It has to be written\n.ui-btn.demo-rung-4, and even then wins only on source order. Rung 4 having zero\nreal call sites across nineteen members is probably why nobody noticed — the\nescape hatch we have been counting on has never been exercised.\n\nThe audit''s F8 literal check matches the cssText serialisation of\nborder: 1px solid transparent, so every Button and Chip specimen in every catalog\ncarries a permanent colour-literal finding for a declaration containing no colour\nliteral.\n\nAnd the focus-coverage repair is only half applied: the browser-normalised\n*:focus-visible strips to '''' and never enters the rule set, so a raw anchor\nreports \"no :focus-visible rule matches\" although the federal ring covers it.\nButtons and Chips pass only because they declare their own — it hits precisely the\nelements members are being told to converge onto.\n\n## Judgement call, and the contract change it required\n\nThe federal library is a separate FEDERAL_LIBRARY const with its own type, not a\ntwentieth element of MEMBER_LIBRARIES with a kind field. It differs from a member\nin all three things that file records: it is not a remote, it has no origin of its\nown, and ui-* is a reserved federal namespace rather than one member''s claim.\nFlattening that into an array with a discriminator would hide the exact\ndistinction the page exists to teach.\n\nOne contract change was genuinely required: rootClass: '''' is now legal. \"No root\nclass needed\" is the DEFINING property of the federal layer and the Catalog type\nhad no way to express it.\n\nRoot tsconfig gains packages/shared-ui in exclude, outside the brief and flagged\nby the engineer rather than slipped in. S1 fails without it, and the comment that\nused to read \"packages/shared-ui is .svelte only\" was true when written and\nstopped being true the moment the package gained a catalog. The prose was correct\nand became wrong with nobody touching it, which is the whole argument for the\ncheck.\n\nGates: 71 -> 71, contrast 30/30, S1-S5 pass, svelte-check clean across shared-ui,\ngallery, docs-portal, corpora-curator, request-reviewer and shell.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43d6d1acbc4fff20c4cd07a86cda00b591634e6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/43d6d1acbc4fff20c4cd07a86cda00b591634e6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDE4NTZmOWIyNGFjZWFkMjIxNmNlZjVmMzIwODU4OTAwMDU2MjgwM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4","sha":"c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4"}],"sha":"1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1856f9b24acead2216cef5f3208589000562803a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:36:29Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:36:29Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): D3 resolved — SelectWrapper--MultiControls, and the naming principle behind it\n\nThe operator''s call, and it is better than the leaning it replaces. A SelectWrapper\nmay not be wrapped around a card that contains controls; the multi-control case\ngets its own named component.\n\nThe earlier leaning hid the distinction inside one component that would quietly\nswitch strategies. That is worse for the reason that matters: an engineer reaching\nfor SelectWrapper would never learn the multi-control case is dangerous. The named\nvariant puts the hazard where the decision is made.\n\nSame principle as rung 3 of the override ladder — radius=\"lg/60\" is deliberately\ncountable because the escape hatch is also the detection mechanism.\n\nMeasured while resolving it, and it inverts the default: EVERY row-rendering\nsurface in the federation contains controls. Minimum 3, maximum 23, not one has\nzero. person-db-resolver has 23, affiliation-rating-resolver 21, org-workbench''s\nRelatedOrgs 16. So --MultiControls is the COMMON case and plain SelectWrapper has\nzero users today. Build the multi-control one first and leave the plain one\nunbuilt until a control-free card appears — shipping a component with no consumers\nis exactly how the federal layer ended up with a spacing scale at 0 uses against\n912 raw paddings. (Counts are file-level, so an upper bound per card; the shape is\nconfirmed by reading prompt-template-manager''s li, which holds a primary button\nand a sibling icon Button.)\n\nEnforcement rather than documentation: on mount, SelectWrapper queries its own\nsubtree for interactive descendants and console-errors if it finds any, the way\nButton already does for size=\"icon\" without a name and Chip for dismissible\nwithout a label. A convention that lives only in a context-v file will be violated\nby the fourth engineer who never reads it — today''s lesson, that a sandbox which\nis not asserted is not a sandbox.\n\nAnd the operator articulated a rule general enough to outlive this decision, so it\nis promoted out of D3 into its own section: spell the variant even when it is not\nstrictly necessary. It organises, it cues the reader before they open the file, it\nmakes ripgrep trivial, it enables script rollups with no doc to maintain, and it\ngives Graphify a real edge to draw. A distinction that exists only in a\nmaintainer''s head is invisible to every tool we own. A thing you can count is a\nthing you can govern — the same argument the override ladder makes for rung 3 and\nthe organ registry makes for fingerprints.\n\nFive decisions remain open.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b93e5d3f78cea5be747e82b550f1eaafa49c106b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/b93e5d3f78cea5be747e82b550f1eaafa49c106b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGMyNDgxZTQ3ZTVmNGQ4NjZmMjdlODBkMDg3MDM3YzIxMzk1MjhjYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b","sha":"71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b"}],"sha":"c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c2481e47e5f4d866f27e80d087037c2139528ca4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:29:28Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:29:28Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"decision(context-v): the list-surface paradigm, six open questions\n\nFirst file in context-v/decisions/ for this repo. The folder is experimental and\nthe context-vigilance skill describes it as \"artifacts of clear decisions made\" —\nthis one is deliberately open, status: Undecided, which sibling repos already\npractise as status: Open. Divergence surfaced rather than normalized, per the\nskill.\n\nAfter Button across 19 units and Chip across 13, the remaining raw controls\nstopped being a grab-bag and became one shape. Counted: SIXTEEN OF EIGHTEEN\nmembers have a header/controls region and an each-rendered list. SearXNG result\nlists, CSV import previews, People and Orgs filter lists, prompt pickers, corpus\nsource lists, connector palettes. That is not the next component, it is the shape\nof the product.\n\nAnd the structure is already written — prompt-template-manager:205 is an <aside>\nwith a heading and a Button, containing a <ul>, containing an each of <li> each\nholding a primary button and a sibling icon Button. Sixteen members arrived at\nthat independently.\n\nSix decisions, each with options, a leaning and what would settle it. The agent\nresolves them as the work reaches them and writes the outcome into the Decided\nline rather than stopping to ask.\n\nThe one worth reading first is D3, because it is a trap rather than a preference.\nSelection-as-composable-wrapper is the right instinct and matches how Radix and\nshadcn separate behaviour from presentation — but every row surface ALREADY\ncontains controls, seven of them in search-results and six in\nprompt-template-manager. If the wrapper renders a <button>, all sixteen members\nget interactive content inside interactive content: the exact defect removed from\nsort-filter-lens today, where a span role=button nested in a button measured\n14x14, thirty-four percent of the WCAG target floor. So the wrapper is never a\nbutton; the primary label is the real control, stretched by a pseudo-element\noverlay, with sibling actions positioned above it.\n\nD4 carries the number that argues for Selector existing at all: six role=\"menu\"\ndeclarations across the federation, ZERO arrow-key handlers, four with no\nmenuitem children, plus a role=\"radiogroup\" with no radios. Every one announces a\nkeyboard widget the member does not implement. Six members getting it wrong\nindependently is not carelessness — the roving-tabindex contract is the substance\nof the organ.\n\nD5 notes that the layout issue''s own expiry condition — three independent members\nreaching for the same shape — is long past at sixteen, and that ListContainer is a\nbetter route into the federal layer than the abstract spacing system that issue\nimagined. padding: var(--space-*) is still at zero uses against 912 raw paddings.\nLayout arrives as a component, not as a doctrine.\n\nAnd D1 records why the one-component-versus-many question does not need answering\nyet: BEM modifier names make it reversible, because grep ''CardRow--'' aggregates\nthe population either way. That convention is already house — shared-ui ships\nToggleHeader__PromptOrPackage--Icons.svelte today.\n\nNon-goals are stated explicitly, including that this is NOT an attempt to contort\none component into sixteen appearances.\n\nRefs #101 #105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"235ec152c5f3cbf5a9b9b1f1fd1908b013bc7688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/235ec152c5f3cbf5a9b9b1f1fd1908b013bc7688"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDcxMDQwNzI5YTgzZjFhZTE3NzIzNmU1N2VlNTM0MTU4NTM5ZWM2MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06","sha":"2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06"}],"sha":"71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/71040729a83f1ae177236e57ee534158539ec62b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:03:16Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:03:16Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(gallery): reserve the ui-* namespace instead of enumerating federal classes\n\nThe containment audit flags any class that does not carry the member''s prefix.\nThat is correct for a member''s own CSS and wrong for a federal component''s, because\nthe member CANNOT prefix a class it does not emit — shared-ui does. So every\ncatalog carried ''ui-btn'' by hand, and Chip made it four entries, and a future\nprimitive with a child element would have meant editing every catalog that had\nalready adopted it.\n\naudit.ts already solves this exact shape one line above, for Svelte''s scoping\nhash, with a comment explaining that exemptClasses is the wrong tool because any\nlisted value goes stale. Federal component classes are the same category, so they\nget the same treatment.\n\nDeliberately a NAMESPACE RESERVATION rather than a shape match, and the reasoning\nis the operator''s: buttons, chips and cards are the highest-traffic paradigms in\nany design system, and they are EXPECTED to accumulate many classes — varieties\nthat differ in look, in structural layout, in which params they take, in what\nactions they enable, in what they call and with what arguments. That growth is the\nsystem working. A check that treats each new one as a finding would be training\npeople to ignore it, which is the opposite of what the audit is for.\n\nSo the rule is ui-* is federal, full stop, and it does not matter how many there\neventually are.\n\nThe trade, stated: a member that names its own class ui-something is now silently\nexempted rather than flagged. Accepted — that convention is worth enforcing\nregardless, and the alternative is a check that goes stale every time a primitive\ngrows.\n\nFive entries come out of the two existing catalogs. ListRow will cost zero.\n\nsvelte-check clean across gallery, corpora-curator and request-reviewer.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9cb9d1ddf08cb6e919332098978c5c3cbafa5a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/a9cb9d1ddf08cb6e919332098978c5c3cbafa5a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDJiNDE2ZDVmNTZlNjM1ZWI1MTdjZjhhZDZjYzUwMTY5MTcxMzdhMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5","sha":"197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5"}],"sha":"2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/2b416d5f56e635eb517cf8ad6cc5016917137a06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:13:09Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:13:09Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(shared-ui, loop): Chip''s dismiss was a target reduction, its hover was invisible, and its headline symptom was wrong\n\nThree defects in the component and its loop, all found by engineers measuring at\nreal call sites rather than reading the header.\n\n## The symptom was wrong, and it sent someone looking for a defect that was not there\n\nChip''s header, the Chip loop and the containment refactor all claimed that in the\nnested-interactive case \"the outer control''s accessible name absorbs the glyph.\"\nMeasured at the call site: it does NOT. That button carries an explicit aria-label,\nso its name was always correct and never contained the x.\n\nThe real defects were HTML validity, an inner control whose accessible name was\nliterally \"x\", and a target measuring 14 x 14 — 196 square pixels against a 576\nsquare pixel floor, THIRTY-FOUR PERCENT of WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8. That is a far worse\nfinding than the one I wrote down, and stating it wrongly cost an engineer a\nsearch. Corrected in both files, with the correction marked rather than quietly\nswapped.\n\n## The dismiss was a target REDUCTION\n\n.ui-chip__dismiss sized from --control-h-sm, so it landed at exactly 24px — on the\nWCAG floor, where the <Button size=\"icon\"> it replaces sat 4px clear at 28. The\nfirst dismissible adoption therefore measured 28 -> 24 and reported it honestly as\na trade. It should not have been a trade. A dismiss is a real control and now gets\nthe real control size.\n\n## The hover was correct and imperceptible\n\nChip''s dismiss hover and Button''s ghost hover were both moved to a\nsurface-independent wash of the text colour this morning, which fixed a real bug:\nthey had been using --color-selected-tint, which is exactly what the chips hosting\nthem are painted with. But two engineers then measured the repaired version at\n1.22 to 1.47:1 against the chip''s own ground and said the quiet part — correct is\nnot the same as perceptible. 14% becomes 22%, the smallest step that reads as a\nstate change on every tone.\n\n## Loop additions from the same reports\n\nThe decision tree pointed the wrong way for a token INSIDE a control''s label — a\nrank circle or count badge in a Button. Those are painted against the control''s\nsurface and usually inherit currentColor from its variant; a Chip paints its own\nground from page-level tokens and would erase the selected-state cue. They stay\nraw and the count-slot organ gets raised.\n\nRung 0 has a Chip-specific regression the Button list did not cover: a Chip in a\ncolumn-flex parent stretches to the column, and --radius-pill makes that far more\nvisible than a small-radius badge ever was. One measured at 854px wide. It\nstretched before the migration too — a 3px band reads as a band and an 854px pill\nreads as a mistake.\n\nAnd two more confidently-wrong-pass traps. color-mix() serialises to\ncolor(srgb r g b / a), so a contrast parser that only knows rgba() returns 1.00 for\nevery hover measurement — indistinguishable from a hover that paints nothing. And\ntwo Svelte syntax limits that bite the obvious way to write a tone map.\n\nStill open and raised, not fixed: Chip emits four classes where Button emits one,\nso every adopting catalog carries four exemptClasses entries. Button''s own header\nexplains why it avoided exactly that. Worth a decision before the next primitive.\n\nFederation 71 -> 71, contrast 30/30, svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"984273179c062e98a9175f473b051a29adef04fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/984273179c062e98a9175f473b051a29adef04fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDE5NzgwOGZmYTc2NmJhZjhiYjJkZGU1YzMxZTQzYTQwNTk3NWQ0ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6","sha":"bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6"}],"sha":"197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/197808ffa766baf8bb2dde5c31e43a405975d4e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:12:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:12:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(sort-filter-lens): six Chips, and the nested interactive control that was 34% of the target floor\n\nSix chip-shaped sites become six <Chip>. Ten rule-sets and 42 declarations\ndeleted, net -27 lines. Rung 1 only plus rung 0 once. Zero deviations. All fifteen\nexisting Buttons untouched, and two new ones added.\n\n## The flagship case, resolved as a sibling pair\n\nThis member shipped a <span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"> INSIDE a <Button>. Both\nact — the body toggles sort direction, the x removes the key — so it is not a\ndismissible Chip. It is a Button plus a sibling Button size=\"icon\" in a rung-0\nwrapper, which is what the loop prescribes for exactly this shape.\n\n  element      span role=button      ->  real <button>, sibling\n  size         14 x 14               ->  28 x 28\n  name         \"x\"                   ->  \"Remove sort key 1: corpus_count\"\n  nested       2                     ->  0\n\n14 x 14 is 196 square pixels against a 576 square pixel floor — THIRTY-FOUR\nPERCENT of WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8. A live failure, not a marginal one.\n\n## And a correction to three documents, including my own\n\nChip''s header comment, the Chip loop and the containment refactor all say the\nouter control''s accessible name \"absorbs the glyph.\" Measured at the actual call\nsite: it does not. That outer button carries an explicit aria-label, so its name\nwas always correct and never contained the x. The real defects were HTML validity,\nthe 14x14 target, and an inner control whose accessible name was \"x\". The\njustification for Chip stands; the stated symptom was wrong and sent an engineer\nlooking for a name defect that was not there.\n\n## The rest\n\nA failed corpus add was drawn in amber, using the warn foreground. A failure is\nerror, red in all three modes. The Lens badge spent accent on what names a KIND of\nmember rather than the current one.\n\nThe cold corpus chip drew its border at 1.34:1 light and 1.69:1 dark, far under\nthe 3:1 non-text floor. Now 3.06 / 3.23 / 3.00.\n\nFound by measuring, and it is the containment breach biting the member that ships\nit: .corpus-chip.loading rendered 87 x 66px instead of 71 x 21, because this\nmember''s own unprefixed global .loading — written for a page-level \"Loading rows…\"\nparagraph — also matched the chip''s state class. Gone, since the chip no longer\ncarries .loading.\n\nLeaked unprefixed class names 50 -> 45, incidental rather than aimed at. The live\ncollisions named in the refactor doc are untouched, and the one class added is\nsfl-prefixed.\n\nEighteen captures — two builds, three modes, three states — with the probe driven\nthrough expand-row, type-URL, Add. A fourth defence specific to this member: the\nstub has no corpus.add case at all, so it throws, and there was no code path from\nthe probe to a write.\n\nMember gate 4 -> 4. svelte-check clean, one pre-existing autofocus warning.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14b0a8ae8ec1c2e872aa16bd67d0e3f5ac2908aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/14b0a8ae8ec1c2e872aa16bd67d0e3f5ac2908aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGJkZTYyNjEzYTQyYjJhNmRkYzVjYzJiYTI4MDBjZjI4ODg3MjA5ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977","sha":"c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977"}],"sha":"bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/bde62613a42b2a6ddc5cc2ba2800cf28887209e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:12:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:12:11Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(corpora-curator): eleven Chips, and five remove buttons that all announced \"remove tag\"\n\nEleven authored chip sites become eleven <Chip>, fifteen rendered instances before\nand after in all three modes — no chip lost, none invented. Seven rule-sets and 30\ndeclarations deleted. Rung 1 only, plus rung 0 twice. Zero deviations. Eight\nButtons untouched.\n\nThe a11y win here is the accessible name, not the target size. Every tag''s remove\ncontrol announced the identical \"remove tag\", so five tags meant five\nindistinguishable controls. dismissLabel names each one now — \"remove tag\nWork-Based-Learning\".\n\nAnd the honest trade, stated rather than buried: the dismiss target went 28x28\nDOWN to 24x24, because Chip''s dismiss sizes from --control-h-sm where\n<Button size=\"icon\"> used --control-h-md. It still clears the WCAG floor, but it\nsits exactly on it where it used to sit 4px clear. Raised federally.\n\nThe connection status drew idle, connecting and auth_required as one\nundifferentiated grey — three conditions rendering identically. Three tones now.\nAnd metadata-only is deliberately neutral rather than warn, because warn would\nmark every un-fetched source in the corpus as a defect when it is simply a\nresting state.\n\nBoth tone maps live in types.ts so the app and the gallery cannot drift apart.\n\nFound by measuring: the detail-panel status chip rendered 854px wide, because\n.cc-field is column-flex and the chip stretched. It stretched before too — but a\n3px-radius band reads as a band, and an 854px pill reads as a mistake. Rung 0\nwrapper.\n\nA comment in App.svelte claimed secondary was distinguishable from the pills by\nboundary colour. Measured, that was inverted: the pill and the Button shared an\nidentical fill and differed only by border. Now both use --color-border-strong and\nthe separation is the fill, a step lighter. Comment rewritten with the numbers.\n\nrevealOnHover deliberately NOT passed: there is no opacity:0, visibility:hidden or\nhover-reveal anywhere in this member''s CSS at HEAD, so passing it would have\nINTRODUCED a hover-only affordance rather than preserved one. Reasoning left in\nthe file.\n\nMember gate 2 -> 2. 12/12 tests pass. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8eee1fd637ff52d25a3136fe3350f0f6d620e5a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/8eee1fd637ff52d25a3136fe3350f0f6d620e5a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGM1MjY4MjQyMWRhZTQ5N2U1NzBjN2U0MmE5NDM4NjVhMDVmZTc5Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45","sha":"8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45"}],"sha":"c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c52682421dae497e570c7e42a943865a05fe7977"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:11:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:11:32Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"chore(response-reviewer): remove probe artifacts committed by mistake, and ignore the path\n\nThe Chip commit for this member swept in eight files under probe/before/ — a\nthrowaway rsbuild harness built to render the pre-change tree for the before/after\nmeasurement. It is build scaffolding, not source, and it does not belong in git.\n\nMy error, not the engineer''s: I staged with a directory-wide `git add\napps/response-reviewer` rather than naming the source files, and the harness rode\nalong. The engineer''s report said the probe was deleted; what it deleted was the\nprobe''s own config and driver, leaving the archived before-tree behind.\n\nRemoved, and the path is now gitignored for both apps/*/probe/ and shell/probe/ so\na stray harness can never be swept in this way again. The loop already requires\ndeleting the probe before the final gate; the ignore is the mechanical backstop\nfor when that is done incompletely, which is the same \"assert it, don''t intend it\"\nlesson the alias incident produced this morning.\n\nNo source file is affected — member gate holds at 9, and the Chip work in this\nmember is unchanged.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc372f269e7308ab0e5f678bb9d57cb0ed058d73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/dc372f269e7308ab0e5f678bb9d57cb0ed058d73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDhkNGU2ZTU2YmNiODRjNmZhZDVhOWMyNTJmZmQ0N2YzYzZlY2ZkNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76","sha":"e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76"}],"sha":"8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/8d4e6e56bcb84c6fad5a9c252ffd47f3c6ecfd45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"cleanup(person-enrichment, records-surface): six stale deviations that outlived rung 0\n\nSix data-deviation declarations removed, the layout fix kept in every case. Four\nin person-enrichment, two in records-surface, and every one of them said some\nversion of \"the ladder has no rung for layout.\"\n\nIt has one. Rung 0 landed this morning, after five layout-only overrides across\nthree members made it undeniable that placement was being routed through the\ndeviation mechanism because the mechanism was the only door in the building. These\nsix were written before that and are annotations that outlived their reason.\n\nThey were also actively harmful. The Deviations catalog only works if it is short\nenough that someone reads it, and a catalog listing six margin adjustments teaches\nits reader to skim — which is exactly where a real deviation would hide.\n\nThree prose comments are corrected alongside, because leaving them would have the\ncode and the commentary disagreeing: two rule headers reading \"Override-ladder\nrung 4\" and a block claiming the fix was \"declared at each of the four call sites\nas rung 4.\" The mechanism explanations underneath, about why the :global() nesting\nis required, are untouched and still true.\n\nWith search-and-add''s cleanup landing in the same wave, the federation-wide\ndata-deviation count is now exactly ONE — a colour deviation in records-surface''s\npromote bar, where the variant enum genuinely has no success or confirm member.\nThat is a real gap in the API, declared in the right place, and it is now visible\nbecause nothing else is crowding it.\n\nPhase 2 of the tidy plan is complete.\n\nBoth member gates unchanged, 2 -> 2 and 3 -> 3.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"62cd6f51e7a0861dd393dc91458618392c0d76c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/62cd6f51e7a0861dd393dc91458618392c0d76c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGUzMDRmODA5OTk4YWY1YmUwZTU0ZmExYmVjYjUwYjE5ZTY2YTBiNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865","sha":"1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865"}],"sha":"e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e304f809998af5be0e54fa1becb50b19e66a0b76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(shell): two Chips in the host, and the hashed-selector property preserved\n\nFour candidates examined, two adopted, two rule blocks deleted. No rungs used, no\nCSS added — so the host''s measured property from the Button rollout holds exactly:\n141 selectors, every one hashed. grep ui-chip across shell/src returns nothing, so\nno member CSS reaches into the component''s internals.\n\nThe measurable win is the boundary, which is finding two on the recurring list:\nthe env tag''s border was --color-border at 1.74:1 dark, 1.23:1 light and 1.55:1\nvibrant, all under the 3:1 floor. Now --color-border-strong at 3.23 / 3.06 / 3.00.\nFont 9px -> 11px; 9px was below the type scale''s smallest step.\n\nrole=\"status\" survives on the copied chip, confirmed by querying [role=\"status\"]\nin the live DOM and getting the ui-chip back. The live region is the entire point\nof that element.\n\nTwo correctly left alone. The queue badge is a circular count inside a Button''s\nlabel — min-width and height and radius and background and colour and font all\noverridden simultaneously to adopt it, which negates the base recipe rather than\nadjusting it, and the tone table would map a count to neutral, silencing an\naccent-filled arrival signal whose whole job is to be loud. It carries no\naria-live, checked. And the didi badge is chip-shaped but is a <summary> — a\nnative disclosure control, so converting it would break the <details>.\n\nThe probe caught its own confidently-wrong pass twice. A menu item''s label is not\nits function here, so the first selector rendered nothing — indistinguishable from\na broken conversion. And the fixture''s display names were deliberately SHORTENED\non the second pass, because long names widened the menu past its 220px min-width\nand would have hidden the exact wrap regression this file documents. At the real\nwidth: option rows 28/28/28px, before and after, all three modes.\n\nMember gate 12 -> 12. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"211358cc343bd73c28ad72ad8ba9ef7952ebf107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/211358cc343bd73c28ad72ad8ba9ef7952ebf107"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDE3NzRjM2FkNDRjZDMxMTBmZDY2ZTc2MzhkYTcwMjI1MjcxYTE4NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564","sha":"77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564"}],"sha":"1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1774c3ad44cd3110fd66e7638da70225271a1865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(enhanced-records-list): two Chips, and four connection states that rendered identically\n\nOne recipe and one unstyled cell become two call sites rendering seven instances.\nNo rungs used. The six filter chips converted to Buttons last rollout stay\nButtons, verified with aria-pressed and five real disabled attributes intact in\nall three modes.\n\nThe find: .erl-status.open was the ONLY state rule in the member, so four of five\nconnection states rendered as plain muted text. closed and error — the two that\nmean the surface is dead — were drawn exactly like connecting, the benign one. A\nuser watching that strip could not tell a dropped socket from a handshake in\nprogress.\n\nFive states now carry four tones plus a dot, with the word unchanged beside it, so\nthe dot is a second encoding rather than the only one.\n\nThe density worry about a chip per row was unfounded and measured rather than\nassumed: table row height 34.7px before, 34.7px after.\n\nThis is the member where the alias trap actually bites — it imports the workspace\n— and the probe verified three ways before reading a number: the sentinel present\nin both bundles, four real-workspace fingerprints each grepping zero, and sockets\nand fetch killed in addInitScript. The fixture was shaped from the member''s own\npredicates, since auto-select only fires on a promotion set or a CSV with more\nthan ten columns, and one derivation covering three of six rows so the origin\nbadge rendered both its branches.\n\nMember gate 2 -> 2. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92982d959633fe11161d337f318cc938a1acb664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/92982d959633fe11161d337f318cc938a1acb664"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDc3MTU2OTYxYTE5NzJjYTk5N2E0NTY2ZjQzMjY0YmI4MTI4OWM1NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1","sha":"c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1"}],"sha":"77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/77156961a1972ca997a4566f43264bb81289c564"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(docs-portal): 157 contrast-ratio chips, half of which were themselves unreadable\n\nTwo recipes become six call sites rendering 157 instances. Two rule blocks\ndeleted. No rungs used at all.\n\nThe irony is the finding. This is the surface that displays the design system''s\ncontrast ratios, and .ratio.ungraded — 75 of the 150 grid cells — carried\nopacity: 0.45 over already-muted text and measured 2.11:1 dark, 1.80:1 light,\n2.28:1 vibrant. Half the contrast report was itself a live WCAG 1.4.3 failure.\nNow 5.47 / 4.57 / 6.46.\n\nOne tone mapping where meaning beat colour: a ratio that clears 3:1 but not 4.5:1\nis usable for a line and not for text — a risk, not a failure. The member drew it\nwith the medium-confidence token; it is warn now.\n\nPass and large previously differed ONLY in text colour — same ground, no border,\nsame size. They now differ in background, boundary and foreground.\n\nThe generic .chip in this host was deliberately not touched, and the reasoning is\nmeasured rather than assumed: members.ts registers exactly one live gallery, whose\nmarkup is cc-prefixed and uses no .chip, .cell, .grid or .ratio. So the collision\nis latent, not live — except that chat ships a bare class=\"chip\" and would be\nrestyled the day it publishes a gallery.\n\nOne containment breach IS live today, though: the bare `section` selector at\napp.css:31 reaches the two <section> elements in the mounted guest''s gallery. That\nis Phase 3, raised not fixed.\n\nThe Tier 1 palette entry is correctly not a Chip — its primary content is a 22x22\ncolour block, the thing being judged, not a label. Chip''s dot is a 4px decorative\nround. Raised as a specimen-card organ.\n\n157 of 157 rendered and measured in both builds across three modes, with the\nsentinel grepped out of both bundles and .ratio present in the before CSS and\nabsent from the after.\n\nMember gate 3 -> 3. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11c1efc72b3264290b0c3f5ded870f98827484df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/11c1efc72b3264290b0c3f5ded870f98827484df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGM5NGQwNTY4MTMyYmEzNDRiYzc0Y2NjZDBhNGM2MGQ2MTFjYjEzZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148","sha":"6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148"}],"sha":"c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/c94d0568132ba344bc74cccd0a4c60d611cb13f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:10:54Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"fix(theme, shared-ui): Chip''s accent tone was failing the floor its own header promises\n\nChip''s header says every tone clears 4.5:1 in all three modes. Its accent tone\nmeasured 4.42:1 in light. Two independent migration agents measured it in their\nprobes before anyone re-read the header, which is the system working — and the\ncontrast gate passed 30 of 30 straight through it, which is the gate not working,\nbecause it walks TEXT pairs and a chip paints its own ground.\n\nThe cause is that the accent ground is an 8-9% wash of primary over the page, so\nin light mode the foreground and the background are the same hue a shade apart.\nDark measures 5.16 and vibrant 6.42; only light is under.\n\nFixed the way every other tone already handles light: a Tier 1 ink. --color__magenta-ink\nat #873ab9 joins red-ink, amber-ink and green-ink, which exist for exactly this\nreason, and a new --color-accent-fg carries it per mode — primary in dark and\nvibrant where primary is already legible on its own wash, magenta-ink in light\nwhere it is not. 5.35:1.\n\nChip''s accent now reads --color-accent-fg rather than --color-primary, for both\nthe text and the boundary.\n\nWorth recording how this was found, because it is the argument for the probes\ncosting what they cost: one agent hit it on a done-count badge and deliberately\ndid NOT route around it by choosing a different tone, on the reasoning that\npicking a tone to dodge a broken token is how the defect stays invisible. It kept\nthe semantically correct tone and raised the token. That is the right instinct and\nit is the only reason this is fixed today.\n\nFederation 71 -> 71, contrast 30/30, S1-S5 pass, svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101 #106\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1d313173725d97e46a8fc4fe1b4717b5144ea02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/d1d313173725d97e46a8fc4fe1b4717b5144ea02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDZmZmJjMGNmNDUzNGJhYzRjZDJhMTc0MDJkNjc3NjBhZjBmNjgxNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9","sha":"4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9"}],"sha":"6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/6ffbc0cf4534bac4cd2a17402d67760af0f68148"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:09:13Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:09:13Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(search-results): five Chips in a 420px rail, and two socket states that had no colour at all\n\nNine chip-shaped elements become five call sites rendering nine instances. Eight\nrule-sets deleted. Rung 0 only, no deviations. Twelve Buttons and both declared\nraw holdouts untouched.\n\nEvery number here was measured at 420px, the rail''s real width, not at a desktop\nviewport.\n\nTwo of five socket states had no rule in the stylesheet at all. connecting and\nauth_required rendered as undifferentiated grey, readable only by their word —\nso the member had five states and three appearances. They are info and warn now,\nwhich is the same mapping four other members arrived at independently this wave.\n\n\"Overdue\" was drawn with the error tokens, and the member''s own tooltip says\n\"past 1.5x the typical duration — IT MAY STILL LAND.\" That is degraded, not\nfailed. It is warn, and the tooltip and the colour finally agree.\n\nThe team target label was tinted with 25% accent while its two siblings were not —\nthree members of one category, one of them coloured. The text already names each,\nso the tint was carrying nothing, and it measured 2.59:1 doing it. Neutral now,\n5.47:1, no information lost.\n\nSeven contrast pairs under 4.5:1 go to one. Five chip heights become one, five\nfont sizes become one, two radii become one.\n\nThe one remaining failure is deliberately NOT routed around: the done-count badge\nis genuinely accent — a count of searches finished and waiting on you is the thing\nin focus — and the federal accent tone measures 4.43:1 in light mode. Choosing\nneutral to dodge a broken token is how the defect stays invisible, so the correct\ntone stays and the token is raised.\n\nAlso raised rather than converged: search-and-add''s .saa-chip is NOT the twin of\n.srq-chip despite the name. One has cursor:pointer, a disabled state and an active\nstate — it is a provider toggle, a Button. The other is a non-interactive target\nlabel, a Chip. Same name, opposite classifications, two members. Worth knowing\nbefore someone converges them by name.\n\nSix controls sit under the 24px target floor and none of them are chips — they are\ninline text links in the accept surfaces, measured at 13 to 19px. Unchanged by\nthis diff; the fix is a link-target pass.\n\nNine of nine rendered and measured across three driven states in both builds, plus\n33 paired gallery measurements. Zero console errors in every run.\n\nMember gate 3 -> 3, byte-identical. svelte-check clean across 91 files.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f090aefc730e70ec999813a44a4e8e15b66345b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/5f090aefc730e70ec999813a44a4e8e15b66345b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDRkN2Q5YzRmNzk0MTZmZjBjOWEwNzUxZTAwMmVkNGM2ZTRhZjQyZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1","sha":"79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1"}],"sha":"4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/4d7d9c4f79416ff0c9a0751e002ed4c6e4af42e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:09:13Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:09:13Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(response-reviewer): 23 Chips, and eight places the colour disagreed with the meaning\n\nFifty chip-shaped elements become 23 call sites rendering 50 instances. 34\nrule-sets deleted, app.css 1066 -> 915. Rung 0 only, no deviations, and all 30\nButtons untouched — the probe confirms identical .ui-btn counts before and after\nin all three view modes.\n\nThe convergence is the headline: ten distinct chip heights become one, seven\ndistinct font sizes become one, three radii become one. Measured, not estimated.\n\nEight sites where the member''s colour and the label''s meaning disagreed:\n\nAn outcome of \"skipped\" was painted GREEN, using the high-confidence token —\nso the one outcome meaning \"we did not look\" read as the one meaning \"we looked\nand it was good.\" It is info now.\n\n\"Unsaved\" was drawn as an error on a danger tint. An unsaved edit is\npending-with-risk, not a failure; it is warn.\n\nTwo provider badges and a prompt badge spent accent and accent-2 on what are\ncategory labels, and \"corpus warm\" spent accent on a verified fact. Pending and\npartial and needs-rerun were three more accents doing warn''s job.\n\nOne of those conversions LOST information and it is raised rather than hidden:\nthe prompt badge and the pack badge render different things — a prompt name\nversus a pack id — and the only signal distinguishing them was hue. That was a\n1.4.1 failure before and it is an information loss after. The fix is a text\nchange, which is content, not a component diff.\n\nSix contrast pairs under 4.5:1 go to zero. The worst was 3.45:1, and it was the\nsame --color-text-muted-on---color-border pairing that has now appeared in five\nmembers sharing no code. A boundary token being used as a surface.\n\nOne finding only a probe control could produce: .resp-app h3 pushes\ntext-transform: uppercase and letter-spacing into every component nested inside\nit. The same Chip measures \"text-transform: none, 62.17px\" inside a rung-0 slot\nand \"uppercase, 0.64px letter-spacing, 73.58px\" without one — rendering \"SAVING…\"\ninstead of \"saving…\". Neutralised on the slot rather than by touching the h3 rule.\n\nOne declared holdout worth its reasoning: a chip carrying a page title or raw URL\ntruncates at 18em with an ellipsis, and Chip models no truncation. Measured 213px\nlegacy versus 445px as a Chip. text-overflow cannot be re-applied from a member\nstylesheet because .ui-chip is inline-flex, so the ellipsis never reaches the\nlabel child — and styling that child from outside is reaching into the component.\n\nFifty of fifty rendered and measured across three view modes, in both a\ngit-archive before-build and the working tree, plus 111 paired gallery\nmeasurements. Each view mode in a FRESH browser context, because the persisted\nview-mode leaked between loads and silently measured by-record three times.\n\nMember gate 9 -> 9. svelte-check clean across 90 files.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23b9c6389e73666b74c58c9cb64fd195e5b8c0f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/23b9c6389e73666b74c58c9cb64fd195e5b8c0f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDc5OTUzZTVmZjM4OTc1MzJhYWM0MGY0MzUzMWNjNTFiYzFlZWUyZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d","sha":"87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d"}],"sha":"79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/79953e5ff3897532aac40f43531cc51bc1eee2f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:08:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:08:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(search-and-add): three Chips, and the last stale deviation leaves the federation\n\nThree chip-shaped call sites become three <Chip>. Three rule-sets deleted. Rung 0\nonly. And this member''s data-deviation goes 1 -> 0, which — with the cleanups the\nother agents landed in person-enrichment and records-surface — takes the\nFEDERATION-WIDE count to exactly 1.\n\nThat one survivor is the single legitimate deviation in the whole system. Phase 2\nof the plan is done: the Deviations catalog is short enough to read, which was the\nentire point of rung 0.\n\nThe cleanup was not the one-line attribute deletion the plan assumed, and the\nreason is worth recording. The class sat DIRECTLY on a Button, and Button\nconsole-errors on any class= without a data-deviation — so removing the annotation\nalone would have shipped a console error at every render. The fix moved to the\nrung-0 form the loop actually prescribes: a plain wrapper span carrying the one\nmargin declaration, with nothing on the component. Verified in the browser rather\nthan by reading — the gap between the scanbar''s right edge and its last child is\n0px before and after, so the button still ends the row exactly as it did.\n\nThird member on the same five-state connection mapping, arrived at independently.\n\nOne live WCAG 1.4.3 failure fixed: the scan-kind label measured 3.45:1 on 11.2px\ntext, the same --color-text-muted-on---color-border pairing that has now appeared\nin four members that share no code. That is a finding about the pairing, not about\nany of them: --color-border is a BOUNDARY token being used as a SURFACE.\n\nAnd one counter-example worth recording, because the rollout keeps finding the\nopposite: \"in corpus\" was already painted with the ok palette, and ok is exactly\nwhat it means. The member''s colour and the label''s meaning agreed, and it was kept\nverbatim.\n\nMember gate 3 -> 3. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83d363a35a9bd3f348b3fb0913ba0ea09e0e9bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/83d363a35a9bd3f348b3fb0913ba0ea09e0e9bbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDg3YjE3ZTYxODc0NDAwMjFjMWE3MDRmNDNmYWM0OTk4MTQwMTBlOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f","sha":"dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f"}],"sha":"87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/87b17e6187440021c1a704f43fac499814010e8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:08:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:08:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(pack-runner): three Chips, and four reasons-you-cannot-fire collapsed into one grey\n\nThree chip-shaped call sites become three <Chip>, seven rendered instances. Three\nrule-sets deleted. No rungs used at all — the existing flex gap already owned the\nspacing, so not even rung 0 was needed.\n\nThe connector palette drew four distinct states identically: needs env, disabled,\nrate-limited and auth failed were all one muted grey on a border-coloured ground.\nThey are four different answers to \"why can''t I fire this\" — configurable but\nunconfigured and throttled are degraded (warn), deliberately off is a plain fact\n(neutral), and a rejected credential is a failure (error). The operator can now\ntell which one they are looking at.\n\nTwo live WCAG 1.4.3 failures fixed there: 3.45:1 dark and 3.72:1 light on 11.2px\ntext. Every tone now clears 4.5:1 in every mode.\n\nAnd a geometric defect only the browser could show: two of those four labels were\nWRAPPING TO TWO LINES — 26px tall against \"disabled\"''s 14px, in an auto grid\ncolumn. Chip''s white-space: nowrap makes all four 17px. That is the loop''s own\n\"a chip that wraps is not a chip\" rule, caught in the wild.\n\nSixty raw buttons stay raw and correctly so. ConnectorChip is clickable with\nlong-press and keyboard handling — emphatically not a Chip — and it never reached\nthe Button rollout either, which is now raised. Its absolutely-positioned\naria-hidden badge is not a chip either.\n\nThe count badge inside the filter Buttons stays raw on purpose, and the reasoning\nis worth keeping: it is designed to inherit currentColor from whichever variant\nits Button is painting. A Chip paints its own ground, so adopting one would negate\nthe base recipe rather than adjust it, and would erase the selected-state cue on\nthe whole filter row. That is a Button count-slot organ, not a Chip.\n\nSeven of seven rendered and measured, including the long-press connector menu\ndriven open so all four palette statuses rendered together.\n\nMember gate 5 -> 5. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5bb75452ecc7d23a434271f6e2cf40c8671b8004","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/5bb75452ecc7d23a434271f6e2cf40c8671b8004"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGRjMDViMmRjMDFmNWNhYmY2NWE3MTcxZjRiYzYwNGI4ZjI5ZGYyOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5","sha":"ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5"}],"sha":"dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/dc05b2dc01f5cabf65a7171f4bc604b8f29df28f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:08:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:08:27Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(chat): five Chips, and an attention colour that was being spent on plain facts\n\nFive chip-shaped call sites become five <Chip>. Five rule-sets and one @keyframes\ndeleted, -34 lines. Rung 0 only, no deviations. Eleven Buttons untouched.\n\nFour of the five chips were painted --color-accent. Accent is the federal\n\"selected, current, in focus\" role, so this member was spending its one attention\ncolour on two plain-fact capability identifiers and a category label — which means\nit had no attention colour left. Only the genuinely-current cast chip keeps it.\nThe rest are neutral, and the surface now has a foreground again.\n\nThe connection status joins the mapping two other members landed on\nindependently: open is ok, connecting is info, auth_required is warn because it is\na gate the operator can clear, closed and error are error. Three members, no\nshared code, converging on the same five-to-four mapping is the convergence this\nrollout exists to produce.\n\nOne colour-alone defect removed, and it is subtler than it looks. The cast chip''s\nONLY signal that an invocation was live was animation: pulse on its dot — and\ntheme.css''s global prefers-reduced-motion block sets animation-iteration-count: 1,\nso for a reduced-motion user that dot pulsed once and then sat there meaning\nnothing. The state was never conveyed at all. The Chip''s dot is static and\naria-hidden, and the text carries it.\n\nEight of eight chip instances rendered and measured, with the status chip driven\nthrough all five connection states and both draft-panel variants exercised from\nfixture turns.\n\nMember gate 3 -> 3. svelte-check clean.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97495814fcc3d991f6d98564cd50d2478f79b8fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/97495814fcc3d991f6d98564cd50d2478f79b8fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGFiNmNmOWY0ODAwNzg4ODZlY2RhN2EzMTVjNmEzZjFkODc0MzJjYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f","sha":"e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f"}],"sha":"ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ab6cf9f480078886ecda7a315c6a3f1d87432cb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:06:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:06:12Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(shared-ui): Chip gains revealOnHover, and the loop gains the leaf it was missing\n\nAdopting Chip in org-workbench silently dropped a specified behaviour.\nEntity-Card-Edit-And-Remove-Affordances D5 rules that micro-affordances rest\ninvisible and are revealed by hover or row focus; Chip renders its dismiss\nalways-visible and exposed no hook, so the only way to restore it was a member\nrule selecting .ui-chip__dismiss — reaching into a component''s internals, which\nhas no rung on the ladder and should not get one.\n\nSo Chip takes a revealOnHover prop, rather than the spec being overruled by a\ncomponent that did not know about it.\n\nIt is OFF by default, and that is the considered half. A hover-only affordance\ndoes not exist on a touch device, so always-visible is the safer default and the\nreveal is the opt-in. The implementation reveals on :hover OR :focus-within so a\nkeyboard user can still reach it, uses opacity rather than display so revealing\nnever reflows the row, drops the transition under prefers-reduced-motion, and\nforces the control visible under @media (hover: none) where there is no hover to\nreveal with.\n\nThree loop gaps also close, all from the same report:\n\nThe decision tree''s first branch had no leaf for an <a href> drawn as a chip. It\nis not a Chip because it acts, and not a Button because it navigates —\nvariant=\"link\" is for a <button> that reads as a link. It is the INTERACTIVE\nBADGE organ, and there are now two sightings of it in two shapes:\nrecord-collector''s .social-chip is the link shape, org-workbench''s\n.ow-kind-editable is the button shape.\n\nThe loop did not say that design:drift is as blind to Chip as it was to Button.\nOne member''s gate moved 7 -> 6 only because a deleted rule happened to carry a hex\nliteral. An agent optimising for the gate deletes nothing, so the loop now says\noutright that the deliverable is the diff and the measurements.\n\nAnd two probe traps, both of which produce a confidently-wrong pass. The probe\nentry must import the member''s app.css itself — src/index.ts imports it,\nApp.svelte does not — and without it the DOM is completely correct while every\ncomputed style reads unstyled, which one run reported as every chip having no\nbackground, no border and no padding. That looked exactly like a finding. Chip\nwork is almost entirely computed-style work, so the trap is far more dangerous\nhere than it was for Button. Second: git archive takes its path relative to the\nrepo root, not the member directory.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"868de7c9c84e402e4e2ef8f5d67e7ecfa25d37e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/868de7c9c84e402e4e2ef8f5d67e7ecfa25d37e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGUyYzk2YzU0NzdkMDEwZGU1MTgxYjQ5ZTkzYzhlODRjN2FlODY5NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48","sha":"1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48"}],"sha":"e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/e2c96c5477d010de5181b49e93c8e84c7ae8695f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:05:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:05:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(record-collector): two Chips, and the ConfidencePill it had been re-deriving\n\nFour chip-shaped call sites become two <Chip>, one <ConfidencePill>, and one\ndeliberate holdout. Seven rule-sets deleted, 28 declarations removed, net -35\nlines of code. Rung 0 only. Zero Buttons touched.\n\nThe documented .social-confidence finding is confirmed and understates it. It\nduplicated ConfidencePill''s band thresholds, band colours, color-mix recipe and\ncurrentColor border exactly, and diverged on min-width, padding, font-size,\nletter-spacing and vertical-align — plus it omitted the clamp and round, having\nduplicated the band expression inline three hundred lines away. The em divergence\ncompounded: 0.68em off a 0.72rem parent rendered the number at 7.83px in a\n16.9 x 9.8px badge. ConfidencePill renders it at 8.99px in 23.1 x 12.8.\n\nAdopting the component rather than converting it to a Chip is the loop''s explicit\ninstruction, and the 23 duplicated lines were dead the moment it was acknowledged.\nCleanly separable if that scope call is wrong: two hunks, and the Chip work stands\nwithout them.\n\nThe finding that matters beyond this member: its connection status was drawn\nBYTE-FOR-BYTE the same wrong way as org-workbench''s — open green, closed and error\nsharing one red, connecting and auth_required sharing one grey. Two members, no\nshared code, the same five-states-three-ways recipe arrived at independently.\nThat is the eleven-renderings-of-one-value problem in miniature, and it is direct\nevidence for the StatusIndicator organ queued at Phase 4.\n\nAlso the same live AA failure as org-workbench, from the same token pair in a\nmember that shares no code with it: --color-text-muted on a --color-border ground,\n3.45:1 at 10px. Now 5.47:1 at 11px. Two independent members reaching for the same\nwrong pair is a finding about the pair.\n\nThe uppercase went with the recipe, which also stops one pack_id rendering\nLINKEDIN in one row and linkedin three lines above it in the same card.\n\n15 of 15 chip-shaped elements rendered and measured across two states, sentinel\npresent in both bundles, real socket URL absent.\n\nMember gate 1 -> 1. Federation 71 -> 71. svelte-check clean across 92 files.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e228c09855b3a11f839590d89790ff8bac92516","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/8e228c09855b3a11f839590d89790ff8bac92516"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDFhOGFmZTA1MTU1ODkzODVkZDI1ZjhmNDUwYjNmNDA1NDRkNzdjNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf","sha":"cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf"}],"sha":"1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/1a8afe0515589385dd25f8f450b3f40544d77c48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:05:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:05:22Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"adopt(org-workbench): eight Chips, and a status that was five states drawn three ways\n\nNine chip-shaped call sites become eight <Chip> and one deliberate holdout. Seven\nrule-sets deleted outright, three reduced to a single layout declaration, 42\ndeclarations removed. Rung 0 only — no rung 2, 3 or 4, and zero data-deviation.\n\nZero <Button> became a <Chip>, which was the whole risk of this wave. The three\nButton call sites that disappeared did not stop being interactive: they became the\nreal nested <button type=\"button\"> inside <Chip dismissible>, one for one.\n\nTwo places where the member''s colour and the label''s meaning disagreed, and\nmeaning won:\n\nThe connection status painted five states three ways — open green, closed and\nerror sharing one red, connecting and auth_required sharing one undifferentiated\ngrey. auth_required is a gate the operator can clear, which is warn; connecting is\ntransient information, which is info; closed is a disconnection, which is error.\nFive states, four tones, each one now saying what it means.\n\nAnd the relevance score was painted ok-green on EVERY value, so 0.41 rendered as\n\"healthy, verified\" exactly like 0.92 — colour claiming to encode something it\nnever encoded. It is neutral now, and the number is the signal, which it always\nwas.\n\nA live WCAG 1.4.3 failure is fixed as a side effect: the kind badge drew\n--color-text-muted on a --color-border ground at 11.2px, measuring 3.45:1. Now\n5.47:1. Three more chip families drew their boundary with --color-border at\n1.69:1 against the page and now use --color-border-strong at 3.44:1 — over the 3:1\nfloor for the first time.\n\nThe holdout''s own rationale was wrong and is corrected in place. It claimed\nmigrating one kind-badge twin would \"split one visual element into two unrelated\nones.\" Measured: they were ALREADY two. The editable twin overrides every painted\nproperty of the span twin, so one renders transparent at 13.6px with no padding\nwhile the other renders filled grey at 11.2px, and both are on screen at once\nbecause three of the member''s lists pass an edit handler and two do not. Measuring\nfirst inverted the answer.\n\n21 of 21 chip-shaped elements rendered and measured across two states, with the\nsentinel present in both bundles and the real socket URL absent from them.\n\nMember gate 7 -> 6 — incidental, a deleted rule happened to carry a hex literal.\nsvelte-check clean across 101 files.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbe4f5d277d4b5484d2009b989118c9ab7feb789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/fbe4f5d277d4b5484d2009b989118c9ab7feb789"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGNmNTM3ODY2NTRhOTI2Y2E5ZjFhNmU3ZGQxNjQ1MGM4YTM2MjJlYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5","sha":"ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5"}],"sha":"cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/cf53786654a926ca9f1a6e7dd16450c8a3622ebf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:04:39Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:04:39Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"feat(theme), doc(DESIGN): --text-meta for 12px, and why the six-step argument was overturned\n\nThe type scale shipped this morning folded 12px into --text-body at 13px, per\nDESIGN.md''s own rationale: an earlier nine-step draft put six steps inside a 5px\nrange and was rejected in review, because a scale whose adjacent steps are\nperceptually indistinguishable does not force a choice. An author facing\n--text-sm (11px) and --text-md (12px) picks arbitrarily, and that is exactly how\n35 sizes happened.\n\nThat argument is reasonable and it has been overturned, on the operator''s call,\nfor a better one.\n\nThe fold is a 1px INCREASE across 130 declarations of dense table content, which\ncan reflow fixed-width columns. That is a real regression accepted up front to win\nan argument about author discipline — and the token indirection makes the trade\nunnecessary. Give both values a token now; if we later decide we only want one,\nmerge them THROUGH THE TOKEN, because --text-label: var(--text-meta) is a one-line\nedit that converges every call site at once.\n\nConverging later costs nothing. Reflowing every dense table now costs something.\nSo the scale absorbs what members already use and convergence becomes a decision\ntaken with evidence rather than in advance. The original concern is not wrong, it\nis just no longer urgent, because the cost of having been wrong about a step is\none line.\n\nThe scale is seven steps: micro 10, label 11, meta 12, body 13, emphasis 15,\nheading 18, display 28. Role-named rather than the xs/2xs/3xs spelling, kept\nconsistent with what shipped hours ago and with DESIGN.md''s own argument that\n\"which small?\" is the question that produced 35 sizes — happy to rename if the\ndimensional spelling is wanted.\n\nChip''s md size moves to --text-meta, which is what a chip body actually is in this\nproduct.\n\nDESIGN.md is updated rather than left stale, because a doc that still says six\nsteps is an instruction to the next agent to undo this. The superseded argument is\nrecorded in place rather than deleted — it is the reasoning, not the conclusion,\nthat is worth keeping.\n\nAlso corrects a second stale rule in the same section: \"Do not define --font-sans\"\nwas overturned earlier today. It IS defined now. Six apps referenced it with three\ndifferent fallbacks, and the divergence was the actual problem, not the second\nfamily. One definition, one fallback stack. The monospace identity is unchanged.\n\nAnd the frontmatter''s \"scale proposed\" now says shipped, since the 🔶 is a ✅.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d078dbd70e4ba69d1230f35103c202452f7e1bc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/d078dbd70e4ba69d1230f35103c202452f7e1bc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKGVmODMyMGUxZDYwZGJiMjQzNmZmODA2NjZmYjc2Y2NiNDk3YzgzZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69","sha":"992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69"}],"sha":"ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/ef8320e1d60dbb2436ff80666fb76ccb497c83d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:43:49Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:43:49Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"loop(context-v), plan(context-v): the Chip executor, and the tidy-every-consumer sequence\n\nThe Chip loop is deliberately a DELTA, not a replacement. Everything mechanical —\nthe probe recipe, the resolve.alias safety rule and its sentinel check,\nmeasure-the-before, gate capture, raise-don''t-chase, the ladder including rung 0 —\nis inherited from the Button loop, which was run nineteen times and revised four\ntimes from engineer reports. Repeating it would fork it.\n\nWhat differs is the judgement, and it is front-loaded because the classification\nIS the risk. Button''s hard question was which variant; Chip''s is whether the thing\nis a Chip at all. A filter chip that toggles a filter is a Button that happens to\nbe chip-shaped, and nineteen members already made that call — so the most likely\nway this wave does damage is by converting interactive controls back into spans.\nThe loop opens with the decision tree and says so in as many words.\n\nTone is semantic, never decorative, with a mapping table and the reason: the\noriginal sweep found seventeen of nineteen packages observing one\nconnection_status and rendering it eleven ways precisely because tone was picked\nby eye. Preserving the member''s colour choice preserves the divergence.\n\nThe plan sequences four phases. Chip across twelve units in five groups; the seven\nstale layout deviations that outlived rung 0 and should take the federation''s\ncount to one; three containment jobs that keep surfacing in migration reports and\nare not component work; and the next organs in evidence order, with ListRow at\n5-plus sightings already past the promotion threshold.\n\nStanding decisions are restated so they stop being re-litigated, and three\ngenuine judgement calls are saved for the operator with the working assumption\nstated for each — dark-mode --color-surface, whether ConfidencePill folds into\nChip, and who absorbs the 1px cost of folding 12px into --text-body.\n\nRefs #101\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8b3fb5def3cf8211a5fb3a69d8b9111829c9fd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/trees/c8b3fb5def3cf8211a5fb3a69d8b9111829c9fd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/git/commits/992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69","node_id":"C_kwDOPSTVMNoAKDk5MmNkZDZhZjFkY2I2MTk3NjcwZWI5ODUxNTMwMTE4NDlhMzJmNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/augment-it/commit/a866ee2104db8f44ac22676a950093f15e272140","sha":"a866ee2104db8f44ac22676a950093f15e272140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/a866ee2104db8f44ac22676a950093f15e272140"}],"sha":"992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits/992cdd6af1dcb6197670eb985153011849a32f69"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/augment-it/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=c825e8a83b11bd6b31b80cfe40714dfc331409f5&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A37%3A18.985Z"}');
